France 24 (EN),Western Europe,en,Ceuta migrant influx reignites immigration divisions in Europe,Ceuta migrant influx reignites immigration divisions in Europe,"Ceuta migrant influx reignites immigration divisions in Europe The arrival of 60,000 people into the Spanish North African enclave of Ceuta from Morocco last week has created serious tensions within the EU over immigration. Spain has called for a meeting of EU interior ministers which is due to take place Tuesday. The arrival of 60,000 people into the Spanish North African enclave of Ceuta from Morocco last week has created serious tensions within the EU over immigration. Spain has called for a meeting of EU interior ministers which is due to take place Tuesday. Issued on:03/08/2026 - 17:57 To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Theunprecedented influx of migrantswho made their way fromMoroccointo theSpanish enclave of Ceutain North Africa last Thursday and Friday has created tensions betweenSpainand the European partners most critical of its migration policy.Italy, followed byDenmark, immediately called for Spain to be suspended from the Schengen Area. The demand has angeredMadrid, who requested a videoconferencemeeting between EU interior ministersto take place on Tuesday. In recent months,Brusselshas alreadysignificantly tightened its immigration legislationthrough theNew Pact on Migration and Asylumwhich, among other measures, allows member states to send rejected asylum seekers to centres outside of the EU’s borders in so-called “return hubs”. To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable i","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 15:57:17 GMT",https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260803-ceuta-migrant-influx-reignites-immigration-divisions-in-europe,2026-08-04 01:17:24
France 24 (EN),Western Europe,en,Bridge collapse in DR Congo reignites debate about mining revenues,Bridge collapse in DR Congo reignites debate about mining revenues,"Bridge collapse in DR Congo reignites debate about mining revenues Several people ended up in the river after an important bridge collapsed on June 3 in the village of Hombo in the eastern part of the DRC. The bridge is one of the failing critical infrastructures in a territory that is home to one of the most lucrative mines in the region. Several people ended up in the river after an important bridge collapsed on June 3 in the village of Hombo in the eastern part of the DRC. The bridge is one of the failing critical infrastructures in a territory that is home to one of the most lucrative mines in the region. Issued on:03/08/2026 - 17:51 The footage shows at least seven people floundering in the muddy river, trying to keep from being swept away by the current. An eighth person seems to be swimming towards them to help. A few seconds later, the man who is filming the scene and describing what is happening turns the camera to show what caused the chaos below: a wooden bridge has broken in half and both sides have collapsed into the water. Large groups of people are gathered on both banks. To display this content from , you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. No one died in the bridge collapse that took place onJune 3, 2026, in Hombo, according to two local sources. However, it has created a complicated situation, especially because the two parts of the village, located on either side of the Luhoho River, actually belong to two different administrative districts or “sectors"". This makes the bridge an even more important link for the local population, says Augustin Mbula, a local journalist based in Walikale territory. ""The bridge means that people can cross the river, but it is also important for commerce. For example, Hombo North [Editor’s note: the part of Hombo located on the western ba","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 15:51:49 GMT",https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20260803-bridge-collapse-dr-congo-reignites-debate-mining-revenues,2026-08-04 01:17:24
