France 24 (EN),Western Europe,en,Anti-war politician and Kremlin critic Boris Nadezhdin flees Russia for France,Anti-war politician and Kremlin critic Boris Nadezhdin flees Russia for France,"Anti-war politician and Kremlin critic Boris Nadezhdin flees Russia for France Kremlin critic and anti-war politician Boris Nadezhdin – who openly criticised President Vladimir Putin and Moscow's Ukraine offensive – said Monday he had fled Russia for Paris. Nadezhdin was recently detained outside Moscow and blocked from running for parliament. Russia's clampdown on dissent has left most critics in jail, in exile or dead. Kremlin critic and anti-war politician Boris Nadezhdin – who openly criticised President Vladimir Putin and Moscow's Ukraine offensive – said Monday he had fled Russia for Paris. Nadezhdin was recently detained outside Moscow and blocked from running for parliament. Russia's clampdown on dissent has left most critics in jail, in exile or dead. Issued on:03/08/2026 - 16:47Modified:03/08/2026 - 16:48 Russian anti-war politician Boris Nadezhdin – who was recently detained outsideMoscowand blocked from running for parliament – said Monday he had left the country, in a video posted fromParis. Nadezhdin, 63, a ⁠former liberal lawmaker, was one of the few politicians who openly criticised PresidentVladimir Putinand Moscow'sUkraineoffensive to have stayed in the country. Almost all of Putin's critics are in jail, in exile or dead. Nadezhdin had been seeking to stand in tightly controlled parliamentary elections in September. Read moreFrench court rejects pro-Kremlin commentator's expulsion appeal As his campaign ramped up last month, authorities labelled him a ""foreign agent"", briefly detained him, then fined him 1,000 rubles ($13) for displaying ""extremist symbols"" in a dramatic hearing that saw paramedics called as his blood pressure spiked. Amid the pressure – which would technically have barred him from standing – he announced he was quitting his campaign, saying he had been ""silenced"" and ""pushed out of politics"". On Monday he posted a video on his Telegram channel, with theEiff","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 14:47:54 GMT",https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260803-anti-war-politician-and-kremlin-critic-boris-nadezhdin-flees-russia-for-france,2026-08-04 01:17:24
