Al Jazeera (EN),Middle East (English),en,"Drone slams into Russian beach, killing at least 7 people","Drone slams into Russian beach, killing at least 7 people","Drone slams into Russian beach, killing at least 7 people Video shows the moment a drone struck a crowded beach near the Russian Black Sea resort of Gelendzhik. Drone slams into Russian beach, killing at least 7 people Video shows the moment a drone struck a crowded beach near the Russian Black Sea resort of Gelendzhik, killing at least seven people, including three children, and wounding dozens. Moscow blamed Ukraine for the attack. It’s unclear if the drone was intercepted or bound for a nearby naval base. Kyiv has not commented. Save Share","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 18:05:23 +0000",https://www.aljazeera.com/video/newsfeed/2026/8/3/drone-slams-into-russian-beach-killing-at-least-7-people?traffic_source=rss,2026-08-04 01:17:29
Al Jazeera (EN),Middle East (English),en,Republicans say they will back Blanche after US Justice Department order,Republicans say they will back Blanche after US Justice Department order,"Republicans say they will back Blanche after US Justice Department order Two Republican senators say they will end their opposition after order cancelling controversial $1.8bn fund. Save Share Two United States Republican senators have said they will end their opposition to US President Donald Trump’s pick to lead the Department of Justice, acting Attorney GeneralTodd Blanche, after Blanche scrapped a controversial “anti-weaponisation fund” that bipartisan critics say would use taxpayer dollars to reward Trump’s political allies. Senators John Cornyn of Texas and Thom Tillis of North Carolina said in a statement on Monday that they would vote to advance Blanche’s nomination to the full US Senate, after he issued an order rescinding the$1.8bn fundthe night before. “We want to express our gratitude to Mr Blanche and his staff for working with us on this, and we look forward to voting to advance his nomination out of the Senate Judiciary Committee soon,” the two senators said. Blanche’s path towards confirmation in the US Senate, where Republicans hold a slim majority, had previously been held up due to concerns about the fund, created for allies ofTrumpwho say they were the victims of government persecution. The possibility that supporters of Trump who took part in the January 6, 2021, assault on the US Capitol could qualify for payments sparked bipartisan backlash. “These people were treated horribly. And this fund could have given them some solace,” Trump said in remarks to the press on Monday, adding that he viewed the fund as a “positive”. Cornyn and Tillis, whose votesBlancheneeds to advance through the Senate Judiciary Committee, had previously said ","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 17:39:38 +0000",https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/8/3/republicans-say-they-will-back-blanche-after-us-justice-department-order?traffic_source=rss,2026-08-04 01:17:29
Al Jazeera (EN),Middle East (English),en,Trump says ongoing talks are Iran’s ‘last chance’,Trump says ongoing talks are Iran’s ‘last chance’,"Trump says ongoing talks are Iran’s ‘last chance’ US president demands &#039;Total Surrender&#039; amid escalating naval blockade in the crucial Strait of Hormuz. Save Share United States President Donald Trump has warned Iran that it has one last chance to forge a deal to avoid massive air strikes. “I want to give them every last chance before decapitation.” When asked whether Iran would be willing to “return to a fully free navigation” of the Strait of Hormuz, Trump told reporters at the White House that the vital waterway “has to be [free], I am not going to let them charge. If anybody is going to charge, we’ll charge …. We have total control”. Trump emphasised that the US has the means to enforce freedom of navigation with its blockade. He also addressed the on-again-off-again nature of discussions about negotiations with Tehran, saying talks were being held “at the request of Iran” and with the support of several Gulf Arab states. “We are talking right now [with Iran] at the request of Iran, backed by Saudi Arabia, backed by the UAE, and backed by Qatar in particular, but others also,” Trump said. “Many countries called, but if it doesn’t happen, this is the last chance for them to sign a good document.” Earlier, Trump posted to his social media platform Truth Social, describing Iran’s leadership as “unbelievably duplicitous”, saying Tehran asked for talks to end the war and then announced that no discussions were being held. Trump claimed that Iran had backtracked, saying “they’re only dealing with ‘Oman.’ They then go on to give their usual blather in saying, the Strait of Hormuz will be operated powerfully by them”. Trump also ","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 17:38:01 +0000",https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/8/3/trump-blasts-duplicitous-iran-after-tehran-denies-it-is-in-talks-with-the-us?traffic_source=rss,2026-08-04 01:17:29
