Al Jazeera (AR),Middle East (Arabic),ar,ساحة الملحمة في جرش تحيي صناعات أردنية تراثية,ساحة الملحمة في جرش تحيي صناعات أردنية تراثية,"ساحة الملحمة في جرش تحيي صناعات أردنية تراثية The Turquoise Mountain Foundation is trying to Introducing new generations to the heritage of their ancestors and their traditional crafts, such as weaving, copper carving, and soap making from herbs and natural oils. Save Share In the epic square in the center of the Jordanian archaeological city of Jerash, life is vibrant with handicrafts that mimic the past and look towards the future, such as loom making, jewelry and stone carving, through an initiative led by the “Turquoise Mountain” Foundation with the aim of re-engaging the local community in traditional Jordanian crafts. The project aims to preserve the rich heritage and introduce it to new generations in light of contemporary technological acceleration, as the rooms of the historical square have turned into live workshops for each craft, by informing visitors about the history of Jordan and its ancient handicrafts, according to what Shorouk Al-Mazraawi, one of those in charge of the project, told Al Jazeera. Those in charge of the initiative are trying to provide models of Jordanian handicrafts, such as weaving, looms, copper carving, and soap making from olive oil, by allocating a separate room for each craft, according to Shorouk. As for the craftsmen participating in the event, they seek to confirm their adherence to the heritage of their ancestors, like Sana","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 21:04:46 +0300",https://www.aljazeera.net/culture/2026/8/4/%d8%b3%d8%a7%d8%ad%d8%a9-%d8%a7%d9%84%d9%85%d9%84%d8%ad%d9%85%d8%a9-%d9%81%d9%8a-%d8%ac%d8%b1%d8%b4-%d8%aa%d8%ad%d9%8a%d9%8a-%d8%b5%d9%86%d8%a7%d8%b9%d8%a7%d8%aa?traffic_source=rss,2026-08-04 01:17:38
