Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,В Эстонии более 100 помощников воспитателей детсадов уволили из-за языковых требований,В Эстонии более 100 помощников воспитателей детсадов уволили из-за языковых требований,"В Эстонии более 100 помощников воспитателей детсадов уволили из-за языковых требований Advertising In the Estonian city of Narva, more than 100 assistant kindergarten teachers were fired due to language requirements. This was reported by the television and radio company ERR. This category of employees must know Estonian at a level of at least B2. The corresponding requirements were adopted back in 2024, but the two-year delay ended on August 1. The employment contracts of 108 teaching assistants were terminated; in order to continue working, employees had to prove their language proficiency. As the head of the education department of Narva, Larisa Degel, explained, there is no risk of disruption to the work of kindergartens, since in some groups second teachers will be able to replace assistants. Last November, it became known that the Estonian authorities are planning to ban the dubbing of films into Russian.","Tue, 04 Aug 2026 03:17:24 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/08/04/v-estonii-bolee-100-pomoschnikov-vospitateley-detsadov-uvolili-iz-za-yazykovyh-trebovaniy/,2026-08-04 01:18:47
