Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,Раскрыто отношение женщин к мужским стонам в постели,Раскрыто отношение женщин к мужским стонам в постели,"Раскрыто отношение женщин к мужским стонам в постели Реклама Сексолог и психотерапевт Бекки Крепсли-Фокс раскрыла отношение женщин к мужским стонам в постели. На эту тему специалисткапобеседовалас изданием Metro. По словам Крепсли-Фокс, женщинам нравятся мужские стоны, так как они показывают, что партнер испытывает настоящее удовольствие. «Стоны могут укрепить связь между супругами. Есть нечто глубоко уязвимое в том, чтобы позволить кому-то увидеть тебя в момент наслаждения — немного потерять контроль над собой у другого на глазах», — объяснила психотерапевт. Сексолог добавила, что мужчины чаще женщин сдерживают желание производить звуки в постели. Причинами этого она назвала то, что в порно мужчины обычно не издают никаких звуков, и то, что их часто с детства учат подавлять эмоции. «Если вы мужчина, который стесняется, опасаясь, что стоны м","Tue, 04 Aug 2026 01:01:03 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/08/04/raskryto-otnoshenie-zhenschin-k-muzhskim-stonam-v-posteli/,2026-08-04 01:19:19
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,Эмили Ратаковски обнажилась на камеру после продажи книги о беспорядочных интимных связях,Эмили Ратаковски обнажилась на камеру после продажи книги о беспорядочных интимных связях,"Эмили Ратаковски обнажилась на камеру после продажи книги о беспорядочных интимных связях Advertising American fashion model Emily Ratajkowski showed a candid photo after selling a book about promiscuity. The post appeared on her Instagram page (owned by Meta, a company recognized as an extremist organization and banned by the Russian Federation). The 35-year-old fashion model appeared in front of the camera against a backdrop of water and sand, holding a glass of drink in her hand. She turned sideways to the photographer and showed off her completely naked body. In June, Ratajkowski spoke for the first time about her intimate life after her divorce from her husband, actor Sebastian Bear-McClard. The model admitted that she could not accept the status of a single mother and for this reason began dating random men. Ratajkowski later wrote a book about it and sold it at auction. The rights to it were acquired by Penguin Press, which paid","Tue, 04 Aug 2026 01:00:58 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/08/04/emili-ratakovski-obnazhilas-na-kameru-posle-prodazhi-knigi-o-besporyadochnyh-intimnyh-svyazyah/,2026-08-04 01:19:21
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,Раскрыты изменения в действиях ВСУ при Драпатом,Раскрыты изменения в действиях ВСУ при Драпатом,"Раскрыты изменения в действиях ВСУ при Драпатом Реклама Посол по особым поручениямМИД РоссииРодион Мирошникрассказал, что изменилось в действияхВооруженных силУкраины(ВСУ) после назначения Михаила Драпатого главнокомандующим. Об этом онвысказалсяв беседе с «Известиями». Мирошник уточнил, что после назначения Драпатого ВСУ усилили удары по гражданским объектам. По его мнению, подобные тенденции появились еще при бывшем министре обороны УкраиныМихаиле Федорове. «Упор на терроризм, на войну с гражданскими объектами и гражданскими лицами был сделан именно при Федорове и сейчас поддерживается и расширяется Драпатым», — отметил он. Федороваотправилив отставку 15 июля. Одной из причин его увольнения называли постоянные конфликты с главнокомандующим Вооруженными силами УкраиныАлександром Сырским. Позже президент УкраиныВладимир ЗеленскийуволилС","Tue, 04 Aug 2026 00:49:00 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/08/04/raskryty-izmeneniya-v-deystviyah-vsu-pri-drapatom/,2026-08-04 01:19:22
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,Норвежский хоккеист описал эмоции от выступления в России,Норвежский хоккеист описал эмоции от выступления в России,"Норвежский хоккеист описал эмоции от выступления в России Реклама Норвежский вратарь Хенрик Хаукеланн описал эмоции после перехода вчелябинский «Трактор». Его слова приводятся насайтекоманды. Хоккеист заявил, что уже успел почувствовать себя вЧелябинскекомфортно. 31-летний норвежец назвал город приятным и уютным, а также положительно оценил арену и организацию в российском клубе. Он добавил, что уже немного прогулялся по центру и рассчитывает оправдать ожидания болельщиков «Трактора». Хаукеланн также подчеркнул, что намерен обеспечивать стабильную игру и надежно защищать ворота команды. Он постарается сохранять спокойствие в матчах. Ранее нападающий клуба Национальной хоккейной лиги «Миннесоты Уайлд»Кирилл Капризовсравнилжизнь вСШАи России. Хоккеист признался, что в США скучает по дому и родным местам","Tue, 04 Aug 2026 00:45:49 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/08/04/norvezhskiy-hokkeist-opisal-emotsii-ot-vystupleniya-v-rossii/,2026-08-04 01:19:23
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,Европейская страна расширила программу воинского призыва,Европейская страна расширила программу воинского призыва,"Европейская страна расширила программу воинского призыва Реклама Около 1,6 тысячи датских призывников, включая женщин приступили к прохождению обновленной 11-месячной военной службы в стране. Об этом сообщаетReuters. Данияранее объявила, что впервые распространит обязательную военную службу на женщин. Кроме того, страна решила увеличить стандартную продолжительность с четырех до 11 месяцев. Европейская страна также намерена нарастить количество ежегодно призываемых в армию новобранцев с пяти до 7,5 тысячи человек к 2033 году. «Это происходит на фоне ускоренного наращивания оборонного потенциала Дании, вызванного вопросами безопасности в Арктике и войной наУкраине», — отмечается в публикации. Ранее власти Даниирешили призыватьв армию женщин для прохождения обязательной срочной службы. Изменения были утверждены на фоне международной напряженности,","Tue, 04 Aug 2026 00:39:00 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/08/04/evropeyskaya-strana-rasshirila-programmu-voinskogo-prizyva/,2026-08-04 01:19:24
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,Назван простой способ замедлить процесс старения организма,Назван простой способ замедлить процесс старения организма,"Назван простой способ замедлить процесс старения организма Реклама Снижение потребления белка может благоприятно влиять на обмен веществ и замедлять процессы старения. К такому выводу пришли авторы обзора более 350 научных исследований,опубликованногов журнале Cell Press Blue (CPB). Исследователи проанализировали данные экспериментов на животных, клинических испытаний и наблюдательных работ. По их данным, умеренное ограничение белка улучшает чувствительность к инсулину, снижает уровень воспаления, уменьшает количество жировой ткани и активирует механизмы, связанные с долголетием. При этом в ряде исследований положительные эффекты наблюдались даже без уменьшения общей калорийности рациона. Одним из ключевых механизмов оказался гормон FGF21, уровень которого повышается при снижении потребления белка. Он помогает организму эффективнее расходовать эне","Tue, 04 Aug 2026 00:32:04 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/08/04/nazvan-prostoy-sposob-zamedlit-protsess-stareniya-organizma/,2026-08-04 01:19:25
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,Мужчина похитил 15-летнюю школьницу и насиловал ее четыре года,Мужчина похитил 15-летнюю школьницу и насиловал ее четыре года,"Мужчина похитил 15-летнюю школьницу и насиловал ее четыре года Реклама ВСШАарестовали мужчину из штата Виргиния, который похитил 15-летнюю школьницу, четыре года держал ее взаперти в своем доме и насиловал. Об этомпишетThe Washington Post. Джонайя Уокер, которой сейчас 19 лет,была найденаполицией в мае. Девушка пропала из своего дома вМилуоки,штат Висконсин, 23 июня 2022 года. По данным следствия, Уокер похитил 37-летний Оуэн Ларс Андерсон. Он ее отвез в свой дом в городе Блаксберг в Виргинии, где держал все это время. В мае девушка сама позвонила в полицию и рассказала, что ее похитили. Она заявила, что познакомилась с Андерсоном в сети, когда ей было 12 лет. Она жаловалась на родителей, а мужчина говорил, что никогда не будет обижать ее. Он стал просить, чтобы она прислала ему свои фото в обнаженном виде, а позже стал шантажировать ее. После похищен","Tue, 04 Aug 2026 00:32:00 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/08/04/muzhchina-pohitil-15-letnyuyu-shkolnitsu-i-nasiloval-ee-chetyre-goda/,2026-08-04 01:19:26
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Turkish cargo ship hit in suspected Ukrainian attack near Russian port (VIDEOS),Turkish cargo ship hit in suspected Ukrainian attack near Russian port (VIDEOS),"Turkish cargo ship hit in suspected Ukrainian attack near Russian port (VIDEOS) <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.08/thumbnail/6a712de985f5407e1b798a54.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> A Turkish cargo ship was struck by suspected Ukrainian drones near a Russian Black Sea port <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643820-turkish-ships-hit-drones/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> A Turkish-operated cargo ship was hit in an apparent Ukrainian drone attack off the Russian Black Sea port of Novorossiysk late on Monday. According to Türkiye’s Directorate General of Maritime Affairs (DGM), the Cameroon-flagged Nadezhda was sailing from Novorossiysk to the Turkish port of Samsun when it was attacked by drones. Russian vessels evacuated the crew from the ship, which sustained damage to its bow and living quarters, the DGM said. Initial reports indicated that three people on board were injured. 3 Ağustos 2026 tarihinde, Novorossiysk Limanı’ndan Samsun’a seyir hâlinde bulunan NADEZHDA isimli Ro-Ro gemisinin, Novorossiysk’e yaklaşık 20 deniz mili açıkta dron saldırısına uğradığı bilgisi alınmıştır.Gemide, 13’ü Türk vatandaşı olmak üzere toplam 22 mürettebat…pic.twitter.com/yb1pDYmCBE The Nadezhda had a crew of 22, including 13 Turkish citizens, according to the DGM. Turkish media reported that the vessel was operated by Samsun-based Kalyoncu Shipping and had been carrying fruit and vegetables from Türkiye to Russia. Rusya'ya sebze taşıyordu: Türk Ro-ro gemisine saldırı!4 mürettebat yaralandıhttps://t.co/JELlPdKDyIpic.twitter.com/JQVWqZMd03 Although Turkish authorities did not identify the perpetrator, the ship’s captain, Yalcin Sahin, was quoted by Turkish media as saying that six or seven Ukrainian drones had struck the vessel. Ukraine has repeatedly targeted civilian ships near Russia’s Black Sea and Sea of Azov coasts, as well as tankers off the Turkish coas","Tue, 04 Aug 2026 00:12:26 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643820-turkish-ships-hit-drones/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-04 01:19:30
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Iran called off Ukraine strikes after Kiev’s ‘apology’ – Khamenei adviser,Iran called off Ukraine strikes after Kiev’s ‘apology’ – Khamenei adviser,"Iran called off Ukraine strikes after Kiev’s ‘apology’ – Khamenei adviser <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.08/thumbnail/6a711c722030277e9b106cff.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Iran called off strikes on Ukraine after Kiev apologized for an attack on an Iranian cargo ship, an adviser to Mojtaba Khamenei has said <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643819-iran-called-off-ukraine-strike/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> Iran called off retaliatory strikes against Ukraine over last month’s attack on a cargo ship in the Caspian Sea after Kiev apologized, a senior adviser to Iranian Supreme Leader Mojtaba Khamenei has said. On July 25, Ukraine struck the Iranian vessel with drones, killing one sailor, and claimed that it was transporting military equipment to Russia. Iran said the ship was carrying civilian cargo and denounced the attack as an act of aggression. Russia identified the vessel as the dry cargo ship Ana. Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps (IRGC) Major General Mohsen Rezaee said on Monday that Tehran had selected targets in Ukraine.“We were set to strike three sites in Ukraine, but canceled the attack following Ukraine’s apology,”Rezaee said, as quoted by Press TV. According to Fars, Rezaee said Kiev had claimed that it attacked the ship by mistake and that Iran had decided to investigate the claim.“Even if it was a mistake, however, there will still be consequences,”he said. Iranian Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi said earlier that his Ukrainian counterpart, Andrey Sibiga, had assured him during a phone call that the attack on the ship“was unintentional and Ukraine seeks no escalation.”Araghchi demanded compensation for the incident. Sibiga initially dismissed Iran’s threats of retaliation as“unjustified and groundless,”but later struck a conciliatory tone, saying that Kiev had“never intended to target civilian vessels or people.” Russia described the attack on ","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 23:00:37 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643819-iran-called-off-ukraine-strike/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-04 01:19:31
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Warsaw appeals €1.3bn Covid bill from von der Leyen’s ‘Pfizergate’,Warsaw appeals €1.3bn Covid bill from von der Leyen’s ‘Pfizergate’,"Warsaw appeals €1.3bn Covid bill from von der Leyen’s ‘Pfizergate’ <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.08/thumbnail/6a70f92885f5406f1a3f33df.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Poland has appealed a Belgian court ruling ordering it to pay for Covid-19 vaccine doses under the EU’s controversial ‘Pfizergate’ deal <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643817-poland-eu-covid-pfizergate/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> Poland has appealed a Belgian court ruling ordering it to pay for millions of Covid-19 vaccine doses it declined to accept under a controversial EU vaccine purchase deal. The case stems from multibillion-euro contracts for Covid shots negotiated by European Commission President Ursula von der Leyen with manufacturers Pfizer and BioNTech during the pandemic. The agreements later became the focus of the so-called ‘Pfizergate’ scandal. In a statement released on Monday, the Polish Health Ministry said the government had appealed the judgment and requested that its enforcement be suspended pending the court’s review. It argued that the lower court had failed to consider all the“relevant factual and legal circumstances”but did not disclose further details. Pfizer sued Poland in 2023 after Warsaw stopped accepting deliveries, arguing that falling demand, an oversupply of vaccines and the economic impact of the Ukraine conflict amounted to force majeure. In April, the Brussels court ruled that Warsaw must accept roughly 64 million doses and pay about €1.3 billion ($1.5 billion), in addition to interest and legal costs. Pfizer defended the ruling, telling Politico it reflected“the importance of the contractual obligations that underpinned a successful European pandemic response”and that the company had shown“significant flexibility”toward member states before pursuing legal enforcement. Von der Leyen has faced scrutiny over her role in the vaccine deals, with opponents accus","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 20:49:40 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643817-poland-eu-covid-pfizergate/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-04 01:19:32
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Ukrainian man stabs local woman in Poland,Ukrainian man stabs local woman in Poland,"Ukrainian man stabs local woman in Poland <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.08/thumbnail/6a70f8a52030277c06691b41.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> A Ukrainian national has been detained in Poland after critically injuring a Polish woman in a stabbing under unclear circumstances <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643816-ukrainian-stabs-polish-woman/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> A Ukrainian national has been arrested after stabbing a Polish woman in Wroclaw, police have said, as public frustration with Ukrainian migrants continues to grow in the EU state. In recent weeks, Poland has been hit by a string of violent incidents between locals and Ukrainian migrants. On several occasions, Polish nationals allegedly confronted migrants over speaking Ukrainian in public, as well as for having questionable nationalist-charged tattoos visible. The latest incident occurred in the southwestern city of Wroclaw on Saturday, when an 18-year-old Ukrainian stabbed a 30-year-old Polish woman, according to local police. The attacker fled the scene and was apprehended the next day. Law enforcement did not reveal any further details about the incident, confirming only that the victim was hospitalized in a life-threatening condition. The motives behind the attack were not immediately clear, while local media reports indicated the incident happened at the entrance hall of a multi-story apartment building. Ukraine’s consulate in Wroclaw acknowledged the incident, confirming the attacker was a migrant from the country.“We strongly condemn all manifestations of violence and aggression, regardless of who is their perpetrator and who is the victim,”the consulate said in a statement. Poland’s main opposition party, Law and Justice, condemned the incident, with its vice-president, Przemyslaw Czarnek, taking jabs at Prime Minister Donald Tusk for staying“silent”on the attack and ","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 20:25:01 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643816-ukrainian-stabs-polish-woman/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-04 01:19:33
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Ceuta migrant surge deepens political divide in Spain,Ceuta migrant surge deepens political divide in Spain,"Ceuta migrant surge deepens political divide in Spain <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.08/thumbnail/6a70d60a2030276d32313d9c.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Spain has become increasingly divided over the migrant influx into the exclave of Ceuta, with politicians trading blame over the crisis <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643807-spain-ceuta-migrants-crisis/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> The record migrant influx into Spain’s North African exclave of Ceuta has fueled political divisions in the country, with the opposition criticizing the government’s handling of the crisis. Madrid has accused Morocco of“weaponizing”migration. Thousands rallied in Madrid and Ceuta on Sunday, demanding Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez’s resignation after nearly 60,000 people entered the exclave from Morocco on Thursday and Friday. In Ceuta, rallies by right-wing politicians and activists drew counterprotests from local residents, including members of the city’s Muslim community. Sanchez rejected calls from Ceuta’s local authorities to declare a national emergency, instead deploying 60 troops – a move dismissed by right-wing European politicians as inadequate. Santiago Abascal, the leader of Spain’s right-wing Vox party, described the mass border crossing as an“invasion”and an“act of war”orchestrated by Morocco and enabled by Sanchez. He blamed the Socialist government for weak border controls and called for the frontier with Morocco to be permanently militarized. The crisis, the largest migrant invasion in the EU’s history, claimed the lives of at least 88 people, a death toll expected to rise further. Many of the victims drowned at sea or were crushed in stampedes at border checkpoints. Although the vast majority of those who entered Ceuta voluntarily returned to Morocco within days, Sanchez described the episode as an“attack.” The crisis also deepened divisions across the EU. Whi","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 18:37:43 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643807-spain-ceuta-migrants-crisis/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-04 01:19:34
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Religious Jews attack Christian monastery in Jerusalem (VIDEO),Religious Jews attack Christian monastery in Jerusalem (VIDEO),"Religious Jews attack Christian monastery in Jerusalem (VIDEO) <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.08/thumbnail/6a70bb2520302779ca43ab71.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Six religious Jews have been arrested after attacking an Armenian monastery in Jerusalem’s Old City <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643812-jews-attack-christian-monestary/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> Six religious Jews have been arrested after attacking the historic St. James Armenian Monastery in Jerusalem’s Old City, according to Israeli police. The group, consisting of five minors and one adult, were caught on video spitting on and banging against the monastery entrance on Sunday night before throwing stones at the walls of the compound, which serves as the regional headquarters of the Armenian Church. When an Armenian woman began filming the attack from a nearby building, the assailants hurled stones toward her window and shouted abuse at her. Police subsequently located and arrested all six suspects. Three have been barred from entering the Old City for 15 days, while police have asked a Jerusalem court to extend the detention of the remaining three. Israeli settlers spit on the porch of Saint James Monastery in the Armenian Quarter of the Old City of Jerusalempic.twitter.com/FYhCSPqEn7 The Armenian Patriarchate has filed a formal complaint and called on US Ambassador Mike Huckabee to press Israel to recognize such incidents as hate crimes. The assault is the latest in a growing wave of attacks on Christians, clergy, and church property in Jerusalem and the occupied Palestinian territories. Christian leaders say priests and pilgrims are routinely spat on, cursed and assaulted by ultra-Orthodox and radical nationalist Jews, while churches, monasteries, and Christian-owned property have been vandalized. Six Israelis were detained after an incident near St. James Monast","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 17:42:25 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643812-jews-attack-christian-monestary/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-04 01:19:35
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,The EU opened the gates. Now it’s fighting over who pays,The EU opened the gates. Now it’s fighting over who pays,"The EU opened the gates. Now it’s fighting over who pays <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.08/thumbnail/6a70772d85f54056a134ba8b.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Spain’s Ceuta border crisis has exposed the Migration Pact’s deepest flaws, from weak external borders to bitter disputes over who must pay <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643780-eu-opened-gates-ceuta/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> On the last days of July, over 50,000 illegal immigrants breached the defensive perimeters of Ceuta and Melilla and swarmed into the Spanish enclaves in North Africa. This occurred against the backdrop of the grandly adopted New Pact for Migration in Brussels, which officially entered into force on June 12. By August 2, at least 72 people had reportedly died during the crossings. This latest migration crisis has already sparked debate about the adequacy of EU legislation and exposed the tensions of the partisan political struggle unfolding within the bloc. Shocked observers have been left wondering who will pay for this influx of migrants. The reasons for this unprecedented wave lie far beyond conventional humanitarian considerations and relate to the use of migration as a geopolitical weapon. The simultaneous collapse of Spain’s borders reveals a ruthless combination: On the one hand, King Mohammed VI of Moroccohas reportedly once again used the ‘migration switch’ as a tool for direct financial blackmail against Madrid in disputes over subsidies. On the other, transnational smuggling syndicates took advantage of a recent Spanish Supreme Court decision to grant illegal residents amnesty, spreading rumors on social media about a supposed ‘opening of borders’. Combined with the perfect July calm in Gibraltar, these factors created the most favorable conditions for crossing one of the EU’s most vulnerable borders. Austria, Denmark, Italy, Slovenia, Finland, and the Czech Republi","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 14:59:57 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643780-eu-opened-gates-ceuta/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-04 01:19:37
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Kiev’s backers facing ‘big problem’ after Macron exit – Telegraph,Kiev’s backers facing ‘big problem’ after Macron exit – Telegraph,"Kiev’s backers facing ‘big problem’ after Macron exit – Telegraph <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.08/thumbnail/6a70909185f540799a66881f.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Kiev’s NATO backers risk disarray as Macron’s exit could open the door to Ukraine-skeptic hardliners, The Telegraph reports <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643801-nato-coalition-big-problem-ukraine/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> French President Emmanuel Macron’s departure from the Elysee Palace next year could open the door to Ukraine skeptics and create a“big problem”for the NATO coalition backing Kiev, The Telegraph reported on Sunday, citing sources. Fears about what the British paper described as a“leadership vacuum”revolve mainly around the so-called“coalition of the willing”– a grouping of roughly 30, mostly NATO, states that has spent over a year drawing up plans to put troops in Ukraine as self-styled“peacekeepers”once a ceasefire is reached. Among the goals of the group – which is dominated by the UK and France – is also to coordinate aid to Kiev. Russia has rejected any unauthorized foreign military presence in Ukraine, suggesting that Western troops would not be“peacekeepers”but rather“occupation forces”and therefore legitimate targets. The Telegraph noted that while new UK Prime Minister Andy Burnham signaled continuity in backing Kiev and NATO, there is no equivalent figure in Paris, with Macron constitutionally required to leave his post after next year’s presidential election. This, the paper added, has sparked concerns about a“slow death”for the coalition. Two potential replacements are Marine Le Pen, leader of the right-wing National Rally, and left-wing firebrand Jean-Luc Melenchon. Both are hardline Ukraine and NATO skeptics. Le Pen has vowed to pull France out of the bloc’s military command, lift sanctions on Russia, and push Kiev toward a peace deal, while Melenchon has pled","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 13:14:15 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643801-nato-coalition-big-problem-ukraine/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-04 01:19:38
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,US must be held to account for continued ‘war crimes’ – FM spokesman to RT,US must be held to account for continued ‘war crimes’ – FM spokesman to RT,"US must be held to account for continued ‘war crimes’ – FM spokesman to RT <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.08/thumbnail/6a70666a203027476b3a2143.png"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> The US should be held accountable for continued “war crimes” against Iranian civilians, Foreign Ministry spokesman Esmaeil Baghaei told RT <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/russia/643796-qeshm-iran-american-airstrike/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> US airstrikes on residential areas and other non-military targets in Iran constitute“war crimes”for which Washington must be held accountable, Iranian Foreign Ministry spokesman Esmaeil Baghaei told RT at a press briefing on Monday. His remarks came after a US airstrike hit a residential neighborhood on Qeshm Island in Iran’s Hormozgan Province last week, leveling a family home and killing three people, including a two-year-old child. Iran said the strike hit a densely populated working-class neighborhood, with footage from the scene appearing to support that claim. US Central Command, however, insisted it had targeted Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps (IRGC) positions in retaliation for the force firing“multiple ballistic missiles”at US troops across the region earlier that week. Baghaei was commenting in particular on a New York Timesreportclaiming the neighborhood was struck by a 2,000-pound Mark 84 bomb – one of the largest conventional weapons in the US arsenal – citing analysis of videos, photographs, and satellite imagery. “Unfortunately, this has become the American way of warfare,”Baghaei said, adding that it was not the first time the US had targeted Iranian civilians and non-military sites with heavy weaponry.“What the US has done in Qeshm, Minab, Lamerd, and elsewhere constitutes war crimes. Every state is not only entitled but obligated to hold those responsible accountable.” He mentioned the infamous strike that came during the initial s","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 12:44:04 +0000",https://www.rt.com/russia/643796-qeshm-iran-american-airstrike/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-04 01:19:39
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Has Türkiye’s F-35 dream crashed for good?,Has Türkiye’s F-35 dream crashed for good?,"Has Türkiye’s F-35 dream crashed for good? <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.07/thumbnail/6a6b6e242030276dbb7b63c7.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Trump’s F-35 promises to Erdogan made headlines, but law, US Congress, and entrenched security politics still decide what actually moves <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643673-turkiye-f35-trump-diplomacy/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> ByMishel Bychkova, Vice-President, Center for Middle Eastern Studies (Moscow) An official letter sent by the US Department of State to Congress in late July set the dispute between Türkiye and the US over F-35 fighter jets back to square one. The transfer of the aircraft and Türkiye’s reinstatement in the program are still impossible because Ankara continues to possess the Russian-made S-400 air defense system and associated equipment, has not provided legally sufficient guarantees that it will avoid similar purchases in the future and has therefore failed to meet the conditions under which the US administration could certify to Congress that the security risks to the F-35 program had been removed. Washington has not closed the door on negotiations, allowing both sides to maintain the appearance of moving forward even though the legal situation has barely changed since Türkiye was expelled from the program. The letter appeared shortly after the NATO summit in Ankara, where Donald Trump, during a meeting with Turkish President Recep Tayyip Erdogan, said that sanctions on Türkiye could be lifted and indicated that the F-35 issue would be resolved positively. He did not announce a signed contract or specify a delivery date, but his words created the impression that the White House had already reached a political decision and that only technical obstacles remained. Erdogan referred to the aircraft previously produced for Türkiye and expressed confidence that Trump would honor his","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 11:46:55 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643673-turkiye-f35-trump-diplomacy/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-04 01:19:40
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Slovakia’s Fico mocks EU’s Russian fur dependency,Slovakia’s Fico mocks EU’s Russian fur dependency,"Slovakia’s Fico mocks EU’s Russian fur dependency <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.08/thumbnail/6a706cd885f54056a134ba81.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Slovak Prime Minister Robert Fico has slammed EU “hypocrisy” after Brussels lifted sanctions on Russian sable pelts <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643790-fico-russian-fur-eu-hypocricy/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> Slovak Prime Minister Robert Fico has mocked the European Commission for what he called blatant hypocrisy after it quietly exempted Russian luxury sable fur from sanctions, reportedly bowing to pressure from member states dependent on the trade. The EU initially banned imports of finished Russian fur garments shortly after the Ukraine conflict escalated in 2022, alongside luxury goods such as diamonds and caviar. Raw pelts remained legal until April, when Brussels closed the loophole by banning both raw and processed furskins, including sable. However, in its 21st sanctions package unveiled late last month – already diluted as member states balked at measures damaging their own economies – Brussels reversed course, exempting raw sable pelts while keeping the ban on finished fur garments. In a video posted on Facebook on Saturday, Fico said Brussels justified the exemption by arguing European luxury furriers had no alternative source for the rare pelts, which are used to make coats costing up to €100,000 ($117,000), as Russia dominates the sable trade. Media reports citing EU diplomats said Italy and Greece, the EU’s largest importers of Russian sable pelts and key hubs for luxury fur production, pushed for the carve-out. “EU hypocrisy blossoms like a cherry tree in May,”Fico said.“Goods we need for our industry or for everyday life are banned from being imported from Russia, even if they are difficult to replace and much more expensive to source elsewhere. But that won’t appl","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 10:35:18 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643790-fico-russian-fur-eu-hypocricy/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-04 01:19:42
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Israeli court blocks crocodile prison guard plan,Israeli court blocks crocodile prison guard plan,"Israeli court blocks crocodile prison guard plan <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.08/thumbnail/6a70228185f54056a134ba69.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> A Jerusalem court has temporarily blocked Ben-Gvir’s project to guard Israeli prisons with Nile crocodiles <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643789-israeli-court-blocks-ben-gvir/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> An Israeli court has temporarily blocked National Security Minister Itamar Ben-Gvir from using Nile crocodiles to guard security prisoners, most of them Palestinians.Ben-Gvir proposed surrounding prisons with crocodile-filled moats in December, arguing that the reptiles would strengthen security and deter escapes.While the Israel Nature and Parks Authority initially deemed the plan unfeasible because Nile crocodiles were considered wild animals that could be kept only in zoos and sanctuaries, the hurdle was removed last month when Environmental Protection Minister Idit Silman redesignated them as“tended wild animals,”potentially allowing their deployment at prisons.On Sunday, however, the Jerusalem District Court issued an injunction against the project following a petition by the animal-rights organization Let Animals Live.Judge Avraham Rubin ruled that the state may not locate crocodiles or prepare them for transfer until further notice. The order will remain in effect while the court considers a longer-term injunction, with the government required to respond by August 16.Ben-Gvir criticized the decision, accusing the judiciary of siding with“terrorists”and thwarting measures intended to strengthen Israeli deterrence.“We know that the terrorists are worried about the arrival of the crocodiles, but today the court came to their aid,”he said, as quoted by the Jerusalem Post.Nearly 10,000 Palestinian political prisoners are being held in Israeli prisons, according to rights gr","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 09:21:32 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643789-israeli-court-blocks-ben-gvir/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-04 01:19:43
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Rare virus with no cure detected in New York,Rare virus with no cure detected in New York,"Rare virus with no cure detected in New York <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.08/thumbnail/6a70047085f54056a134ba64.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> US-based Stony Brook Medicine has confirmed the first Bourbon virus case in New York and called for expanded surveillance and testing <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643787-bourbon-virus-new-york/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> The first case of Bourbon virus has been confirmed in New York, prompting researchers to call for expanded surveillance and testing amid warnings that the rare tick-borne infection may be more widespread than currently known. Discovered in 2014 and named after Bourbon County, Kansas, where it was first identified, the virus is believed to be transmitted by the lone star tick. There is no vaccine or medicine available to prevent or treat the illness. Symptoms include fever, fatigue, rash, headache, body aches, nausea, and vomiting. Only six human cases have been reported since the virus was identified, primarily in the central US. The first known patient, diagnosed in Kansas in 2014, died. According to a Stony Brook Medicinestudyreleased last month, Bourbon virus“could soon begin to complicate diagnoses if it becomes more prevalent this summer and in coming years.” Researchers studied blood samples from 107 patients who developed fever and other symptoms after recent tick bites in Suffolk County between 2019 and 2024 and found that two had antibodies to Bourbon virus. One of the patients, a 67-year-old Long Island man, developed severe symptoms and was hospitalized after being bitten by lone star ticks in 2021. He was initially treated with doxycycline for suspected Lyme disease, but his fatigue and severe headaches failed to improve. He eventually made a full recovery, but a re-examination of his test results showed an eightfold increase in Bourbon virus antibody levels over ","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 03:57:55 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643787-bourbon-virus-new-york/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-04 01:19:44
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Helicopters collide while battling wildfires (VIDEOS),Helicopters collide while battling wildfires (VIDEOS),"Helicopters collide while battling wildfires (VIDEOS) <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.08/thumbnail/6a6fe42d2030271a0d70c4c0.png"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Two Bell firefighting helicopters collided near Athens, killing a Greek coordinator and a Danish pilot. <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643785-firefighting-helicopter-crash-greece/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> Two firefighting helicopters collided in midair in Greece, killing two crew members, as hundreds of personnel battled at least 220 wildfires recorded nationwide over the past week, according to the Greek Fire Service. Nearly 500 firefighters and 23 aircraft were deployed to the main front west of Athens alone, but gale-force winds drove flames through dry forests and hampered the response, preventing some aircraft from safely reaching the sea to collect water. Hundreds of people were evacuated from coastal communities by boat after flames and smoke cut off roads. The collision occurred on Sunday near Psatha, around 70 km west of Athens, as the aircraft battled a major wildfire that broke out near Agios Vasileios on Friday before spreading toward Porto Germeno and the forested mountains west of the capital. BREAKING: Two firefighting helicopters collided Sunday while battling a wind-driven wildfire in the Porto Germeno area west of Athens. Video captured one of the aircraft crashing to the ground after the midair collision.pic.twitter.com/4kTHa7wR0V A Greek coordinator and a Danish pilot aboard one helicopter were killed, while the crew of the second aircraft – a Greek national and a British national – survived. No injuries were reported on the ground. 🚁 Battling the flames in Porto Germeno – Villia, Greece.Firefighters, supported by aerial firefighting operations, continue their efforts to contain the wildfire. Every minute counts in protecting lives, forests, and local commu","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 01:05:21 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643785-firefighting-helicopter-crash-greece/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-04 01:19:45
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Trump teases Iran talks as Truth Social starts selling fast access to his posts,Trump teases Iran talks as Truth Social starts selling fast access to his posts,"Trump teases Iran talks as Truth Social starts selling fast access to his posts <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.08/thumbnail/6a6fde1e203027231f2ac0fd.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> US President Donald Trump has teased new negotiations with Iran after abruptly calling off a major attack in a Truth Social post <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643786-trump-iran-truth-social/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> US President Donald Trump has teased new negotiations with Iran after abruptly calling off a major attack in a Truth Social post published on the same day that his media company began selling Wall Street firms millisecond-fast access to the platform’s market-moving content. Speaking to reporters aboard Air Force One on Sunday, Trump claimed that talks would begin on Monday and said several Middle Eastern governments had urged him to give diplomacy another chance. “We’re just going to see whether or not we can make a deal,”Trump said, claiming that the canceled operation would have been the“biggest attack since World War II.” Last Monday, Trump claimed that“very friendly negotiations”with Tehran were already underway. Within days, however, the US had resumed bombing Iran, while Trump adopted increasingly aggressive rhetoric, promising to hit the country“very hard.” The US Department of War declared it was“locked and loaded”and prepared to unleash what Trump claimed would be levels of military power not seen since World War II. US media reported on Friday that Washington and Israel were preparing anextensive campaignagainst Iranian power plants, refineries, and other energy infrastructure. The threats, combined with continued disruption to shipping through the Strait of Hormuz, helped sustain fears of a wider energy shock and propelled crude prices toward $90 a barrel. On Saturday, however, Trump abruptly called off the strikes in aTruth Social post, claiming that I","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 00:13:14 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643786-trump-iran-truth-social/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-04 01:19:46
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,"Over 70,000 petition against NYC Mayor Mamdani attending 9/11 commemoration","Over 70,000 petition against NYC Mayor Mamdani attending 9/11 commemoration","Over 70,000 petition against NYC Mayor Mamdani attending 9/11 commemoration <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.08/thumbnail/6a6fb3ba2030271f5546b59b.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> An online petition urging NYC Mayor Zohran Mamdani to stay away from the 9/11 celebrations, has gained over 70,000 backers <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643781-nyc-mayor-mamdani-petition/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> A petition urging New York City Mayor Zohran Mamdani to stay away from the commemoration of the 9/11 attacks has gained traction online, attracting more than 70,000 backers. This year marks the 25th anniversary of the attack, which resulted in nearly 3,000 fatalities and the destruction of the Twin Towers of the World Trade Center in New York City. The annual commemoration is customarily held at the monument built on the spot where the towers used to stand. It is frequented by senior local and federal officials. The upcoming anniversary sparked controversy well before the event, with a group of relatives of the victims launching a petition against Mamdani’s participation. According to the petitioners, the motion has nothing to do with the mayor’s religion, but with his controversial views and perceived connections to radicals. The petition, which was launched last month, reached 50,000 verified signatures earlier this week and over 70,000 as of Sunday. It calls out the Muslim mayor over what it described as“public positions, associations, and responses to rhetoric that many perceive as hostile to these shared values.” Among other things, it listed the mayor’s connections to radical Brooklyn Imam Siraj Wahhaj and the appointment of Ramzi Kassem, who previously represented a terrorist convicted in an Al-Qaeda tanker bombing plot. The petition also called out his father, Mahmood Mamdani, over his 2004 book ‘Good Muslim, Bad Muslim’, in which the political scientist argued t","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 21:16:58 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643781-nyc-mayor-mamdani-petition/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-04 01:19:47
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Top stories that shaped the past week,Top stories that shaped the past week,"Top stories that shaped the past week <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.08/thumbnail/6a6f94e82030271fcc6a4cf6.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> RT looks back at the top stories of the week and the latest developments connected to the hottest topics <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643772-top-stories-rt-weekly/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> RT showcases its top five stories of the week and dives deeper into the topics that shaped the news over the past seven days. FIFA crisis as testament to US decline In an opinion piece, foreign policy expert and historian Aleksandr Bobrov reflected on the ongoing FIFA crisis triggered by its controversial handling of the World Cup in the US. The tournament was marred by a series of scandals, including harsh treatment of national teams by immigration authorities, and the lifting of a ban on a US player following a call between President Donald Trump and FIFA President Gianni Infantino. Bobrov views the debacle as a manifestation of a broader US decline and Washington’s weakening grip on global institutions it can no longer fully control. The FIFA scandal has been further aggravated by Infantino’s botched attempt to sell to private investors stakes in a $20 billion subsidiary to run the World Cup. The plan met with an overwhelmingly negative reaction and was opposed by UEFA’s national associations and other federations around the globe. Infantino eventually abandoned it. While the scandal might not finish off FIFA itself, it is expected to result in the early departure of its embattled boss. British AI drive runs into energy shortage UK energy regulator Ofgem has proposed a plan to introduce stricter rules and additional fees for AI data center developers, supposedly aimed at tackling“unviable, stalled, or speculative projects.”The regulator now wants to slap a refundable fee o","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 19:09:31 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643772-top-stories-rt-weekly/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-04 01:19:48
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,UEFA has built football’s apartheid system – now it wants to play savior,UEFA has built football’s apartheid system – now it wants to play savior,"UEFA has built football’s apartheid system – now it wants to play savior <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.08/thumbnail/6a6f5c2c2030271d65766614.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> UEFA forced FIFA to abandon its World Cup investment plan, but the boycott was really about money, Russia, Israel and control <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643771-uefa-has-built-footballs-apartheid/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> ByAlan Moore, a Vilnius-based sports journalist and host of Capital Sports 3.0. A former athlete, he has over 30 years of professional sports and higher education experience across the globe. ByAlan Moore, a Vilnius-based sports journalist and host of Capital Sports 3.0. A former athlete, he has over 30 years of professional sports and higher education experience across the globe. As I sat in the Olympic Stadium in Athens on Thursday night, I would like to say I felt the hand of history on my shoulder, but instead I felt a sick feeling in my stomach at how European football has been irreversibly damaged by the holier than thou brigade at UEFA. UEFA, the governing body for football in Europe and subordinate only to global overseer FIFA and to the richest clubs on the continent, has effectively created a full-on apartheid system that sees the rich get even richer and their power increasingly unchecked. And they showed their power in beating back FIFA’s bid to commercialize their biggest cash cow: the World Cup. In 1971, Panathinaikos made it to the final of the European Champions Cup, the previous name of the UEFA Champions League. The first and only Greek club to do so, they lost 2-0 to mighty Ajax of Amsterdam, who at the time were in their pomp with the late Johan Cruyff. The Greeks subsequently made two semifinals, in 1985 and 1996, but on Thursday played in the continent’s third tier competition, the UEFA Conference League. If the capital club go on to win thi","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 15:11:07 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643771-uefa-has-built-footballs-apartheid/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-04 01:19:49
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Sunken Nazi warships resurface in Europe amid record heatwave (PHOTOS),Sunken Nazi warships resurface in Europe amid record heatwave (PHOTOS),"Sunken Nazi warships resurface in Europe amid record heatwave (PHOTOS) <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.08/thumbnail/6a6e5a1685f540353e379464.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Water levels in the Danube River have reached record lows, revealing relics of the past ranging from shipwrecks to mammoth bones <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643756-nazi-warships-europe-heatwave/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> Several sunken World War II-era Nazi warships have resurfaced in the Danube River amid a major heatwave and prolonged drought. The vessels became visible as the water level in Europe’s second-longest river fell to record lows. Photos and videos posted on social media showed massive shipwrecks lying in the water and on a sand ridge in the middle of the waterway near the village of Prahovo in Serbia. Elsewhere, the wreck of a Hungarian cargo ship that sank in 1937 resurfaced near the Croatian village of Opatovac. Some 200 vessels could be lying on the bottom of the Danube River, according to the European Investment Bank. River transport has nearly come to a halt due to the low water levels, according to Hungary’s Transport Ministry. 🇷🇸🇭🇷 A sunken German flotilla has surfaced in Serbia due to the shallowing of the Danube, Reuters reports.The rusting hulks of the German flotilla, sunk in 1944 during the retreat before the Red Army, are reportedly posing a threat to shipping.pic.twitter.com/WwacLDGlgC Hungarian Prime Minister Peter Magyar also said that the Paks nuclear power plant, which covers nearly half of Hungary’s electricity needs, could be shut down for weeks because of insufficient water levels. Na Dunavu kod Prahova.Stari nacististički brodovi se vide zbog niskog vodostaja.📷Đorđe Kojadinovićpic.twitter.com/b44rZe2H4J In Budapest, a German WWII artillery shell was found near Margaret Bridge – one of the city’s major traffic arteries – last week. The discovery pro","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 14:45:27 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643756-nazi-warships-europe-heatwave/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-04 01:19:49
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,US punished Colombia’s outgoing leader for calling Gaza war ‘genocide’ – FM to RT (VIDEO),US punished Colombia’s outgoing leader for calling Gaza war ‘genocide’ – FM to RT (VIDEO),"US punished Colombia’s outgoing leader for calling Gaza war ‘genocide’ – FM to RT (VIDEO) <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.08/thumbnail/6a6f3428203027681706a019.png"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Israel is to blame for the US’ long-running tensions with Colombia’s outgoing President Gustavo Petro, FM Rosa Yolanda Villavicencio told RT <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643770-colombia-trump-palestine-israel/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> Israel is at the heart of Washington’s long-running tensions with Colombia and its outgoing President Gustavo Petro, Foreign Minister Rosa Yolanda Villavicencio has told RT. In an exclusive interview aired on Sunday, Villavicencio insisted that the decisive factor behind US sanctions on Petro was not his alleged failure to combat drug trafficking but rather his outspoken support for Palestine and repeated accusations that Israel was committing genocide in Gaza. Relations between Bogota and Washington – Colombia’s largest trading partner – steadily deteriorated during Petro’s presidency over US policy in Latin America, particularly toward Venezuela and Cuba, regional anti-drug efforts, and broader geopolitical differences, most notably Petro’s outspoken support for Palestine and criticism of Israel. This culminated in Washington sanctioning Petro last year, accusing him of“allowing drug cartels to flourish”and“refusing to stop”narcotics trafficking. US President Donald Trump called Petro an“illegal drug leader,”and openly backed right-wing presidential candidate Abelardo de la Espriella, who campaigned on restoring closer ties with Washington, over Petro ally and left-wing Senator Ivan Cepeda in the election earlier this year. Villavicencio rejected Washington’s justification for sanctioning Petro, arguing that his administration had delivered record results in combating drug trafficking. “We are talking about record-breaking seizures ","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 14:32:20 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643770-colombia-trump-palestine-israel/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-04 01:19:51
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,US and Israel staged Spain migration invasion – Iran,US and Israel staged Spain migration invasion – Iran,"US and Israel staged Spain migration invasion – Iran <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.08/thumbnail/6a6f4942203027726045c406.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Iran has accused the US and Israel of engineering Spain’s deadly migrant crisis in Ceuta to punish Madrid over Gaza and Iran war stance <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643773-us-israel-staged-spain-migrant-crisis/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> The US and Israel orchestrated the mass migrant crossing from Morocco into Spain’s North African enclave of Ceuta to punish Madrid for its refusal to bow to pressure on the Middle East conflicts, Iran’s embassy in Kenya has suggested. Spain has been at odds with Washington and West Jerusalem over the Gaza war and strikes on Iran. Over the past several days, roughly 50,000 to 60,000 migrants crossed from Morocco into Ceuta by land and sea in numbers equivalent to some 70% of the enclave’s regular population. The local authorities admitted they had been“completely overwhelmed”by the sudden surge. The crisis, the largest human traffic invasion in the EU’s history, claimed the lives of at least 86 people, a toll expected to rise further. Many of the victims drowned in the sea or were crushed in the stampede at border checkpoints. On Friday, the Iranian Embassy in Nairobi described the migrant surge as“an operation organized by Washington and Tel Aviv – coordinated with certain neighboring authorities – to destabilize Spain.” It also branded the crisis“a gift to Europe’s far right”and“punishment for the country that dared to challenge the American Empire and its Israeli henchmen,”warning that“the empire never tolerates defiance.” Neither the US nor Israel commented on the accusation. However, Israeli Ambassador to the UN Danny Danon slammed Spain’s handling of the crisis.“Spain, which never misses an opportunity to lecture Israel, has declared a state of emergency in Ceuta f","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 14:10:37 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643773-us-israel-staged-spain-migrant-crisis/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-04 01:19:52
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,ASEAN: The last place where serious diplomacy still happens,ASEAN: The last place where serious diplomacy still happens,"ASEAN: The last place where serious diplomacy still happens <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.07/thumbnail/6a6b667c20302762cc5441d5.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> With conflict spreading and old forums faltering, Manila became one of the rare places where powers still chose dialogue <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643671-asean-diplomacy-still-happens/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> ByLadislav Zemánek, non-resident research fellow at China-CEE Institute and expert of the Valdai Discussion Club ByLadislav Zemánek, non-resident research fellow at China-CEE Institute and expert of the Valdai Discussion Club In late July, the Philippines did something that has become increasingly rare. It made great powers sit down. Under the chairmanship of the Philippines, the 59th ASEAN Foreign Ministers’ Meeting in Manila and its dense constellation of related gatherings turned the capital into one of the few reliable stages where rivals still appear in the same rooms, exchange views, and keep channels open. From July 20 to 24, foreign ministers from Southeast Asia, the United States, China, Russia, Japan, India, Europe, and beyond convened against a distinctly unsettled backdrop of escalating hostilities between the US and Iran and rising tensions between Beijing and the Philippines after incidents in the South China Sea. Yet ASEAN did what it has long done best – it refused to let the friction dictate the terms. The organization offered something that is in very short supply in the modern world of competing geopolitical blocs: a neutral platform where conversation remains possible and practical cooperation continues. The timing was anything but comfortable. The Middle East conflict has already begun to squeeze energy prices, shipping insurance, and supply-chain calculations across Asia. For a region whose growth remains tightly linked to imported fuel, the risks are ve","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 11:47:38 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643671-asean-diplomacy-still-happens/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-04 01:19:53
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Trump cancels planned attack on Iran,Trump cancels planned attack on Iran,"Trump cancels planned attack on Iran <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.08/thumbnail/6a6ecd8a85f54057a766c94c.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Trump has canceled a planned attack on Iran after saying the outlines of a deal had been agreed to reopen the Strait of Hormuz <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643765-trump-cancels-planned-attack-iran/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> US President Donald Trump has canceled a planned attack on Iran after saying the outlines of an agreement had been reached that could reopen the Strait of Hormuz and address what he described as Tehran’s“nuclear threat.” CBS News reported that the US and Israel had been preparing a major bombing campaign against the Islamic Republic’s energy infrastructure that could begin as early as the weekend. The network said the proposed operation, which it described as potentially one of the harshest campaigns against Iran to date, was expected to target power plants and oil refineries, while military officials also reportedly discussed cutting electricity across Tehran. In a post on Truth Social on Saturday, Trump wrote that despite the US being“locked and loaded”to strike Iran at“levels of Military Terror, Strength, and Power not seen since World War II,”he had agreed to requests from Tehran and Middle Eastern nations to hold off on the attack because the“parameters”of a deal had been agreed upon. Trump said the proposed agreement would include“the Immediate, Complete, and Total OPENING OF THE HORMUZ STRAIT, and an end to Iran’s nuclear threat.” “Based on this request, I have agreed, for the future benefit of the WORLD and, likewise, the survival of a successful and prosperous Iran, to cancel the attack, subject to being able to rapidly make a DEAL,”Trump wrote, adding that Israel had joined Washington in the commitment. Iranian officials, however, disputed Trump’s account. A source ","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 10:37:03 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643765-trump-cancels-planned-attack-iran/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-04 01:19:53
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,WATCH devastating wildfires tear through Washington state,WATCH devastating wildfires tear through Washington state,"WATCH devastating wildfires tear through Washington state <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.08/thumbnail/6a6ef5312030276e9d72ad78.png"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Thousands of families have been ordered to evacuate as fast-moving wildfires sweep through Spokane County in Washington state <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643767-wildfires-spokane-washington-us/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> Wildfires burning across more than 100,000 hectares in Washington state, US, have triggered widespread evacuations and power outages around the city of Spokane, state officials said on Saturday. Large parts of Spokane County were placed under the highest Level 3 evacuation order as strong winds drove flames into residential areas. Officials urged residents to leave immediately“due to the life-threatening conditions,”while an evacuation shelter was opened at a local community college. The largest blaze, the Old Trails Fire, ignited around noon and had burned more than 1,000 hectares by late afternoon, according to the Washington State Department of Natural Resources (DNR). The fire spread rapidly through brush and grass into residential neighborhoods. Videos circulating on social media showed burning homes, towering plumes of smoke, and orange skies as long lines of vehicles fled the area. Volleyball friends on the way out of the evacuation zone in Spokane on W Strong, after evacuating from Spike and Dig but then being trapped at the Indian Trail Safeway#OldTrailsFire#WAWildfirepic.twitter.com/fBGmRbktYD Washington State Forester George Geissler said the blaze threatened about 4,000 structures. Man this is not good. A community off of Tiffany Ave. in Spokane, with homes on fire, and not a single fire engine in sight. After watching the devastation unfold in Altadena and the Palisades in 2025, seeing neighborhoods once again surrounded by flames is gut-wrenching.🎥KHQ…pic.twitte","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 08:44:29 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643767-wildfires-spokane-washington-us/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-04 01:19:54
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,US politicians are swearing more than ever – study,US politicians are swearing more than ever – study,"US politicians are swearing more than ever – study <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.08/thumbnail/6a6eea6185f540562067dcf3.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Trump and Biden accounted for 78% of all swear words publicly used by US presidents since 1919, a Cardiff University study has found <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643766-us-politicians-public-profanity/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> US politicians are using profanity in public far more frequently than in the past, according to research published by Cardiff University politics lecturer Dr Joseph Phillips. Some 87% of the 692 documented instances of presidents, vice presidents, and presidential candidates using profanity in public have occurred in just the last decade, Phillips wrote. The overwhelming majority of those cases – 78% – came from President Donald Trump and his predecessor Joe Biden, according to the study published this week. On Wednesday, Trump was heard using another expletive following an Iranian attack on US forces in Jordan. According to Fox News’ chief foreign affairs correspondent, Trey Yingst, the president said:“We’re going to beat the f**king s**t out of them.”Biden previously made headlines while serving as vice president, when he was caught on a hot mic telling then-President Barack Obama that signing the 2010 Affordable Care Act was a“big f**king deal.” For US presidents to use profanity publicly was once exceptionally rare, Phillips noted. According to the study, President Woodrow Wilson became the first to publicly use a naughty word, when he said he’d made a“conspicuous *ss of himself”in 1919. However, Trump has introduced a broader range of profanities into presidential rhetoric, using words such as“bullsh*t,”“ba***rd,”“b***ch,”and“f**k”in speeches, interviews, and social media posts, according to Phillips. The researcher argued that the trend reflects broader changes in polit","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 07:09:26 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643766-us-politicians-public-profanity/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-04 01:19:55
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,"Killers of Russian siblings confess to more murders in Thailand (PHOTOS, VIDEOS)","Killers of Russian siblings confess to more murders in Thailand (PHOTOS, VIDEOS)","Killers of Russian siblings confess to more murders in Thailand (PHOTOS, VIDEOS) <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.08/thumbnail/6a6e9aa785f54046c0131f15.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Four suspects have been arrested in Thailand in connection with the high-profile murders of two Russian nationals and a local family <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643761-russians-killed-thailand-kidnapping/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> Thai police have arrested four suspects in a high-profile case involving the kidnapping and murder of two Russian nationals and a local family of three. Diana Nazimova, 22, and her brother Roman, 17, disappeared near the resort city of Pattaya earlier this week. The siblings moved to Thailand with their mother several years ago and lived in the Huai Yai area southeast of Pattaya. According to police, they left their home on a rented Honda ADV 150 motorcycle before dawn on July 26. Shortly afterwards, Diana sent her mother a message saying that someone appeared to be following them, before contact with the two was lost. CCTV footage showed them speaking with another motorcyclist not far from their home before their disappearance, according to local media. The incident prompted a search operation, and their vehicle was discovered three days later, dismantled and buried in a wooded area near an abandoned cemetery. Police identified two men – Thana ‘Pong’Koedthong, 43, and Thongchai ‘Thong’Srinil, 39 – as the principal suspects in the case. The two were detained near Thailand’s border with Cambodia on July 31 following a five-day manhunt. BREAKING: Two Russian siblings missing in#Thailandhave been killed over a motorcycle.17-year-old Roman was shot dead.His 22-year-old sister Diana was beaten to death.Thai police arrested two suspects near the#Cambodian🇰🇭 border. The men confessed to murdering the pair…pic.twitter.com/hFMz769EFh During questioning, th","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 04:07:58 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643761-russians-killed-thailand-kidnapping/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-04 01:19:56
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Chaotic shootout outside US burger joint kills three (VIDEOS),Chaotic shootout outside US burger joint kills three (VIDEOS),"Chaotic shootout outside US burger joint kills three (VIDEOS) <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.08/thumbnail/6a6eabd985f54061244ce8bd.png"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Three people were killed and two others injured in a shooting at an Idaho In-N-Out, where witnesses say an armed bystander returned fire. <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643762-idaho-restaurant-shootout-killed/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> Three people were killed and at least two others injured when a gunman opened fire at a crowded In-N-Out restaurant in Idaho, triggering an apparent exchange of gunfire with an armed bystander. The attack unfolded at around 2:30pm on Saturday in Twin Falls, approximately 130 miles (210km) southeast of Boise. The restaurant had opened only about a week earlier and was packed with customers in one of the city’s busiest commercial districts. The shooting apparently began inside the restaurant before spilling into the surrounding area, according to footage showing terrified customers and employees fleeing into the parking lot and onto the road as shots rang out. Video circulating online shows a man armed with an AR-style rifle and dressed in a black shirt and jeans walking out of the venue as the crowd flees. He then approaches a white car, opens its trunk and reaches inside. BREAKING: Active shooter reported near the In-N-Out Burger at Canyon Rim in Twin Falls, Idaho; according to police.pic.twitter.com/RbWtWahDq8 In another clip, the suspect is seen walking through a parking lot near a Tesla charging station and firing several shots. WATCH: Active shooter roaming around Twin Falls Visitor Center in Idaho, seen firing at a Tesla vehicle.pic.twitter.com/QGOViBoLMR Separate footage appears to show another man firing a pistol at the rifleman. Eyewitness Lane Koehn, 34, also told the Associated Press that he saw a man with a handgun open fire after the suspected attacker","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 02:34:29 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643762-idaho-restaurant-shootout-killed/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-04 01:19:57
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,"No spontaneous combustion? Regarding the causes of the Ceuta migrant surge, look who’s gloating","No spontaneous combustion? Regarding the causes of the Ceuta migrant surge, look who’s gloating","No spontaneous combustion? Regarding the causes of the Ceuta migrant surge, look who’s gloating <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.08/thumbnail/6a6e60ee20302733fe3a9e43.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> The Ceuta migrant surge was sold as a border panic. The harder question is who benefited from lighting the fuse. <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643757-no-spontaneous-combustion-regarding-causes/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> ByTarik Cyril Amar, a historian from Germany working at Koç University, Istanbul, on Russia, Ukraine, and Eastern Europe, the history of World War II, the cultural Cold War, and the politics of memory ByTarik Cyril Amar, a historian from Germany working at Koç University, Istanbul, on Russia, Ukraine, and Eastern Europe, the history of World War II, the cultural Cold War, and the politics of memory The recent burst of illegal migration into Spain’s Moroccan exclave of Ceuta was, above all, a sensational media event produced for political effect. It will have lasting consequences, but not in terms of who ended up where: Of the about 50,000 migrants who suddenly, as if on command, stormed Ceuta by land and sea,almost all quickly went back to Morocco. According to the EU’s home affairs commissioner,not a singleCeuta-crasher made it to the European mainland. In that sense, the whole thing might as well not have happened. Apocalyptic fantasies of Ceuta turning into a wide open gate to the rest of fortress Europe were always, at best, silly: no, you can’t just travel on into Spain from there or to British Gibraltar, for that matter. Worse, there have been many deliberate attempts at political profiteering by spreading panic. All through the West, figures from across the political spectrum did not miss a beat trying to exploit the Ceuta emergency: In America, PresidentDonald Trump– under pressure from his self-imposed fiasco in Iran – spoke of a“catast","Sat, 01 Aug 2026 21:17:44 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643757-no-spontaneous-combustion-regarding-causes/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-04 01:19:58
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Why Western Europe needs a Russian threat,Why Western Europe needs a Russian threat,"Why Western Europe needs a Russian threat <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.08/thumbnail/6a6e105220302739ea08d354.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> As the US steps back from Europe, the Russian threat offers Brussels a unifying cause – and Ukraine the army needed to sustain confrontation <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643747-western-europe-needs-russian-threat/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> ByFyodor Lukyanov, the editor-in-chief of Russia in Global Affairs, chairman of the Presidium of the Council on Foreign and Defense Policy, and research director of the Valdai International Discussion Club. ByFyodor Lukyanov, the editor-in-chief of Russia in Global Affairs, chairman of the Presidium of the Council on Foreign and Defense Policy, and research director of the Valdai International Discussion Club. The term 'collective West', widely used in Russia, is rarely employed in the West itself, except perhaps when discussing Russian political thinking. What’s commonly heard, however, is the long-running debate over what the West actually is and that discussion has continued in philosophy and politics since at least the 18th century. The concept has never had a fixed definition, even among those who are supposedly part of it so instead, the West has usually been defined in opposition to something else. At different times, that “other” has been Byzantium and Eastern Orthodoxy, the Ottoman Empire and the Islamic world, or even Germany, which was once regarded by some as alien to the European spirit. Russia has frequently occupied the same role, albeit there have been periods when Russia was considered part of the Western community, but this generally happened when Western Europe’s great powers needed the support of a major ally against one of their own rivals, and once that purpose had been served, Russia was once again treated as an outsider. There was also a longstanding d","Sat, 01 Aug 2026 20:15:13 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643747-western-europe-needs-russian-threat/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-04 01:19:59
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Germany has reached a new low in election rigging,Germany has reached a new low in election rigging,"Germany has reached a new low in election rigging <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.07/thumbnail/6a6b56b885f5402e8747fc49.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Local officials in Lower Saxony are blocking AfD candidates from running, using intelligence reports instead of courts or due process. <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643665-germany-afd-voter-suppression/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> ByTarik Cyril Amar, a historian from Germany working at Koç University, Istanbul, on Russia, Ukraine, and Eastern Europe, the history of World War II, the cultural Cold War, and the politics of memory ByTarik Cyril Amar, a historian from Germany working at Koç University, Istanbul, on Russia, Ukraine, and Eastern Europe, the history of World War II, the cultural Cold War, and the politics of memory Today’s Germany is a grim, unhappy place. Thirty-six years after West Germany’s take-over of the former East Germany (polite term: re-unification), which was supposed to herald a golden age of national fulfilment, citizens are in a very foul mood. According to Ipsos, one of Germany’s go-to pollsters, their morale is at a“historic nadir,”and they are“losing confidence about the country’s future.”As of last month, fear of poverty and inequality was“clearly increasing,”with 37 percent of all respondents picking it as their number-one angst, followed by“migration”(31 percent),“inflation”(30 percent), worries over the healthcare system (26 percent) and“criminality and violence”(25 percent). Note that all top five anxieties focus on what is going wrong at home. That doesn’t mean, though, that Germans are optimistic about the world or Germany’s place in it: 24 percent of the Ipsos poll respondents fear“military conflicts between states.” If the mood is sour, it’s very good reasons: Germany’s abysmally,unprecedentedly unpopularandembattledchancellor, Friedrich Merz, is desperately trying t","Sat, 01 Aug 2026 15:00:02 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643665-germany-afd-voter-suppression/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-04 01:19:59
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,US to step back from NATO Ukraine aid group leadership – Politico,US to step back from NATO Ukraine aid group leadership – Politico,"US to step back from NATO Ukraine aid group leadership – Politico <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.08/thumbnail/6a6df83f85f54057a766c8ec.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> The Pentagon will reportedly hand command of Ukraine aid mission to another bloc member as the US scales back its military role in Europe <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643743-us-drop-nato-ukraine-assistance/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> The Pentagon is planning to transfer leadership of the Germany-based NATO command coordinating military aid to Ukraine to another member of the military bloc as Washington continues to scale back its military presence in Europe, Politico reported on Friday, citing an unnamed NATO official. Ukraine has been heavily dependent on weapons supplies from its Western backers throughout the conflict, which is now in its fifth year. Moscow has condemned the weapons shipments to Ukraine, arguing that they only prolong the conflict without changing the outcome, and warning that the military assistance shows that NATO is a direct party to the conflict, thereby risking a direct confrontation between Russia and the bloc. The reported plan follows a broader shift in US defense policy under President Donald Trump, whose administration plans to reduce troops and critical weapons systems in Europe and redirect some resources to Asia and other regions. The White House has also pushed NATO members in Europe to take greater responsibility for regional security to significantly raise defense spending. The Security Assistance Group-Ukraine (SAG-U), based in the German city of Wiesbaden, coordinates weapons deliveries, training and logistical support for Ukraine. The NATO official told Politico that the transition is expected to take up to a year, while a US deputy will remain involved through the alliance’s military command structure. SAG-U was always intended to be a temporary organ","Sat, 01 Aug 2026 14:16:45 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643743-us-drop-nato-ukraine-assistance/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-04 01:20:00
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,"Strongest quake in 40 years rocks Italy’s volcanic region, injures dozens (VIDEOS)","Strongest quake in 40 years rocks Italy’s volcanic region, injures dozens (VIDEOS)","Strongest quake in 40 years rocks Italy’s volcanic region, injures dozens (VIDEOS) <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.08/thumbnail/6a6df1e9203027325534bc62.png"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> At least 26 people have been injured after the strongest earthquake in four decades struck Italy’s Campi Flegrei volcanic area near Naples <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643745-quake-italy-volcanic-region/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> A magnitude 4.7 earthquake struck the Campi Flegrei volcanic region near Naples in southern Italy on Friday evening, injuring at least 26 people, two of them critically, and damaging dozens of buildings. The earthquake hit at 7:46pm local time at a shallow depth of about 3km, according to Italy’s National Institute of Geophysics and Volcanology (INGV). Its epicenter was between the towns of Pozzuoli and Quarto. Civil protection officials said that it was the strongest quake recorded in the area since continuous instrumental monitoring began, surpassing two magnitude 4.6 tremors registered in 2025. The quake was felt across Naples, Ischia, Procida, and much of the Gulf of Naples. Seismographs have since recorded more than 60 aftershocks, the strongest measuring magnitude 3.8 late on Friday and another of 3.1 early on Saturday. Civil Protection Minister Nello Musumeci warned that the seismic swarm is continuing and that further earthquakes above magnitude 3 remain possible. The worst damage was reported in Pozzuoli, where falling masonry, collapsing facades, and landslides damaged homes, businesses, and parked vehicles, according to multiple videos posted online. Grietas en casas, derrumbes, coches dañados y diez personas levemente heridas. Este es el primer reportaje del fuerte terremoto de magnitud 4.7 que sacudió la zona de Campi Flegrei esta tarde, con el epicentro en la zona de Solfatara de Pozzuoli. En las comunas de Flegrei, los…pic.twitter.c","Sat, 01 Aug 2026 14:09:23 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643745-quake-italy-volcanic-region/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-04 01:20:01
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,OpenAI uncovers more AI breakout incidents – Reuters,OpenAI uncovers more AI breakout incidents – Reuters,"OpenAI uncovers more AI breakout incidents – Reuters <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.08/thumbnail/6a6ddccd85f54048606bedb2.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> OpenAI has found more AI containment breaches while investigating last month’s Hugging Face hack, Reuters reports citing sources <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643742-openai-ai-breakouts-probe/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> OpenAI has uncovered additional cases in which its autonomous AI models breached containment and acted without human instruction, Reuters has reported, citing sources. The findings come as the company expands its investigation into a hacking incident last month in which an AI bot went rogue while attempting to cheat in an internal cybersecurity test. During tests of GPT-5.6 Sol and another unreleased model, both stripped of their safety guardrails, the systems were assigned ExploitGym – a benchmark designed to measure AI models’ ability to identify and exploit known software vulnerabilities. Instead of completing the tasks, one model escaped its supposedly isolated testing environment, gained internet access and hacked into Hugging Face – an online repository for AI models and datasets – in search of ready-made answers. OpenAI initially said the intrusion was limited to Hugging Face. However, in a statement on Wednesday, it acknowledged the hacking spree had also compromised four accounts across four separate services. On Friday, Reuters reported that additional containment breaches had since been uncovered, although it remains unclear how many incidents occurred, when they happened or what systems they targeted. One source told the news agency the breaches were limited in scope and that none of the AI bots are believed to have left OpenAI’s internal network. Reuters said OpenAI and outside experts are also reviewing logs from earlier this year to determine whether other simi","Sat, 01 Aug 2026 13:51:24 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643742-openai-ai-breakouts-probe/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-04 01:20:02
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Trump warns US faces Spain-style migrant invasion,Trump warns US faces Spain-style migrant invasion,"Trump warns US faces Spain-style migrant invasion <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.08/thumbnail/6a6dbf3085f54045b852962a.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> US President Donald Trump used Spain’s migration crisis to claim the US was overrun by illegal newcomers under his predecessor <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643740-trump-us-faces-spain-migrants/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> The surge of migrants across the border from Morocco into Spain is an example of what could happen to the US if Republicans aren’t elected, US President Donald Trump has claimed. Trump has repeatedly attacked his political opponents over immigration, blaming his predecessor Joe Biden for illegal border crossings. An estimated 50,000 migrants, mostly young men, swam from Morocco and crossed into the Spanish exclave of Ceuta earlier this week in an unprecedented influx that triggered a humanitarian crisis in the city. The Spanish Interior Ministry has reported that around 48,000 had voluntarily returned by Friday evening. “What’s happening with Spain, with tens of thousands of Illegal Immigrants invading it, happened in the United States during the Sleepy Joe Biden Administration, and it will happen again, only worse, if the Dumocrats ever again gain power,”Trump said late on Friday in a brief post on Truth Social, urging Americans to vote Republican in the midterm elections. The remarks come ahead of US midterm elections scheduled for November as Trump faces slipping approval ratings. A recent poll found that most US adults believe he has not focused enough on the everyday concerns of ordinary Americans, that his economic policies have worsened conditions, and that his military decisions in Iran have harmed the US. White House principal deputy press secretary Anna Kelly said on Friday that Trump“has long warned Europe what would happen if they continue to implement far-left, g","Sat, 01 Aug 2026 09:45:43 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643740-trump-us-faces-spain-migrants/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-04 01:20:03
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,US can take ‘whatever we want’ from Ukraine – Trump,US can take ‘whatever we want’ from Ukraine – Trump,"US can take ‘whatever we want’ from Ukraine – Trump <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.08/thumbnail/6a6da57185f54067fb780f69.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> The US can take “whatever we want” from Ukraine’s rare earth deposits under a 2025 pact, Donald Trump has claimed <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643741-us-take-whatever-we-want-ukraine-trump/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> The US can take“pretty much whatever we want”from Ukraine’s rare earth deposits under a minerals agreement signed last year, President Donald Trump has said, adding that profits from the agreement could ultimately exceed total American aid to Kiev since 2022. Trump made the remarks in an interview with Real America’s Voice aired on Friday as he chastised his predecessor Joe Biden for“giving away”a purported $300 billion in military support to Ukraine without securing repayment. “He could have Europe… paid for it. All you had to do is ask,”Trump said, adding that under his administration European nations now cover more of the costs. Trump said Ukraine has“very rich, very fertile soil in terms of rare earth.”“We have a contract signed [with Ukraine] having to do with rare earth. We can go in there at any time we want and take pretty much whatever we want. That was a pretty good deal,”he said. The US president was referring to a rare earth deal signed in Washington in April 2025, which established the US-Ukraine Reconstruction Investment Fund. The deal grants Washington preferential access to new Ukrainian mineral, oil, and gas projects, with emphasis on elements such as lithium, titanium, graphite, and uranium. Ukraine retains formal ownership of its resources and receives 50% of profits from new extraction projects. Trump has portrayed the deal as a way to pay for US military aid to Kiev. While he has claimed it amounted to more than $300 billion, the figure is widely disputed","Sat, 01 Aug 2026 07:52:11 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643741-us-take-whatever-we-want-ukraine-trump/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-04 01:20:04
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,New abuse probe raises Epstein behavior at elite US arts school,New abuse probe raises Epstein behavior at elite US arts school,"New abuse probe raises Epstein behavior at elite US arts school <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.07/thumbnail/6a6cb867203027597b652985.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> A Michigan arts school probe found 70 abuse accounts spanning decades, including allegations against the late pedophile Jeffrey Epstein <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643723-abuse-probe-epstein-art-school/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> An investigation into a prestigious arts school in the US state of Michigan has uncovered decades of alleged sexual misconduct by dozens of faculty and staff members, while also revealing new allegations involving the late pedophile Jeffrey Epstein. The 97-pagereport, released by Sanghavi Law Office earlier this week, was commissioned by the Interlochen Center for the Arts in 2024, to investigate allegations of abuse against several faculty members. The inquiry was later broadened and ultimately included allegations involving Epstein, a donor to the school. Investigators collected 70 accounts from former students alleging physical conduct of a sexual nature involving 47 faculty and staff members between the 1950s and the 2010s, with most of the reported incidents occurring before 2000. The report describes a pattern of misconduct ranging from grooming, flirting, and inappropriate touching to sexual contact. Epstein, who attended Interlochen’s summer camp in 1967 and donated more than $400,000 to the institution between 1990 and 2003, according to media reports, is also the subject of allegations in the report. Two former students accused the disgraced financier of sexual misconduct. One woman told investigators Epstein repeatedly touched her inappropriately under the guise of accidental contact while she was staying in a camp building that then bore his name. She said he later paid for trips to New York, where the unwanted touching continued. Another former student ","Sat, 01 Aug 2026 03:02:11 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643723-abuse-probe-epstein-art-school/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-04 01:20:05
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Anthropic says Claude AI models launched three unintended cyberattacks,Anthropic says Claude AI models launched three unintended cyberattacks,"Anthropic says Claude AI models launched three unintended cyberattacks <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.07/thumbnail/6a6c952e203027266a7af00c.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Anthropic has reported three cases in which its Claude AI models unintentionally targeted real companies during cybersecurity evaluations. <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643717-anthropic-accidental-hacking-review/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> AI developer Anthropic has disclosed three incidents in which its Claude AI models unintentionally targeted real-world organizations during cybersecurity evaluations that were supposed to take place in an isolated environment. The cases were identified retrospectively during a review prompted by a similar incident involving OpenAI and Hugging Face, an online repository for AI models and datasets, which was reported this month. Anthropic said that it had found three incidents dating back to April. In each case, a misconfigured test environment retained access to the internet, enabling Claude to interact with real companies and public services. The company attributed the problem to a“misunderstanding”with its evaluation partner, Irregular. The tests involved“capture the flag”exercises requiring Claude to obtain restricted information from simulated targets. However, the model was incorrectly told that the network had no connection to the outside world, pushing it toward treating any systems it encountered as part of the exercise. In one case, the fictional company that Claude had been instructed to infiltrate shared its name with a real internet domain. The model accessed the genuine site during four separate test runs and extracted information that reportedly included application and infrastructure credentials. During another evaluation, Claude encountered fictional instructions directing a software engineer to install Python code. It then uploaded a m","Fri, 31 Jul 2026 23:52:40 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643717-anthropic-accidental-hacking-review/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-04 01:20:06
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Kiev’s dirty war goes global,Kiev’s dirty war goes global,"Kiev’s dirty war goes global <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.07/thumbnail/6a6b4cc8203027435c32f401.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> From Africa to the Caspian Sea, each strike is an attempt to market Ukraine as a useful Western asset that still deserves cash and weapons <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643658-kiev-drone-war-global/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> ByMurad Sadygzade, President of the Middle East Studies Center, Visiting Lecturer, HSE University (Moscow). ByMurad Sadygzade, President of the Middle East Studies Center, Visiting Lecturer, HSE University (Moscow). On the morning of July 25, Ukrainian drones attacked an Iranian merchant vessel in the Caspian Sea. An explosion occurred on board, killing one sailor and injuring another. Tehran described the incident as an act of aggression, summoned Ukraine’s chargé d’affaires and warned that retaliatory measures could follow. Vladimir Zelensky did not deny that the operation had taken place, claiming that the targets were vessels allegedly involved in transporting military cargo linked to Iran. Yet within days, Ukrainian diplomacy abruptly changed its tone. Foreign Minister Andrey Sibiga told his Iranian counterpart that the merchant vessel had been struck unintentionally, after which discussions over compensation began. So long as the operation could be presented to Western audiences as another demonstration of the long-range capabilities of the Ukrainian security services, Kiev was eager to speak of success. Once it became clear that Tehran intended to demand accountability, the initial bravado gave way to attempts to portray the incident as an accident. In other words, the Ukrainian leadership sought to reap the publicity benefits of the strike without showing any willingness to accept responsibility for its consequences. At almost the same time, reports emerged from Iraq ","Fri, 31 Jul 2026 23:28:53 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643658-kiev-drone-war-global/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-04 01:20:07
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,US and Israel preparing to bomb Iranian energy infrastructure – media,US and Israel preparing to bomb Iranian energy infrastructure – media,"US and Israel preparing to bomb Iranian energy infrastructure – media <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.07/thumbnail/6a6d4a7985f54045b852961d.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> The US and Israel are reportedly preparing a major bombing campaign against Iranian energy sites that could begin as early as this weekend <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643737-us-israel-strikes-iran/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> The US and Israel are preparing a major bombing campaign against Iranian energy infrastructure that could begin as early as this weekend, according to multiple media reports. The proposed operation would target power plants, oil refineries, and other energy-related facilities in what CBS News described as potentially one of the harshest bombing campaigns against Iran to date. American and Israeli forces are reportedly coordinating their preparations, although the precise scope and duration of the operation have not been finalized. CBS and Axios reported that US President Donald Trump is seriously considering the strikes but has not yet issued final authorization. The Wall Street Journal, citing separate US officials, subsequently claimed that Trump has already ordered a new attack that could begin over the weekend and last several days. US officials have reportedly discussed completing the strikes before financial markets open on Monday because of concerns that attacks on Iranian energy facilities could disrupt oil prices and damage the US and global economies. The strike plan was reportedly discussed during Trump’s cabinet meeting at Camp David on Friday. Some White House aides focused on domestic politics strongly opposed the escalation, CBS reported, although the president publicly indicated that heavier attacks are approaching. “We’ll be hitting them very hard,”Trump told reporters.“At some point, they’re going to say, ‘We just can’t take it anymore.’” Military","Fri, 31 Jul 2026 22:34:51 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643737-us-israel-strikes-iran/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-04 01:20:07
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,US loses F-35B stealth jet in unexplained ‘mishap’ (VIDEOS),US loses F-35B stealth jet in unexplained ‘mishap’ (VIDEOS),"US loses F-35B stealth jet in unexplained ‘mishap’ (VIDEOS) <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.07/thumbnail/6a6d1a9785f5404fd6471e19.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> A US Marine Corps F-35B stealth fighter crashed and caught fire at Marine Corps Air Station Miramar in San Diego, California, on Friday <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643736-f35-jet-crash-california/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> A US Marine Corps F-35B stealth fighter crashed and caught fire at Marine Corps Air Station Miramar in San Diego, California, on Friday, apparently resulting in the total loss of the $109 million aircraft, according to footage from the scene. Emergency crews responded at around 10 AM local time to what the military described as a“Class A mishap,”its category for the most serious accidents. The aircraft was assigned to Marine Aircraft Group 11 of the 3rd Marine Aircraft Wing. “The pilot ejected, was transported to a local medical facility in stable condition for evaluation and treatment of non-life-threatening injuries,”the Marine Corps said in a follow-up statement, adding that the crash occurred on the base’s flightline. JUST IN: An F-35 caught fire after a mishap at Marine Corps Air Station Miramar in San Diego on Friday morning. Emergency crews responded to heavy smoke around 10 a.m. Cause under investigation.- FOX 5pic.twitter.com/oDthXqbQRf Footage from the scene showed a thick column of black smoke rising above the base. Aerial video showed the burned-out jet lying in a scorched dirt field near the runway as military personnel and firefighters surrounded the wreckage. Exclusive video sent by our follower.Initial reports indicate that a U.S. Marine Corps F-35B Lightning II has crashed at Marine Corps Air Station Miramar, home of the 3rd Marine Aircraft Wing, in San Diego, California.pic.twitter.com/qze3GLm8Og The crash also sparked a vegetation fire, prompting a response","Fri, 31 Jul 2026 21:59:25 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643736-f35-jet-crash-california/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-04 01:20:08
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Even mild winter could turn into nightmare for Ukraine — expert,Even mild winter could turn into nightmare for Ukraine — expert,"Even mild winter could turn into nightmare for Ukraine — expert Vasily Koltashov, director of the Institute of New Society, said that a mild winter with fluctuating temperatures would damage water supply systems MOSCOW, August 4. /TASS/. Even a moderately cold winter risks turning into a logistical nightmare for Ukraine, significantly straining its rear, economist Vasily Koltashov, director of the Institute of New Society, wrote in a column for TASS. ""Higher-than-average precipitation is forecast for the autumn and winter. Damaged roads, a shortage of filling stations, frequent railway breakdowns, and accidents at depots could turn even a moderately cold winter into a logistical nightmare,"" he said. A mild winter with fluctuating temperatures will also damage water supply systems, the expert added. ""Preliminary forecasts indicate that the coming winter will feature brief cold spells alternating with prolonged thaws, rain, and wet snow. Given the specific climatic conditions, even a relatively mild but damp winter characterized by constant temperature swings will inflict maximum damage on aging Soviet-era water supply and sanitation systems, which simply cannot withstand the repeated freezing and thawing of the soil,"" he said. Koltashov identified energy generation and fuel infrastructure as Ukraine’s Achilles' heel, noting that over 200 gas stations were destroyed in the country between May and July. The expert predicts that by winter, gas stations in the country’s left-bank region could virtually disappear. ""The situation with electricity is even worse. Almost all thermal power plant capacity has been lost, and nuclear power generation could be drastically reduced due to the disabli","Tue, 04 Aug 2026 04:06:38 +0300",https://tass.com/economy/2168619,2026-08-04 01:20:11
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,"Death toll from Venezuela earthquake rises to 6,125","Death toll from Venezuela earthquake rises to 6,125","Death toll from Venezuela earthquake rises to 6,125 According to a weekly state bulletin, 6,462 people were rescued during search-and-rescue operations CARACAS, August 4. /TASS/. The death toll from the devastating earthquake in Venezuela has risen to 6,125, according to a weekly bulletin published on the Telegram channel of President of the country's National Assembly Jorge Rodriguez. According to the weekly update, 6,462 people were rescued during search-and-rescue operations, 60,992 people received medical treatment, 287 housing units were provided to those left homeless, and 43,679 structures were inspected and assessed, of which 41,624 had sustained damage. The earthquake struck Venezuela on the evening of June 24. Two powerful tremors of magnitude 7.2 and 7.5 occurred about 40 seconds apart. Their epicenters were located about 10 km apart in Yaracuy state. The earthquake was followed by over 1,500 aftershocks.","Tue, 04 Aug 2026 03:47:21 +0300",https://tass.com/emergencies/2168617,2026-08-04 01:20:12
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Russia has not conveyed signals to West on Ukraine via Kazakhstan — MFA,Russia has not conveyed signals to West on Ukraine via Kazakhstan — MFA,"Russia has not conveyed signals to West on Ukraine via Kazakhstan — MFA Mikhail Galuzin added that Moscow maintains direct contact with those capable of influencing Kiev ST. PETERSBURG, August 4. /TASS/. The Russian side has not conveyed any signals to the collective West regarding a settlement in Ukraine via Kazakhstan, Russian Deputy Foreign Minister Mikhail Galuzin told TASS, adding that Moscow maintains direct contact with those capable of influencing the Kiev regime and sees no need to trouble its Kazakhstani friends with this matter. Kazakhstan's President Kassym-Jomart Tokayev said at a meeting with his Russian counterpart Vladimir Putin on July 25 that he was receiving numerous signals from Europe and the United States regarding the current state of affairs surrounding the conflict in Ukraine. The Russian leader then briefed his Kazakh counterpart in detail on the current situation regarding Ukraine. Moscow ""sees no need to trouble its Kazakhstani friends regarding this matter"" or ask them to convey anything to the collective West, Galuzin said on the sidelines of the third Kazakhstan-Russia Media Forum. ""We maintain contact and communication directly with those capable of influencing the Kiev regime,"" he said. ""I cannot say that these forces are listening to us closely, but we are continuing our efforts in this direction,"" the diplomat stressed. The first Media Forum between Russia and Kazakhstan was held at the TASS headquarters in Moscow in November 2024, marking the agency’s 120th anniversary. The second meeting in this format took place last year in Almaty.","Tue, 04 Aug 2026 03:28:21 +0300",https://tass.com/politics/2168615,2026-08-04 01:20:13
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,"US has shifted tactics in war with Iran, betting on internal destabilization — expert","US has shifted tactics in war with Iran, betting on internal destabilization — expert","US has shifted tactics in war with Iran, betting on internal destabilization — expert Oleg Akulinichev, deputy chairman of the Russian-Iranian Business Council, noted that the strategic goals of the US and Israel remain unchanged TEHRAN, August 4. /TASS/. The conflict between the US and Iran has taken on a new, more complicated form, with Washington making the internal destabilization of the Islamic Republic its primary objective, Oleg Akulinichev, deputy chairman of the Russian-Iranian Business Council at the Russian Chamber of Commerce and Industry, scholar and diplomat, said in an interview with TASS. ""The failure of the military strategy does not mean that Iran’s adversaries have abandoned their intentions. The conflict, like all such wars, is multifaceted. Hybrid warfare tools are now coming to the fore, with their goal being not so much the military defeat of Iran as its internal destabilization,"" he said, adding that ""the situation resembles a chess match,"" with each side currently seeking new, creative, and unconventional ways to exert pressure on the other. The war has not ended, it has simply shifted to a new phase of fierce military, diplomatic, and informational maneuvering, with each side attempting to impose its own version of how the conflict should unfold, the expert said. ""Underlying this diplomatic game is a fundamental reality: while the strategic goals of the US and Israel may not have been achieved during the period of active hostilities, they remain unchanged,"" he stressed. That said, both sides have gone too far to simply back down, yet are too exhausted to continue a full-scale war, Akulinichev added. Earlier, US President Donald Trump announced that the United States and Iran ","Tue, 04 Aug 2026 03:13:36 +0300",https://tass.com/politics/2168613,2026-08-04 01:20:14
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,New Pentagon contracts won’t help Ukraine with Patriots — expert,New Pentagon contracts won’t help Ukraine with Patriots — expert,"New Pentagon contracts won’t help Ukraine with Patriots — expert Nikolay Novik, an expert at the Higher School of Economics, says that the actual increase in output will occur in 2027-2028, not in the coming months MOSCOW, August 4. /TASS/. Kiev should not count on the US expanding production of the Patriot and THAAD interceptor missiles, Nikolay Novik, an expert at the Institute for Global Military Economics and Strategy at the National Research University Higher School of Economics, told TASS, adding that agreements concluded by the Pentagon will not lead to increased deliveries to Ukraine in the coming months, which is why the Prioritised Ukraine Requirements List (PURL) program remains the primary mechanism for Kiev to obtain them. The Pentagon previously announced the signing of framework agreements with Northrop Grumman totaling $3 bln. The execution of these contracts will eventually allow for an around threefold increase in the production volume of the PAC-3 missiles for the Patriot systems and a fourfold rise for THAAD system components. ""The seven-year timeframe of new contracts means that the actual increase in output will occur in 2027-2028, not in the coming months. Therefore, the PURL mechanism, which handles approximately 95% of the supplied missiles, remains the only effective channel for Ukraine. Over the year the program has been in operation, 29 countries have contributed $6.7 bln to it,"" the expert said. For Ukraine, the impact of the concluded agreements is indirectly rather than directly positive, he noted. US President Donald Trump promised Vladimir Zelensky a license to manufacture Patriot interceptors back in July but effectively abandoned the idea on July 31, s","Tue, 04 Aug 2026 02:55:12 +0300",https://tass.com/politics/2168611,2026-08-04 01:20:15
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Ukraine’s energy sector faces 650 mln euros shortfall ahead of difficult winter — PM,Ukraine’s energy sector faces 650 mln euros shortfall ahead of difficult winter — PM,"Ukraine’s energy sector faces 650 mln euros shortfall ahead of difficult winter — PM Sergey Koretsky also said that the Ukraine Energy Support Fund has raised over 2 bln euros, which is insufficient MOSCOW, August 4. /TASS/. Ukraine’s energy sector faces a funding shortfall of around 650 mln euros ahead of a difficult winter, said the country’s Prime Minister Sergey Koretsky. According to Ukraine’s Channel 24, the premier stated at a meeting with ambassadors in Kiev on Monday that the unmet funding requirement of the Ukrainian energy sector ahead of the heating season stands at about 650 mln euros. While the Ukraine Energy Support Fund has already raised over 2 bln euros, this amount is insufficient, he noted. ""The pace of aid mobilization must not be allowed to slow down. Objectively, this winter is going to be difficult,"" Koretsky stressed. He also believes that some CIS countries could assist Ukraine with railcars and locomotives, given the damage to its railway infrastructure.","Tue, 04 Aug 2026 02:14:37 +0300",https://tass.com/world/2168609,2026-08-04 01:20:16
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Amur tiger cubs transferred by Russia to Kazakhstan could be released into wild in year,Amur tiger cubs transferred by Russia to Kazakhstan could be released into wild in year,"Amur tiger cubs transferred by Russia to Kazakhstan could be released into wild in year The cubs need to reach the age of 18 months, Kazakhstan’s Ministry of Ecology says ASTANA, August 4. /TASS/. Amur tiger cubs transferred by Russia to Kazakhstan will remain in captivity for about another year, until they reach the age of 18 months, Kazakhstan’s Ministry of Ecology announced. The tiger cubs arrived in the republic in May at the age of 6-7 months, the ministry said, adding that they continue to grow and develop in specially equipped enclosures at the Ile-Balkhash State Nature Reserve in southern Kazakhstan. ""They will remain under the supervision of specialists until they reach the age of 18 months,"" the ministry stated. Specialists will decide whether each tiger cub can be released into the wild following veterinary examinations and behavioral tests. Moreover, a male tiger remains under constant observation. ""A decision regarding his release into the wild will be made once all tests are complete and his readiness for independent life has been confirmed,"" the ministry noted. In May, four Amur tigers were transported from Khabarovsk to the Ile-Balkhash Nature Reserve. They are the closest relatives of Caspian tigers, which used to inhabit Central Asia. In Kazakhstan, they went extinct by 1948. The country expects that the special program will help revive their population.","Tue, 04 Aug 2026 01:19:13 +0300",https://tass.com/society/2168605,2026-08-04 01:20:17
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Russia ready for negotiations on Ukraine with mature approach from West — MFA,Russia ready for negotiations on Ukraine with mature approach from West — MFA,"Russia ready for negotiations on Ukraine with mature approach from West — MFA Mikhail Galuzin added that Moscow has ""repeatedly demonstrated this"" ST. PETERSBURG, August 4. /TASS/. Moscow is open to negotiations on Ukraine provided there is a constructive and mature approach from Western countries, Russian Deputy Foreign Minister Mikhail Galuzin told TASS. ""We are always ready for negotiations and open to a negotiated solution, we have repeatedly demonstrated this. It was the other side, the Ukrainian side, that withdrew from the talks, it would pull out, then forbid itself from engaging in them, behaving, to put it very mildly, inconsistently,"" he said on the sidelines of the third Kazakhstan-Russia Media Forum. If in the West, ""within the camp of Ukraine’s sponsors, there has matured an understanding of the need for an honest, constructive dialogue aimed at addressing the well-known root causes of the conflict, then perhaps prospects for such a dialogue will emerge,"" the official noted. ""But if not, if there is no such readiness on the other side, and there is no willingness to ensure that the Kiev regime abides by the agreements reached between its Western sponsors and us, then we will continue the special military operation, seek to eliminate the root causes of the conflict, and defend our interests through military means, acting in a targeted and effective manner to minimize destruction and protect our people on both sides of the line of contact,"" Galuzin added. The first Media Forum between Russia and Kazakhstan was held at the TASS headquarters in Moscow in November 2024, marking the agency’s 120th anniversary. T","Tue, 04 Aug 2026 00:20:02 +0300",https://tass.com/politics/2168603,2026-08-04 01:20:17
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,"Qatar, Egypt, Turkey condemn Israel’s ceasefire violations in Gaza","Qatar, Egypt, Turkey condemn Israel’s ceasefire violations in Gaza","Qatar, Egypt, Turkey condemn Israel’s ceasefire violations in Gaza The mediators particularly condemned the targeting of healthcare facilities and medical infrastructure, and the resulting civilian casualties DOHA, August 3. /TASS/. Qatar, Egypt, and Turkey, which are acting as mediators in an effort to settle the conflict in the Gaza Strip, have strongly condemned Israel’s actions in the enclave as a flagrant violation of the ceasefire agreement, according to their joint statement released by the Qatari Foreign Ministry. ""The State of Qatar, the Arab Republic of Egypt, and the Republic of Turkey, in their capacity as the mediating countries, express their strong condemnation and denunciation of the ongoing Israeli violations in the Gaza Strip, particularly the targeting of healthcare facilities and medical infrastructure, and the resulting civilian casualties, including women and children, which constitute a flagrant violation of international law and international humanitarian law,"" the statement reads. ""The mediators stress the need for Israel to comply with all of its obligations under international law and to fully uphold its commitments under the ceasefire agreement, affirming that the continuation of these violations constitutes a breach of the agreement and undermines the efforts aimed at implementing its second phase, particularly following Hamas and the Palestinian factions’ announcement of their acceptance of the roadmap, especially the provision concerning the confinement of weapons. They further warn that these violations threaten the path toward de-escalation and exacerbate the suffering of civilians in the Gaza Strip,"" it says. The mediators called on the internatio","Tue, 04 Aug 2026 00:03:47 +0300",https://tass.com/world/2168599,2026-08-04 01:20:19
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,"Ukrainian drone kills one, wounds two people in car near Belgorod","Ukrainian drone kills one, wounds two people in car near Belgorod","Ukrainian drone kills one, wounds two people in car near Belgorod The incident ocurred in the settlement of Oktyabrsky BELGOROD, August 3. /TASS/. A Ukrainian drone has hit a car in the Belgorod Region, killing one person and wounding two others, the regional emergency center said on the Max messenger. ""In the settlement of Oktyabrsky, an FPV drone struck a car. The woman who was in the vehicle died from her injuries on the spot. The ambulance crew is transporting the man and woman with multiple shrapnel wounds to the regional clinical hospital. Doctors assess the man’s condition as serious,"" it said.","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 23:34:24 +0300",https://tass.com/politics/2168593,2026-08-04 01:20:20
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,"Turkish intel chief, Hamas leader discuss roadmap for second stage of Gaza peace plan","Turkish intel chief, Hamas leader discuss roadmap for second stage of Gaza peace plan","Turkish intel chief, Hamas leader discuss roadmap for second stage of Gaza peace plan The sides also discussed the humanitarian situation in the Gaza Strip ISTANBUL, August 3. /TASS/. Turkish National Intelligence Organization Director Ibrahim Kalin met with the new head of the radical movement Hamas’s Politburo, Khalil al-Hayya, in Ankara to discuss a roadmap for transiting to the second stage of US President Donald Trump’s peace plan for Gaza, theAnadolunews agency reported. The two also discussed the humanitarian situation in the Gaza Strip. The Turkish intelligence chief expressed support for Palestine and called for international efforts to put an end to the Israeli aggression in the Palestinian enclave. In addition, they discussed Turkey, Qatar, and Egypt’s joint efforts toward ensuring peace in Gaza. Last week, the Hamas delegation met with Turkish Foreign Minister Hakan Fidan in Ankara.","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 23:28:47 +0300",https://tass.com/world/2168591,2026-08-04 01:20:21
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Negotiations are Iran’s chance to avoid ‘decapitation’ — Trump,Negotiations are Iran’s chance to avoid ‘decapitation’ — Trump,"Negotiations are Iran’s chance to avoid ‘decapitation’ — Trump According to the US president, Washington could increase the scale of attacks WASHINGTON, August 3. /TASS/. US President Donald Trump said that negotiations with the United States are the last opportunity for Iran to avoid a blow to the leadership of the Islamic Republic. ""I think we're going to maybe get something, but I want to give them every last chance before decapitation. It's very tough to do what we have planned, still plan. We'll see what happens,"" he told reporters. ""This is a big move to do an attack that big on a country I'd rather not do. Now we've already threw lots of large attacks, but they were normal large. Hopefully they'll come to their senses.""","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 23:24:01 +0300",https://tass.com/world/2168589,2026-08-04 01:20:22
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Nadezhda crew evacuate to Novorossiysk after Ukraine’s drone attack,Nadezhda crew evacuate to Novorossiysk after Ukraine’s drone attack,"Nadezhda crew evacuate to Novorossiysk after Ukraine’s drone attack There were 22 crew members on board ISTANBUL, August 3. /TASS/. The crew of the Nadezhda vessel that was attacked by Ukrainian drones near Novorossiysk has been evacuated to the Russian port, Turkey’s Transport Ministry said. ""On August 3, 2025, the Ro-Ro-type vessel Nadezhda that was on its way from the port of Novorossiysk to Samsun was reportedly attacked by drones some 20 nautical miles off Novorossiysk’s coast. There were 22 crew members, including 13 Turkish nationals, onboard. Initial reports indicate damage to the ship’s living premises and bow. The fire has not yet been put out,"" it said. ""The crew members have been safely evacuated to the port of Novorossiysk by the Russian naval forces. Initial reports indicate that three crew members may be in critical condition. The fire onboard continues, and the rescue operation is impossible due to ongoing risks of drone attacks in this area,"" the ministry added. The Cumhuriyet newspaper reported earlier, citing the ship’s captain, that it was attacked by six to seven Ukrainian drones. The 118-meter vessel for the transportation of rolling cargoes Nadezhda (IMO number: 7702657) was built in 1978 in Denmark. According to publicly available data, it is owned by Nadezhda Roro Inc. Its operational and technical manager is Turkish company Kalyoncu Ro Ro Denizcilik.","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 23:15:35 +0300",https://tass.com/emergencies/2168585,2026-08-04 01:20:24
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Iran drops plans to strike Ukraine after its apology for attack on ship — TV,Iran drops plans to strike Ukraine after its apology for attack on ship — TV,"Iran drops plans to strike Ukraine after its apology for attack on ship — TV According to Press TV, Mohsen Rezaee, a military adviser to the Iranian supreme leader, earlier reported plans to attack three facilities on Ukrainian territory MOSCOW, August 3. /TASS/. Tehran has abandoned plans to attack three facilities on Ukrainian territory in response to a strike on an Iranian vessel in the Caspian Sea after Kiev issued an apology, said Mohsen Rezaee, a military adviser to the Iranian supreme leader, as reported by thePress TVchannel. He said that Ukraine must be held accountable for its actions, theFarsagency writes. Earlier, Iranian Foreign Ministry Spokesman Esmaeil Baghaei stated that Tehran has evidence that the Ukrainian armed forces’ strike on the Iranian vessel was deliberate, despite Kiev’s assurances to the contrary.","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 23:04:59 +0300",https://tass.com/world/2168583,2026-08-04 01:20:24
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Trump says won't let Iran charge toll for Hormuz passage,Trump says won't let Iran charge toll for Hormuz passage,"Trump says won't let Iran charge toll for Hormuz passage USA will charge that, President Donald Trump said WASHINGTON, August 3. /TASS/. Washington will not allow Iran to charge a toll for ships passing through the Strait of Hormuz, President Donald Trump said. ""I'm not going to let them charge. Anybody's going to charge, we will charge. We're the ones that has total control,"" Trump told reporters. ""No, there's not going to be charging. We're not talking about charging at all. There won't be charging."".","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 22:43:14 +0300",https://tass.com/world/2168579,2026-08-04 01:20:26
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Russian divers win silver at 2026 European Aquatics Championships,Russian divers win silver at 2026 European Aquatics Championships,"Russian divers win silver at 2026 European Aquatics Championships Russia’s silver medalists are Evgenii Kuznetsov and Nikita Shleikher, with their eventual result of 408.99 points PARIS, August 3. /TASS/. Russian divers won silver on Monday at the 2026 European Aquatics Championships in Paris in the Men's Synchronised 3m Springboard event. Russia’s silver medalists are Evgenii Kuznetsov and Nikita Shleikher, with their eventual result of 408.99 points. German divers clinched the gold with 423.84 points and Italians packed the bronze with 3686.07 points. The 2026 European Aquatics Championships are scheduled to be hosted by the French capital of Paris between July 31 and August 16 at the 5,000-seat capacity Paris Aquatic Center. Russia is competing at the European Championships for the first time since 2021.","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 22:42:42 +0300",https://tass.com/sports/2168581,2026-08-04 01:20:27
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,"US and Iran discuss resumption of shipping in Strait of Hormuz by August 4, Trump says","US and Iran discuss resumption of shipping in Strait of Hormuz by August 4, Trump says","US and Iran discuss resumption of shipping in Strait of Hormuz by August 4, Trump says The US president mentioned complete opening of the strait WASHINGTON, August 3. /TASS/. US President Donald Trump said that the United States and Iran are discussing the resumption of normal shipping in the Strait of Hormuz by Tuesday. ""We're talking about the strait, the opening of the strait, having it open literally by tomorrow, completely open, and that's phase on,"" he told reporters.","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 22:02:13 +0300",https://tass.com/world/2168575,2026-08-04 01:20:27
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Zelensky dismisses Ukrainian ambassador to US,Zelensky dismisses Ukrainian ambassador to US,"Zelensky dismisses Ukrainian ambassador to US A new ambassador has not yet been appointed MOSCOW, August 3. /TASS/. Vladimir Zelensky has dismissed Ukraine’s Ambassador to the United States Olga Stefanishina. ""To dismiss Stefanishina Olga Vitalyevna from her position as Ambassador Extraordinary and Plenipotentiary of Ukraine to the United States of America,"" Zelensky’s decree reads. Stefanishina served as Ukrainian ambassador to the United States since August 27, 2025. A new ambassador has not yet been appointed. Shortly after Zelensky’s decree was posted on his website, Stefanishina said the decision was her own. ""Today, I decided to step down as Ukraine’s ambassador to the United States. This is my own decision stemming from personal circumstances that were mentioned earlier,"" she wrote on Facebook (Facebook is banned in Russia due to its ownership by Meta, which has been designated as extremist). She posted a photo of her letter of resignation where she also cited ""personal circumstances"" as the reason for her leaving the post. At the same time, she promised to provide comments on the probe against her in the near future. ""As for the issues going around about me in the mass media, I will comment on them specially and publicly soon,"" she added. Reports on Stefanishina’s voluntary resignation appeared in Ukrainian media back on July 13. According to Verkhovna Rada (Ukrainian parliament) member Alexey Goncharenko (designated as a terrorist and extremist in Russia), Stefanishina has already returned to Kiev and may be charged by Ukraine’s National Anti-Corruption B","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 21:51:18 +0300",https://tass.com/world/2168571,2026-08-04 01:20:29
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Ukrainian drones injure four people on Turkish vessel heading to Russia — paper,Ukrainian drones injure four people on Turkish vessel heading to Russia — paper,"Ukrainian drones injure four people on Turkish vessel heading to Russia — paper The boat was carrying fresh vegetables and fruits ISTANBUL, August 3. /TASS/. A Ukrainian drone has injured four sailors, including three Turks, on vessel Nadezhda, flying a Cameroonian flag, theCumhuriyetnewspaper reported. The boat was carrying fresh vegetables and fruits from the Turkish port of Samsun to Novorossiysk. The story said that six to seven Ukrainian drones attacked the ship at around 4:30 p.m. local time (1:30 p.m. GMT) about 30 miles off Novorossiysk triggering a fire. The 118-meter vessel for the transportation of rolling cargoes Nadezhda (IMO number: 7702657) was built in 1978 in Denmark. According to publicly available data, it is owned by Nadezhda Roro Inc. Its operational and technical manager is Turkish company Kalyoncu Ro Ro Denizcilik.","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 21:49:54 +0300",https://tass.com/emergencies/2168569,2026-08-04 01:20:30
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,NATO command responsible for coordinating arms supplies to Kiev remains in US hands,NATO command responsible for coordinating arms supplies to Kiev remains in US hands,"NATO command responsible for coordinating arms supplies to Kiev remains in US hands The process of transferring command positions in Europe to European generals did not affect this command structure of the alliance BRUSSELS, August 3. /TASS/. The NATO command in Wiesbaden for coordinating military supplies to Ukraine (NSATU) is now headed by US Army Lieutenant General Guillaume Beaurpere, who has taken the reins from Lieutenant General Curtis Bazzard, said chair of the NATO Military Committee, Admiral Giuseppe Cavo Dragone. Thus, the process of transferring command positions in Europe to European generals, which the United States and NATO said would be launched this year, did not affect this command structure of the alliance. ""Today, at Clay Kaserne in Wiesbaden NATO Security Assistance and Training for Ukraine changes command,"" he wrote on X. ""To Lieutenant General Guillaume Beaurpere: welcome! You take charge of a mission that matters."" Cavo Dragone noted the particular importance of NSATU for NATO. ""We imagined the wars of this century as bits and bytes. What we are watching is different: masses and machines together - soldiers, artillery, logistics under fire, married to cheap, fast, tactically decisive solutions and uncrewed systems, and applied AI iterating in weeks, not procurement cycles. NSATU sits where that knowledge is generated, and it feeds both our strategic commands,"" he said. NSATU began to be hastily created virtually immediately after Donald Trump’s victory in the US elections to ensure coordination of military supplies to the Kiev regime in case Trump cuts aid to Kiev.","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 21:18:43 +0300",https://tass.com/world/2168565,2026-08-04 01:20:30
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Russia driving Ukraine from its positions in Veliky Burluk direction — administration head,Russia driving Ukraine from its positions in Veliky Burluk direction — administration head,"Russia driving Ukraine from its positions in Veliky Burluk direction — administration head According to preliminary information, the Kiev regime will tighten mobilization in Kharkov and the Kharkov Region to replenish the shortage of personnel in the armed formations, Vitaly Ganchev said MOSCOW, August 3. /TASS/. Russian troops are systematically driving the Armed Forces of Ukraine from their positions in the Veliky Burluk direction, dealing the Ukrainian army losses there, the head of the Kharkov military-civilian administration Vitaly Ganchev stated at a briefing, commenting on the liberation of Bely Kolodez. On August 3, the Russian Defense Ministry reported that the country's Battlegroup North had taken control of the settlement of Bely Kolodez in the Kharkov Region. ""The Russian army is systematically driving the enemy from our territory and advancing in the Veliky Burluk direction. According to preliminary information, the Kiev regime will tighten mobilization in Kharkov and the Kharkov Region to replenish the shortage of personnel in the armed formations operating on the Kharkov direction,"" Ganchev said.","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 21:08:33 +0300",https://tass.com/politics/2168563,2026-08-04 01:20:31
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Russian diplomat points to Ukraine’s attacks on Zaporozhye NPP,Russian diplomat points to Ukraine’s attacks on Zaporozhye NPP,"Russian diplomat points to Ukraine’s attacks on Zaporozhye NPP The Russian charge d'affaires outlined Moscow’s official position on Ukraine’s attacks against civilian facilities and infrastructure in Russia STOCKHOLM, August 3. /TASS/. Russia’s charge d’affaires, who was summoned to the Swedish Foreign Ministry on Monday, outlined Russia’s official position regarding Ukraine’s attacks on civilian targets on Russian territory, placing particular emphasis on the Kiev regime’s continued attacks on the Zaporozhye Nuclear Power Plant, the Russian embassy told TASS. ""On August 3, 2026, Russia’s charge d’affaires in Sweden was summoned to the Swedish Foreign Ministry, where the Swedish side lodged a protest over Russia’s strikes on Ukrainian territory. For his part, the Russian charge d'affaires outlined Russia’s official position on Ukraine’s attacks against civilian facilities and infrastructure in Russia. Special attention was drawn to the Kiev regime’s continuing attacks on the Zaporozhye NPP. It was stressed that such reckless actions are fraught with serious risks,"" it said.","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 20:59:04 +0300",https://tass.com/politics/2168559,2026-08-04 01:20:32
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Six people injured by mines remotely planted by Ukraine in Energodar over day,Six people injured by mines remotely planted by Ukraine in Energodar over day,"Six people injured by mines remotely planted by Ukraine in Energodar over day Mayor Maxim Pukhov said that medical workers are providing all necessary assistance to the victims MELITOPOL, August 3. /TASS/. Six civilians of Energodar were injured over the course of a day as a result of mine explosions involving mines remotely planted by the Armed Forces of Ukraine, the city's mayor, Maxim Pukhov, reported on his Max channel. ""According to updated data, six civilians were injured today as a result of mine explosions. All of them have been taken to the emergency department of Medical Unit No. 145 in Energodar, and all of them are civilians who were following their usual routes as they became victims of remote mining carried out by the Kiev regime,"" he wrote. He added that doctors are doing everything possible to nurse them back to health. This is not the first such incident. ""Medical workers are providing all necessary assistance to the victims: some patients have been hospitalized, while others are receiving outpatient treatment. In addition, yesterday, city residents who had been injured in similar explosions involving unidentified explosive devices also sought treatment at the emergency department,"" Pukhov wrote.","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 20:28:25 +0300",https://tass.com/emergencies/2168555,2026-08-04 01:20:33
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Trump claims US fully controls Strait of Hormuz,Trump claims US fully controls Strait of Hormuz,"Trump claims US fully controls Strait of Hormuz The US president said that nothing gets through to Iran, unless the United States wants it to WASHINGTON, August 3. /TASS/. US President Donald Trump has claimed that the United States fully controls the Strait of Hormuz and will also keep a naval blockade of Iran until a deal is signed or Tehran surrenders. He said on Truth Social that the strait, despite Iran's statements, ""is already completely controlled by the United States Navy."" Speaking about the naval blockade of the Islamic Republic, Trump said: ""Nothing gets through to Iran, unless we want it to, and nothing will get through, unless a Deal, or Total Surrender, is accomplished."" Earlier, Trump said that the United States and Iran would begin negotiations on a peace deal on August 3. He also said he had agreed to cancel a planned large·scale strike against the country to reach an agreement with Tehran. According to the US president, Iran and some Middle Eastern states asked Washington to refrain from the attack, as the parties had already outlined the contours of a future agreement. Trump said that it should include the immediate opening of the Strait of Hormuz and the elimination of the Iranian nuclear threat.","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 19:39:01 +0300",https://tass.com/world/2168553,2026-08-04 01:20:33
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,"IN BRIEF: Seven people killed in drone attack on Gelendzhik, three children among them","IN BRIEF: Seven people killed in drone attack on Gelendzhik, three children among them","IN BRIEF: Seven people killed in drone attack on Gelendzhik, three children among them The regional emergency center said 40 people were injured KRASNODAR, August 3. /TASS/. According to the latest reports, seven people, including three children, were killed when a drone crashed in Gelendzhik. TASS has compiled the key facts about the incident. - According to Krasnodar Region Governor Veniamin Kondratyev, the drone crashed in the village of Arkhipo-Osipovka near Gelendzhik. - According to him, the attack was aimed at civilian infrastructure. - Emergency and special services are working at the crash sites. - According to the latest data, seven people were killed, including three children. - The regional emergency center said 40 people were injured. - According to Alexey Kuznetsov, an aide to the health minister, 21 people were hospitalized. - He said that nine people, including three children, were in serious condition. - According to Kuznetsov, all the injured people are receiving full medical care. He said that 19 people received outpatient care. - Telemedicine consultations with specialists from federal medical centers were organized. - Kondratyev said that he had instructed Gelendzhik head Alexey Bogodistov to provide all necessary support to the victims and their families. - He described the incident as a cynical and inhumane terrorist attack. - The Prosecutor's Office of Gelendzhik is monitoring the rights of citizens in connection with the drone attack. - Cooperation with all relevant agencies was established to provide prompt assistance to the residents. - A hotline was set up. - An emergency center was set up ","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 19:28:50 +0300",https://tass.com/emergencies/2168551,2026-08-04 01:20:35
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,No NATO-Kiev agreement on production of Patriot systems by winter — US envoy to NATO,No NATO-Kiev agreement on production of Patriot systems by winter — US envoy to NATO,"No NATO-Kiev agreement on production of Patriot systems by winter — US envoy to NATO Matthew Whitaker said that Washington is ""going to do first things first"" NEW YORK, August 3. /TASS/. A long-term agreement on joint production of Patriot systems with Ukraine will not be implemented by the coming winter, US Permanent Representative to NATO Matthew Whitaker said in an interview with Fox Business. ""Obviously, the most important thing right now is that the air defense that Ukraine needs to survive another winter is moved as quickly as possible. Whether that's from our allies who have extra missiles, or whether that's producing more in our own factories, and a long-term production deal is not going to be [made] by this winter, we're going to keep working on it. But we're going to do first things first,"" Whitaker said. US President Donald Trump said on July 31 that the United States should be very careful with granting licenses to other countries to manufacture its weapons. He said that Washington had not agreed to supply Kiev with either Patriot system technology or Tomahawk cruise missiles, and questioned this possibility.","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 19:26:53 +0300",https://tass.com/world/2168549,2026-08-04 01:20:36
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Zelensky seeks to drag Muslim world into conflict in Ukraine through Umerov’s appointment,Zelensky seeks to drag Muslim world into conflict in Ukraine through Umerov’s appointment,"Zelensky seeks to drag Muslim world into conflict in Ukraine through Umerov’s appointment Russian lawmaker Leonid Ivlev recalled that Rustem Umerov is a Crimean Tatar and Kiev has been unsuccessfully seeking to use them for its purposes for decades SIMFEROPOL, August 3. /TASS/. By appointing Rustem Umerov Ukraine’s foreign intelligence chief, Vladimir Zelensky obviously seeks to drag Islamic countries into the Ukrainian crisis, a Russian lawmaker told TASS. Earlier, Zelensky signed a decree appointing former National Security and Defense Secretary Rustem Umerov as the head of Ukraine’s Foreign Intelligence Service. According to Zelensky, Umerov will simultaneously address issues of diplomacy, defense, negotiations with the United States and other partners, as well as talks on ending the war. ""Umerov’s appointment as head of Ukraine’s foreign intelligence service, as he (Zelensky - TASS) sees it, could boost the Muslim world’s support for the Kiev regime. Following the scandal involving Zelensky and [Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin] Netanyahu in the struggle for US assistance, this is yet another desperate attempt in the Kiev regime’s policy,"" said Leonid Ivlev, a member of the Russian State Duma, or lower house of parliament. He recalled that Umerov is a Crimean Tatar and Kiev has been unsuccessfully seeking to use them for its purposes for decades. According to Ivlev, in his new capacity, Umerov will have all the capacities to act widely beyond Ukraine, including to influence Muslim countries and organizations. He warned, however, that Ukraine’s attempt to stake on the Muslim world will be an absolute failure. ""It is already evident for all, both for the military and politicians in various countries, that Ukraine is ce","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 19:25:13 +0300",https://tass.com/politics/2168547,2026-08-04 01:20:37
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Russian-Kazakh Media Forum discusses role of media in building trust between nations,Russian-Kazakh Media Forum discusses role of media in building trust between nations,"Russian-Kazakh Media Forum discusses role of media in building trust between nations Its plenary session focused on the strategic role of the mass media in countering disinformation and consolidating bilateral ties ST. PETERSBURG, August 3. /TASS/. Building trust between the peoples of Russia and Kazakhstan and the role of journalists in this process were the key topics of the 3rd Russian-Kazakh Media Forum. Its plenary session focused on the strategic role of the mass media in countering disinformation and consolidating bilateral ties. ""One cannot but see that amid an extremely complex and dangerous international situation our professional journalistic community plays a very important role in building trust between countries and peoples,"" TASS Director General Andrey Kondrashov said. Alexander Smirnov, head of the Russian presidential public relations directorate, stressed the strategic importance of close cooperation between the two countries’ media structures, describing it as a ""direct reflection of the high level of the Russian-Kazakh allied relations."" ""The global situation is getting tenser and tenser year after year, and the global system of international relations is living through a profound transformation. Today, as never befor, reliable information and cultural ties between Russia and Kazakhstan have a special strategic value,"" he noted. According to Smirnov, Russian and Kazakh media are combating the West’s attempts to sow mistrust among them, as well as to propagate narratives distorting their shared history. ""Today, we are witnessing an escalation in the intensity of information wars, which are being waged against our countries. External forces are resorting to the massiv","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 19:20:38 +0300",https://tass.com/society/2168543,2026-08-04 01:20:38
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,"Trump says US and Iran in talks, even if Tehran denies it","Trump says US and Iran in talks, even if Tehran denies it","Trump says US and Iran in talks, even if Tehran denies it The US president said the sides are ""talking of a solution to a problem"" that Tehran have caused WASHINGTON, August 3. /TASS/. US President Donald Trump said that the United States and Iran are holding negotiations, even if Tehran does not publicly acknowledge it. ""They ask for a meeting, some would say 'beg', talks begin, with more scheduled in the immediate future, and they say, openly and proudly, that they’re not having any discussions, that nothing is being talked about, and they’re only dealing with Oman,"" he wrote on Truth Social. ""Whether Iran wants to admit it or not, we are, in fact, talking of a solution to a problem that they have caused, for decades. It is very simple, IRAN WILL NEVER HAVE A NUCLEAR WEAPON!""","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 19:19:33 +0300",https://tass.com/world/2168545,2026-08-04 01:20:39
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Russian synchronized swimmers win their first gold at European Aquatics Championships,Russian synchronized swimmers win their first gold at European Aquatics Championships,"Russian synchronized swimmers win their first gold at European Aquatics Championships This is the seventh medal at this tournament for Russian athletes PARIS, August 3. /TASS/. Russian synchronized swimmers have won gold medals in Team Free at the 2026 European Aquatics Championships in France. The Russian synchronized swimmers scored 285.0346 point. Spain is second (282.3541) and Italy is third (256.1558). The Russian team includes Kira Cherezova, Maiia Doroshko, Ekaterina Kossova, Elizaveta Minaeva, Svetlana Pavlova, Elena Shabanova, Elizaveta Smirnova, and Olga Tiutiunik. This is the seventh medal at this tournament for Russian athletes. Earlier, Russians won three silver and three bronze medals. Russians are competing in the neutral status. Russia is competing at the European Championships for the first time since 2021.","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 19:14:59 +0300",https://tass.com/sports/2168541,2026-08-04 01:20:40
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Four Zaporozhye nuclear plant workers injured by Ukrainian mine blast — ZNPP,Four Zaporozhye nuclear plant workers injured by Ukrainian mine blast — ZNPP,"Four Zaporozhye nuclear plant workers injured by Ukrainian mine blast — ZNPP According to the statement, any civilian could become a victim of remote mining MELITOPOL, August 3. /TASS/. Four employees of the Zaporozhye nuclear power plant have been injured by an explosion of a Ukrainian mine planted in Energodar using a drone, the ZNPP said on Max messenger. ""Tonight, the Ukrainian Armed Forces used drones to remotely mine roads in the industrial zone and at the entrance to Energodar. As a result of an explosion on one of the mined sections, four employees of the Zaporozhye nuclear power plant, including representatives from the fire safety department, security department, and transport department, were injured on their way to work,"" it said. The nuclear power plant noted that any civilian could become a victim of remote mining. ""The use of drones to mine roads means that ordinary routes used daily by the NPP employees, emergency services, and city residents are turned into a deadly danger zone. Any civilian car, motorcycle, or bicycle could become a victim of such an attack. Such actions are directed not against military facilities, but against civilians and vital infrastructure,"" it said.","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 19:08:26 +0300",https://tass.com/emergencies/2168539,2026-08-04 01:20:40
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Talks with Ukraine on production of Patriot systems progressing — US envoy to NATO,Talks with Ukraine on production of Patriot systems progressing — US envoy to NATO,"Talks with Ukraine on production of Patriot systems progressing — US envoy to NATO Matthew Whitaker believes the process is moving forward NEW YORK, August 3. /TASS/. The United States is making progress in negotiations with Ukraine on joint production of Patriot systems, US Permanent Representative to NATO Matthew Whitaker said in an interview with Fox Business. ""Nothing to announce this morning, but I think it [the progress] is consistent with the meetings we had in Ankara with Zelensky, my follow-up meetings two weeks ago in Kiev, where we talked to the Ukrainians about some of these co-production opportunities, and my meetings also with the companies that have these technologies and can prop up manufacturing. So I think we're moving forward,"" Whitaker said, answering a question about US President Donald Trump's statement regarding joint Patriot production. US President Donald Trump said on July 31 that the United States should be very careful with granting licenses to other countries to manufacture its weapons. He said that Washington had not agreed to supply Kiev with either Patriot system technology or Tomahawk cruise missiles, and questioned this possibility.","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 18:05:28 +0300",https://tass.com/world/2168537,2026-08-04 01:20:41
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Ukrainian army trying to hush up internal conflict over Drapaty appointment — official,Ukrainian army trying to hush up internal conflict over Drapaty appointment — official,"Ukrainian army trying to hush up internal conflict over Drapaty appointment — official Vladimir Vasilenko previously said that Drapaty’s appointment as the Ukrainian army commander-in-chief exacerbated disagreements among service members in Ukraine’s southern group of forces GENICHESK, August 3. /TASS/. The Ukrainian military command is trying to conceal an internal conflict within the ranks of Ukraine’s southern group of forces following the appointment of Mikhail Drapaty as the commander-in-chief, said Vladimir Vasilenko, the press secretary of the Kherson Region’s governor. ""The Ukrainian military command is trying to conceal the internal conflict and is preventing the dissemination of information about what is happening. However, hushing up the problems only fuels discontent,"" he told reporters. Vasilenko previously said that Drapaty’s appointment as the Ukrainian army commander-in-chief exacerbated disagreements among service members in Ukraine’s southern group of forces and provoked a negative reaction among personnel. On July 22, Vladimir Zelensky appointed Drapaty as the Ukrainian army’s commander-in-chief. Later, in a video interview that was widely circulated in the media, Drapaty called the people of Russia ""a nation that has no right to exist."" He called the people of Donbass ""a contingent unwilling to work, who don’t care what country they live in."" He also stated that residents of the Donetsk People’s Republic (DPR) and Lugansk People’s Republic (LPR) need to be re-educated in the spirit of Ukrainian nationalism.","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 18:04:15 +0300",https://tass.com/politics/2168535,2026-08-04 01:20:42
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Twenty-one people hospitalized after being injured in Ukrainian UAV attack on Gelendzhik,Twenty-one people hospitalized after being injured in Ukrainian UAV attack on Gelendzhik,"Twenty-one people hospitalized after being injured in Ukrainian UAV attack on Gelendzhik The Health Ministry added that 19 people received outpatient medical care MOSKOV, August 3. /TASS/. Twenty-one people injured as a result of Ukraine's drone attack on Gelendzhik have been hospitalized, including three children, Alexey Kuznetsov, assistant to the Russian Health Minister, told journalists. ""According to operational data, 21 people injured in the drone attack by Ukrainian neo-Nazis in Gelendzhik have been hospitalized, including three children,"" he said. The assistant minister added that 19 people received outpatient medical care. Telemedicine consultations with specialists from federal medical centers are being conducted.","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 18:02:14 +0300",https://tass.com/emergencies/2168531,2026-08-04 01:20:43
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Hamas urges mediators to push Israel to agree to ceasefire in Gaza,Hamas urges mediators to push Israel to agree to ceasefire in Gaza,"Hamas urges mediators to push Israel to agree to ceasefire in Gaza According to the source, the movement insists on ""direct intervention"" by mediators to compel Israel to fully halt the fighting DOHA, August 3. /TASS/. The Palestinian movement Hamas has called on mediators to put direct pressure on Israel to achieve a complete ceasefire in the Gaza Strip, a source in the movement's leadership toldAl Jazeera. ""The movement contacted the mediators and demanded a clear position regarding the latest escalation by the occupation forces in Gaza,"" a Hamas representative said. According to him, the movement insists on ""direct intervention"" by mediators to compel Israel to fully halt the fighting. The source also stressed that the continuation of Israeli strikes threatens current agreements. ""We made it clear to the mediators that the continued attacks will disrupt the implementation of the agreement and the negotiations over its timeline,"" he added. In January 2025, Israel and Hamas reached a ceasefire agreement in the Gaza Strip with the mediation of the United States, Egypt, and Qatar. The initiative consisted of three stages: the first included a halt to hostilities, the release of detained persons, an expansion of humanitarian aid deliveries to the enclave, and a partial withdrawal of Israeli forces. The subsequent phases envisaged ending the conflict, withdrawing Israeli forces, and rebuilding the Gaza Strip. On July 30, US President Donald Trump said an agreement had been reached providing for the complete disarmament of Hamas formations. On August 1 and 2, the Israel Defense Forces reported strikes on positions of Hamas armed formations. Al Jazeera, citing sources in ","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 17:58:07 +0300",https://tass.com/world/2168529,2026-08-04 01:20:44
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Russia's antimonopoly watchdog opens antitrust case against Apple,Russia's antimonopoly watchdog opens antitrust case against Apple,"Russia's antimonopoly watchdog opens antitrust case against Apple The watchdog stated that Apple had failed to comply with an earlier warning regarding the pre-installation of a national messenger and a Russian application store on iOS devices MOSCOW, August 3. /TASS/. Russia's Federal Antimonopoly Service (FAS) has opened an antitrust case against Apple Inc., the regulator told reporters on Monday. ""In accordance with the law on protection of competition and prior enforcement practice against Apple, which has been upheld by judicial authorities, the service has opened a case against the company,"" the FAS said. The watchdog stated that Apple had failed to comply with an earlier warning regarding the pre-installation of a national messenger and a Russian application store on iOS devices, including iPhones and iPads.","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 17:45:23 +0300",https://tass.com/economy/2168523,2026-08-04 01:20:45
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Drapaty’s appointment exacerbates disagreements in Ukrainian army — official,Drapaty’s appointment exacerbates disagreements in Ukrainian army — official,"Drapaty’s appointment exacerbates disagreements in Ukrainian army — official Vladimi Vasilenko added that Mikhail Drapaty earned a reputation among the fighters as a ""meat general"" GENICHESK, August 3. /TASS/. The appointment of Mikhail Drapaty as the Ukrainian army’s commander-in-chief has exacerbated disagreements among the Ukrainian southern group of forces’ service members and provoked a negative reaction among the personnel, Vladimir Vasilenko, the press secretary of the Kherson Region’s governor, said. ""The change of the commander-in-chief of the Ukrainian armed forces has not resolved, but rather significantly exacerbated disagreements between service members of various units of the Ukrainian southern group of forces. Mikhail Drapaty’s appointment caused a very negative reaction among the personnel who remember well his command methods in the Kherson sector: harsh pressure on subordinates, disregard for human losses, and a desire to achieve goals at any cost,"" he told reporters. Vasilenko added that Drapaty earned a reputation among the fighters as a ""meat general."" On July 22, Vladimir Zelensky appointed Drapaty as the Ukrainian army’s commander-in-chief. Later, in a video interview that was widely circulated in the media, Drapaty called the people of Russia ""a nation that has no right to exist."" He called the people of Donbass ""a contingent unwilling to work, who don’t care what country they live in."" He also stated that residents of the Donetsk People’s Republic (DPR) and Lugansk People’s Republic (LPR) need to be re-educated in the spirit of Ukrainian nationalism.","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 17:41:57 +0300",https://tass.com/politics/2168521,2026-08-04 01:20:45
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Transport Ministry works on alternative logistics due to attacks on vessels in Sea of Azov,Transport Ministry works on alternative logistics due to attacks on vessels in Sea of Azov,"Transport Ministry works on alternative logistics due to attacks on vessels in Sea of Azov The ministry noted that the headquarters aims to protect the transport industry and economic interests MOSCOW, August 3. /TASS/. The Russian Transport Ministry has established a headquarters to develop alternative logistics routes and redirect cargo flows to other modes of transport, the ministry reported. ""Due to the tense situation in the Sea of Azov following enemy drone attacks on maritime vessels, the Russian Transport Ministry is taking all necessary measures to ensure cargo logistics in the Azov-Black Sea basin. A special headquarters has been organized to coordinate transportation,"" the statement said. The ministry noted that the headquarters aims to protect the transport industry and economic interests. Furthermore, several stevedoring companies stand ready to handle additional cargo volumes and accelerate shipping rates at terminals, depending on their technological capabilities. ""In cooperation with the Defense Ministry, additional measures are being implemented to ensure safety of navigation and protect maritime vessels in the Azov-Black Sea basin,"" the Transport Ministry added.","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 17:41:00 +0300",https://tass.com/economy/2168517,2026-08-04 01:20:46
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Russia takes control of nearly 600 sq km of land in special military op zone in July,Russia takes control of nearly 600 sq km of land in special military op zone in July,"Russia takes control of nearly 600 sq km of land in special military op zone in July Expert Andrey Marochko said that 32 settlements came under control of Russian forces over the month LUGANSK, August 3. /TASS/. Russian fighters took control of almost 600 square kilometers of territory in the special operation zone in July, 200 square kilometers more than in June, said military expert Andrey Marochko. ""According to the monitoring resources, the Russian Armed Forces took control of about 570 square kilometers of territory, which is 200 square kilometers more than in June,"" he said during a live broadcast on his VKontakte page. Marochko said that 32 settlements came under control of Russian forces over the month. Most of them were in the Kharkov Region, where the Russian military liberated 12 settlements. Second-most was in the Donetsk People’s Republic, where 11 settlements came under control of Russian troops. The military expert highlighted that Battlegroup North liberated the most settlements — 11. In July, the North fighters achieved the best results in liberating territories in the special military operation zone, Marochko said.","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 17:30:07 +0300",https://tass.com/defense/2168515,2026-08-04 01:20:47
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Pentagon concludes agreements worth $3 billion to increase interceptor production volumes,Pentagon concludes agreements worth $3 billion to increase interceptor production volumes,"Pentagon concludes agreements worth $3 billion to increase interceptor production volumes The department emphasized that this will in the future help triple production volumes of PAC-3 missiles for Patriot and quadruple those for THAAD systems WASHINGTON, August 3. /TASS/. The Pentagon has concluded agreements worth over $3 billion with Lockheed Martin and Northrop Grumman aimed at expanding production capacities for munitions for Patriot and THAAD air defense systems, according to statements from the US military department and Northrop Grumman. The Pentagon noted that the ""two framework agreements"" are aimed at expanding ""production capacity of critical missile-interceptor components."" The department emphasized that this will in the future help triple production volumes of PAC-3 missiles for Patriot and quadruple those for THAAD systems. Northrop Grumman clarified that two multi-year framework agreements worth over $3 billion were signed. Of this amount, $2 billion will be directed toward the production of engines and other systems for PAC-3, and $1 billion toward increasing production volumes of THAAD components over seven years. At the end of July, the Pentagon reported that it had increased the value of a seven-year contract with Lockheed Martin for the production and supply of Patriot munitions to $58.6 billion.","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 17:19:54 +0300",https://tass.com/world/2168513,2026-08-04 01:20:48
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,Trump says US to hold off attacks on Iran,Trump says US to hold off attacks on Iran,"Trump says US to hold off attacks on Iran US President Donald Trump said on Saturday that he has agreed to hold off fresh attacks against Iran. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied US President Donald Trump says he has agreed to hold off fresh attacks against Iran, according to a post on his Truth Social account. /@realDonaldTrump US President Donald Trump said on Saturday that he has agreed to hold off fresh attacks against Iran. In a post on Truth Social, Trump said the United States ""is locked and loaded and ready to go against the Islamic Republic of Iran, at levels of Military Terror, Strength, and Power not seen since World War II."" ""Despite this, we have just been asked by Iran, and other Middle Eastern Countries, to hold off any attack in that the perimeters of a deal has been agreed to,"" he said. ""This would include the Immediate, Complete, and Total OPENING OF THE HORMUZ STRAIT, and an end to Iran's nuclear threat,"" he added. Trump also warned that his decision is ""subject to being able to rapidly make a DEAL."" At a Cabinet meeting on Friday at the Camp David retreat, Trump said he believed US negotiators, including his son-in-law Jared Kushner, special envoy Steve Witkoff and Secretary of State Marco Rubio, could still reach a deal with Iran. But Trump also said he was losing faith in the Iranians, saying, ""They break their word so often"" – a claim Tehran has frequently leveled at Washington – and said he would be ""hitting them."" U","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 02:06:53 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-08-02/news-1Ph3KHhmY8w/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-04 01:20:49
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,Challenges persist despite Hamas backing Gaza ceasefire roadmap,Challenges persist despite Hamas backing Gaza ceasefire roadmap,"Challenges persist despite Hamas backing Gaza ceasefire roadmap Hamas has approved the latest draft of a roadmap aimed at completing the implementation of the second phase of the Gaza ceasefire agreement, marking a potential breakthrough in negotiations after more than two and a half years of conflict in the enclave. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied Palestinians sit outside their tent at a camp for displaced people in Nuseirat, central Gaza Strip, on July 31, 2026. /VCG Hamas has approved the latest draft of a roadmap aimed at completing the implementation of the second phase of the Gaza ceasefire agreement, marking a potential breakthrough in negotiations after more than two and a half years of conflict in the enclave. However, major disputes between Hamas and Israel remain unresolved, particularly over the sequence of key steps, including disarmament, Israel's military withdrawal and Gaza's post-war governance. While Hamas says the transfer of weapons can only take place after Israeli forces withdraw from Gaza, Israel insists that the enclave must be fully demilitarized before any withdrawal. Analysts caution that Hamas' acceptance of the roadmap does not necessarily indicate a fundamental political shift, but rather reflects its attempt to adapt to the realities of the prolonged conflict. They said the agreement's success will ultimately depend on whether all parties can fulfill their commitments during the implementation process. Hamas, Israel make contradictory claims In a statement on Friday, Hamas said it agreed to include discussions on the transfer of heavy weapons within the framework of the Gaza cea","Sat, 01 Aug 2026 02:27:45 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-08-01/Challenges-persist-despite-Hamas-backing-Gaza-ceasefire-roadmap-1PfmDv8ZTUs/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-04 01:20:49
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,Japan officially launches new intelligence body. Why is it dangerous?,Japan officially launches new intelligence body. Why is it dangerous?,"Japan officially launches new intelligence body. Why is it dangerous? Japan has taken further steps to strengthen its security apparatus and military capabilities, with the government establishing a new national intelligence agency and conducting its first test launch of a long-range cruise missile, moves that have sparked concerns over the country's accelerating military buildup. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi talks about setting up the National Intelligence Bureau at her office in Chiyoda Ward, Tokyo, Japan, May 27, 2026. /VCG Japan has taken further steps to strengthen its security apparatus and military capabilities, with the government establishing a new national intelligence agency and conducting its first test launch of a long-range cruise missile, moves that have sparked concerns over the country's accelerating military buildup. On Friday, the Japanese government officially established the National Intelligence Bureau aimed at enhancing the country's intelligence-gathering capabilities. Hara Kazuya was appointed as the head of the new intelligence agency. Meanwhile, according to Japan's Ministry of Defense, the country's Self-Defense Forces conducted a test launch of the US-made Tomahawk cruise missile in the Pacific Ocean on July 28, marking Japan's first such test. The Tomahawk is a subsonic long-range cruise missile typically launched from naval vessels and submarines. Designed mainly for naval deployment, it also has land-based variants, with a maximum range exceeding 2,000 kilometers. Experts said Japan's recent moves, including strengthening its intelligence capabilities and accelerating the development and deployment o","Fri, 31 Jul 2026 05:25:39 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-07-31/Japan-officially-launches-new-intelligence-body-Why-is-it-dangerous--1PdPlb5zuOk/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-04 01:20:49
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,US launches fresh strikes against Iran as war engulfs more countries,US launches fresh strikes against Iran as war engulfs more countries,"US launches fresh strikes against Iran as war engulfs more countries The United States launched new strikes against Iran and Iran-backed groups on Wednesday, as Washington and Tehran continued a cycle of military escalation that has heightened fears of a broader regional conflict. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied US President Donald Trump speaks in the Oval Office of the White House in Washington, DC, July 29, 2026. /VCG The United States launched new strikes against Iran and Iran-backed groups on Wednesday, as Washington and Tehran continued a cycle of military escalation that has heightened fears of a broader regional conflict. US Central Command (CENTCOM) said on social media that US forces had carried out strikes against Iran, calling the operation ""a powerful response"" to Tuesday's firing by Iran on US bases in Jordan and at ships in the Strait of Hormuz. The strikes came after US President Donald Trump threatened to hit Iran ""hard"" in retaliation for Tehran's latest actions. According to Iran's Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps (IRGC), Iran had earlier targeted a US air base in Jordan with ballistic missiles and halted three ""violating"" oil tankers in the Strait of Hormuz. The US and Jordan said the missiles were intercepted. Following the Iranian attacks, CENTCOM said US and Saudi forces had conducted strikes in Iraq against what they described as ""Iran-aligned"" targets. Iraq's paramilitary Popular Mobilization Forces (PMF) said on Wednesday that multiple PMF headquarters across several provinces, including Baghdad, Basra and Nineveh, were hit in the US-Saudi strikes","Thu, 30 Jul 2026 04:06:43 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-07-30/US-launches-fresh-strikes-against-Iran-as-war-engulfs-more-countries-1Pc683we5nG/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-04 01:20:49
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,China responds to reports of a Chinese missing in Pakistan's avalanche,China responds to reports of a Chinese missing in Pakistan's avalanche,"China responds to reports of a Chinese missing in Pakistan's avalanche China is acting swiftly to verify the relevant information regarding recent reports that several mountain climbers, including a Chinese national, went missing in an avalanche in Pakistan, a Chinese Foreign Ministry spokesperson said in Beijing on Friday. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied Chinese Foreign Ministry spokesperson Mao Ning answers questions at a regular press briefing in Beijing, China, July 31, 2026. /CMG China is acting swiftly to verify the relevant information regarding recent reports that several mountain climbers, including a Chinese national, went missing in an avalanche in Pakistan, a Chinese Foreign Ministry spokesperson said in Beijing on Friday. Spokesperson Mao Ning made the remarks at a daily press briefing, adding that China stands ready to assist its nationals if needed and would like to provide assistance in accordance with Pakistan's needs.","Fri, 31 Jul 2026 10:45:10 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-07-31/China-responds-to-reports-of-a-Chinese-missing-in-Pakistan-s-avalanche-1PedB6OHHaw/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-04 01:20:50
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,Ceuta crossing death toll climbs,Ceuta crossing death toll climbs,"Ceuta crossing death toll climbs The Spanish government has reinforced security in Ceuta by deploying additional National Police officers, Civil Guard personnel and military units, while emergency reception facilities remain under heavy pressure. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied Migrants try to cross from Morocco into the Spanish enclave of Ceuta, Friday, July 31, 2026. /CFP At least 34 people have died while attempting to reach Spain's North African enclave of Ceuta by sea, as nearly 50,000 migrants crossed into the territory from neighboring Morocco over the past two days. Spanish Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez described the incident as ""a violation of Spain's territorial integrity."" According to Spanish authorities, most of the victims drowned while attempting to swim around the El Tarajal border breakwater separating Morocco and Ceuta. Sanchez visited Ceuta on Friday with Interior Minister Fernando Grande-Marlaska to assess the situation. During the visit, he announced new border security measures, including the installation of floating barriers near the El Tarajal breakwater to prevent further sea crossings. He also pledged to accelerate the identification and return of irregular migrants, thanked Morocco for its cooperation in border management and repatriation, and vowed to intensify efforts against human trafficking networks. The Spanish government has reinforced security in Ceuta by deploying additional National Police officers, Civil Guard personnel and military units, while emergency reception facilities remain under heavy pressur","Fri, 31 Jul 2026 16:01:15 GMT",https://newsaf.cgtn.com/news/2026-08-01/Ceuta-crossing-death-toll-climbs-1PeB8TCEW3u/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-04 01:20:50
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,African leaders reaffirm support for Somalia mission,African leaders reaffirm support for Somalia mission,"African leaders reaffirm support for Somalia mission The leaders agreed that Africa must play a bigger role in financing and sustaining the African Union Support and Stabilization Mission in Somalia to ensure it remains operational. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied African leaders meeting in Uganda's capital, Kampala, discussed the future of the African Union Support and Stabilization Mission in Somalia (AUSSOM) as concerns grow over how to finance the operation that has supported Somalia's fight against the militant group Al-Shabaab for nearly two decades. Leaders said preserving the gains made against Al-Shabaab will require stronger political commitment and more reliable funding as Somalia gradually takes greater responsibility for its own security. The discussions come as the United States (US) is hesitant to commit additional funding, while European partners are facing growing financial pressure. The leaders agreed Africa must play a bigger role in financing and sustaining the mission to ensure it remains operational. Ugandan President Yoweri Museveni said Somalia would not be abandoned, despite potential funding withdrawals by external partners, insisting that the country has the capacity to manage its own security challenges. Uganda has contributed troops to peacekeeping operations in Somalia since 2007 and remains one of the mission's largest troop-contributing countries. The summit reaffirmed support for Somalia's security transition while calling for predictable and sustainable backing from international partners. A","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 18:43:25 GMT",https://newsaf.cgtn.com/news/2026-08-03/African-leaders-reaffirm-support-for-Somalia-mission-1PhLIx0pMf6/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-04 01:20:50
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,"EU in talks with OpenAI, Anthropic after AI models go rogue","EU in talks with OpenAI, Anthropic after AI models go rogue","EU in talks with OpenAI, Anthropic after AI models go rogue EU in talks with OpenAI, Anthropic after AI models go rogue Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied /VCG The European Commission is in talks with OpenAI and Anthropic after their AI models went rogue, Commission officials said on Friday, ‌as they touted landmark EU rules requiring strict monitoring of high-risk systems. Europe's AI Act, which kicks in on August 2, is the first legislation in the world to regulate a technology ​used in almost all sectors of business and society. The ​rules require certain AI systems to tell users when they are ⁠interacting with AI and when content has been generated or altered by it. Violations can result in heavy fines, ranging from €7.5 million ($8.2 million) or 1.5% of turnover to €35 million or 7% of global ​turnover. Anthropic ​said on Thursday some of its Claude AI models had hacked into the systems ​of three companies during cybersecurity tests, days after rival OpenAI revealed that one of its AI agents went on a rogue attack. Both companies have briefed the Commission on the incidents, the ​officials told reporters. ""We have been informed by the two providers of incidents bilaterally ​before they become public. We are in contact with them. They will also report to ‌us ⁠more information as we speak. We will see also if we need to follow up more formally on those things,"" one of the officials said. Another official talked up","Fri, 31 Jul 2026 14:06:55 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-07-31/EU-in-talks-with-OpenAI-Anthropic-after-AI-models-go-rogue-1PeupOpdm36/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-04 01:20:50
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,Japan's new intelligence agency launch fuels neo-militarism,Japan's new intelligence agency launch fuels neo-militarism,"Japan's new intelligence agency launch fuels neo-militarism Japan on Friday officially launched its National Intelligence Bureau, aimed at enhancing the country's intelligence-gathering capabilities, marking a complete recasting of the decentralized intelligence landscape that Japan had maintained for over 80 years since the end of World War II. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied Japan's House of Councillors approves a bill to establish a new National Intelligence Council during a plenary session in Tokyo on May 27, 2026. /VCG Editor's note: The author is Cai Liang, director and research fellow at the Center for Northeast Asian Studies, Shanghai Institutes for International Studies. Japan on Friday officially launched its National Intelligence Bureau, aimed at enhancing the country's intelligence-gathering capabilities, marking a complete recasting of the decentralized intelligence landscape that Japan had maintained for over 80 years since the end of World War II. Japaneseprime minister now holds supreme authority over intelligence coordination, and the intelligence capabilities of multiple government departments have been fully consolidated. This deep reform of the intelligence system is by no means an ordinary administrative ""optimization""; it is a bureaucratic engine that is accelerating Japan's neo-militarism. Japan's security framework will become increasingly centralized and militarized, significantly elevating regional security risks. Looking back at history, Japanese intelligence agencies inflicted immense suffering and committed horrific atrocities across Asia and beyond, leaving memories that remain vivid and chilling to this day","Fri, 31 Jul 2026 12:37:14 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-07-31/Japan-s-new-intelligence-agency-launch-fuels-neo-militarism-1PeoacbcTBu/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-04 01:20:50
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,"Thousands rally in Kyiv, renew calls for defense minister's return","Thousands rally in Kyiv, renew calls for defense minister's return","Thousands rally in Kyiv, renew calls for defense minister's return Thousands rally in Kyiv, renew calls for defense minister's return Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied Several thousand Ukrainians rallied through central Kyiv on Friday, signaling to President Volodymyr Zelenskyy that opposition to his decision to oust Defense Minister Mykhailo Fedorov, widely credited with driving military innovation during Ukraine's conflict with Russia, remains strong. Fedorov, who only took charge of the ministry in January, was dismissed in a surprise and poorly explained government reshuffle in mid-July. Since then, Ukrainians have been gathering next to the presidential office, calling for Fedorov to be reinstated after he refused to accept another government post. ""I don't like it when decisions are made, and then no one can explain why they were made,"" Oleksandr, a 40-year-old IT worker, said. Zelenskyy initially said he removed Fedorov because of a major conflict with then commander-in-chief Oleksandr Syrskyi, whom he dismissed a week later under public pressure triggered by the crisis. But speculation grew that Fedorov was forced out because of his efforts to tackle alleged corruption in the defense sector. Fedorov appeared to lend weight to those claims in a recent interview, though he provided no details. On Friday, aiming to draw the president's attention, protesters marched through Kyiv's historic center until the crowd poured into K","Sat, 01 Aug 2026 02:39:10 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-08-01/Thousands-rally-in-Kyiv-renew-calls-for-defense-minister-s-return-1Pfih8xbLSU/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-04 01:20:51
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,"Five dead, 41 missing after ferry catches fire in Indonesia's Java Sea","Five dead, 41 missing after ferry catches fire in Indonesia's Java Sea","Five dead, 41 missing after ferry catches fire in Indonesia's Java Sea Five people were killed and 41 others remain missing after the Mutiara Sentosa 2 caught fire in the Java Sea north of Madura Island in Indonesia's East Java province, the National Search and Rescue Agency said Sunday. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied The passenger ship Mutiara Sentosa 2 on fire in the Java Sea north of Madura Island, East Java, Indonesia, August 2, 2026. /VCG Five people were killed and 41 others remain missing after the Mutiara Sentosa 2 caught fire in the Java Sea north of Madura Island in Indonesia's East Java province, the National Search and Rescue Agency said Sunday. A total of 225 people had been evacuated, the agency said. The vessel, operating on the Surabaya-Makassar route, was carrying 271 people, including 232 passengers and 39 crew members. Authorities said the vessel was about 19 nautical miles (35.2 km) offshore when it was almost completely engulfed in flames, with passengers gathering on the bridge and at the bow as they waited to be evacuated. Several nearby vessels took part in the rescue operation, while a joint search and rescue team deployed additional vessels and personnel to evacuate survivors and search for the missing. The search operation remains underway, and the cause of the fire is under investigation.","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 09:15:07 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-08-02/news-1Phym4rVrkk/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-04 01:20:51
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,"One killed, three injured in Kyiv attack, mayor says","One killed, three injured in Kyiv attack, mayor says","One killed, three injured in Kyiv attack, mayor says One killed, three injured in Kyiv attack, mayor says Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied One person was killed and three others were injured after Russia launched a ballistic missile attack on Ukraine's capital, Kyiv, on Saturday, Mayor Vitali Klitschko said.","Fri, 31 Jul 2026 23:31:09 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-08-01/news-1PfdIHVNvDG/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-04 01:20:51
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,"1 killed, 5 injured in Portland neighborhood shooting: Authorities","1 killed, 5 injured in Portland neighborhood shooting: Authorities","1 killed, 5 injured in Portland neighborhood shooting: Authorities One person was killed and five others injured in a neighborhood shooting in Portland, in the US state of Oregon, on Sunday morning, the local government said in a press release. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied A neighborhood shooting leaves one person dead and five others injured in Portland, Oregon, US, August 2, 2026. /CMG One person was killed and five others injured in a neighborhood shooting in Portland, in the US state of Oregon, on Sunday morning, the local government said in a press release. At 3:33 a.m., Portland police officers assigned to North Precinct responded to a report of a shooting in the 5800 block of Northeast Alberta Street, the release said. When they arrived, they found two victims with apparent gunshot wounds. Both were taken to the hospital by ambulance. A short time later, officers learned that four additional victims had arrived at local hospitals in private vehicles, it added. An adult male later died at the hospital, while the other five injured were treated and their injuries are not believed to be life-threatening, the release said, adding that a teenager is among the injured. The suspect or suspects fled the scene after the shooting, and no immediate arrests have been made. Portland Police Homicide Unit detectives are asking anyone with information about the case who has not spoken to police to submit a tip online.","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 23:05:31 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-08-03/news-1PivHdGiNLG/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-04 01:20:51
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,China helps Burkina Faso youth build farming skills,China helps Burkina Faso youth build farming skills,"China helps Burkina Faso youth build farming skills China is supporting agricultural skills training in Burkina Faso, where young farmers are learning practical vegetable cultivation techniques aimed at improving food security and creating sustainable livelihood opportunities. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied China is supporting agricultural skills training in Burkina Faso, where young farmers are learning practical vegetable cultivation techniques aimed at improving food security and creating sustainable livelihood opportunities. The program, led by Chinese agricultural experts in the town of Kindi, in west-central Burkina Faso, forms part of broader China-Africa cooperation in agriculture, education and community development. The training combines classroom instruction with hands-on agricultural practice. Participants are learning vegetable production techniques, including tomato cultivation, and are expected to demonstrate the skills they have acquired during the course. For many trainees, the program offers an opportunity to improve traditional farming practices through modern agricultural methods. Practical skills by Chinese agriculture experts during youth training in Burkina Faso. /CGTN Africa ""This training is very useful to us. We usually cultivate small gardens, but this training adds new knowledge. China has a highly developed agricultural sector, and we should seize this opportunity to learn,"" said trainee Ouedraogo Safiata. Another participant, Sankara Yacouba, said the program had changed how trainees approach farming. ""The focus on horticulture and the tr","Fri, 31 Jul 2026 14:59:52 GMT",https://newsaf.cgtn.com/news/2026-07-31/China-helps-Burkina-Faso-youth-build-farming-skills-1Pesaom8OLS/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-04 01:20:52
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,US-Iran hostilities spread across multiple fronts as tensions escalate,US-Iran hostilities spread across multiple fronts as tensions escalate,"US-Iran hostilities spread across multiple fronts as tensions escalate The military confrontation between the United States and Iran continues to intensify, with both sides launching retaliatory strikes and the conflict showing signs of expanding across multiple fronts in the Middle East. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied A general view of damaged structures at a site of US-Saudi joint strikes in Bartalla in the northern Iraqi Nineveh province, July 29, 2026. /VCG The military confrontation between the United States and Iran continues to intensify, with both sides launching retaliatory strikes and the conflict showing signs of expanding across multiple fronts in the Middle East. According to a statement released by the US Central Command, US forces struck dozens of targets linked to Iran's Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps (IRGC) in the early hours of Thursday local time. The targets included military command centers, missile and drone facilities, coastal surveillance and defense positions, as well as sites associated with maritime combat capabilities. On the same day, explosions were reported in several parts of southern Iran, including Hormozgan, Bushehr and Khuzestan provinces. In one incident, a US strike reportedly hit a residential area on Qeshm Island in Hormozgan Province, killing a family of three, according to local reports. In response to the US attacks, the IRGC said it launched several ballistic missiles at a US military base in Jordan, claiming that the strike destroyed three US F-35 fighter jets and severely damaged three others. The IRGC also said that several milita","Fri, 31 Jul 2026 05:14:35 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-07-31/US-Iran-hostilities-spread-across-multiple-fronts-as-tensions-escalate-1PdSDDmRTva/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-04 01:20:52
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,"OPEC+ continues to raise oil production by 188,000 bpd in September","OPEC+ continues to raise oil production by 188,000 bpd in September","OPEC+ continues to raise oil production by 188,000 bpd in September Seven OPEC+ countries agreed on Sunday to raise the oil production cap in September by 188,000 barrels per day (bpd) from August levels, according to a statement published after a virtual meeting of OPEC+. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied The logo of the OPEC is seen at its headquarters in Vienna. /VCG Seven OPEC+ countries agreed on Sunday to raise the oil production cap in September by 188,000 barrels per day (bpd) from August levels, according to a statement published after a virtual meeting of OPEC+. The decision was announced following the meeting attended by Saudi Arabia, Russia, Iraq, Kuwait, Kazakhstan, Algeria and Oman, which reviewed global market conditions and outlook. OPEC+ countries consist of members of the Organization of the Petroleum Exporting Countries (OPEC) and its allies. In their collective commitment to supporting oil market stability, the seven participating countries decided to implement a production increase from the voluntary cuts announced in April 2023, the statement said. The voluntary production cuts of 1.65 million bpd were first announced in April 2023 and later extended through the end of 2026. The decision made on Sunday marks the sixth consecutive month for the OPEC+ to ramp up its production. According to the statement, the seven countries will flexibly adjust their production in line with evolving market conditions. They are set to meet on September 6 to decide on production levels for October.","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 11:26:29 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-08-02/news-1PhHK4Vfe5W/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-04 01:20:52
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,China cotton association rejects US forced labour claims,China cotton association rejects US forced labour claims,"China cotton association rejects US forced labour claims A Chinese industry association has voiced strong opposition to the United States' decision to add 43 Chinese companies, including cotton textile firms, to the so-called ""Uyghur Forced Labor Prevention Act Entity List,"" saying the move seriously violates the basic rules of international trade. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied File photo of a cotton-harvesting machine operating in a field in Awat county, northwest China's Xinjiang Uygur Autonomous Region. /VCG A Chinese industry association has voiced strong opposition to the United States' decision to add 43 Chinese companies, including cotton textile firms, to the so-called ""Uyghur Forced Labor Prevention Act Entity List,"" saying the move seriously violates the basic rules of international trade. The China Cotton Association (CCA) said in a statement released on Saturday that the US allegations of ""forced labor"" lack factual and legal basis, noting that China's cotton industry has consistently followed a market-oriented and modern development path. In Xinjiang, a major cotton-producing region in China, more than 90% of cotton harvesting is now carried out by machines, with highly automated and large-scale operations covering the entire industrial chain from planting and harvesting to processing and textile production, the association said. The labor rights and interests of cotton farmers and industry workers are strictly protected by Chinese laws, and their employment choices are completely voluntary. ""There is no so-called 'forced labor,'"" the statement said. The US move disregards facts and imposes a ""presumption of guilt"" on Chinese","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 14:47:40 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-08-02/China-cotton-association-rejects-US-forced-labour-claims-1PhQJ83qcxO/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-04 01:20:52
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,Seed bank boosts Zimbabwe's food security,Seed bank boosts Zimbabwe's food security,"Seed bank boosts Zimbabwe's food security The seed bank has 285 members and stores traditional small-grain seeds that farmers can access during droughts and other difficult growing seasons. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied The Mutiusinazita Seed Bank, a community-run initiative in eastern Zimbabwe, is helping smallholder farmers preserve traditional crop varieties and improve resilience to climate change. The seed bank has 285 members and stores traditional small-grain seeds that farmers can access during droughts and other difficult growing seasons. The initiative is rooted in indigenous farming practices in which families selected and preserved their best seeds for future harvests. ""If we store the seed at our homesteads, they are susceptible to pests and degradation due to the elements. But the way they are stored in the bank protects them from damage,"" said Nyadzi Mupungi, secretary of the Mutiusinazita Seed Bank. The project also creates additional income opportunities by allowing farmers to sell seeds directly to other growers. Seed containers are labelled with the producer's name and contact details, while the community has established a nursery for indigenous tree species to restore biodiversity and generate another source of revenue. Traditional grains are becoming increasingly important as climate change brings hotter temperatures and more frequent dry spells. ""They have a better chance of surviving even during dry spells; they also have a better chance of surviving in the ","Fri, 31 Jul 2026 16:17:12 GMT",https://newsaf.cgtn.com/news/2026-08-01/Seed-bank-boosts-Zimbabwe-s-food-security-1PeCiTnI5tS/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-04 01:20:52
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,African Union calls for El Nino preparedness across Africa,African Union calls for El Nino preparedness across Africa,"African Union calls for El Nino preparedness across Africa The AU convened a ministerial meeting to assess member states' preparedness and strengthen early warning systems. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied The African Union (AU) has called on member states to strengthen preparedness measures as forecasts point to a strong El Nino expected to intensify from August, raising the risk of extreme weather across parts of the continent. The World Meteorological Organization has warned the climate pattern is expected to strengthen from August. The warning comes as parts of Southern Europe and North Africa experience extreme heat, with temperatures in Tunisia exceeding 49 degrees Celsius in some areas and several countries battling wildfires this summer. Speaking in New York on Friday, UN Secretary-General Antonio Guterres warned that the phenomenon could worsen the impacts of climate change. Africa is still recovering from the devastating 2023-2024 El Nino, which brought severe droughts and floods, destroyed crops and livestock, and pushed millions into hunger. Experts warn the new El Nino could be among the strongest on record. ""This El Nino year is very strong; it's the strongest in the last 30 years. We expect the consequences to be very, very strong,"" said Ousmane Ndiaye, Director General of the African Center of Meteorological Application for Development. Ndiaye said climate models show East Africa is likely to receive more rain than usual between August and November, w","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 12:15:24 GMT",https://newsaf.cgtn.com/news/2026-08-02/African-Union-calls-for-El-Nino-preparedness-across-Africa-1PhDZzvmsZG/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-04 01:20:53
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,Mexico businesses squeezed by tariff uncertainty,Mexico businesses squeezed by tariff uncertainty,"Mexico businesses squeezed by tariff uncertainty Mexico businesses squeezed by tariff uncertainty Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. Alasdair Baverstock Copied Mexican businesses are facing higher costs and supply chain disruptions as trade negotiations with the United States continue. Small manufacturers and wholesalers say tariffs on imports from non-free trade agreement countries have driven up prices for textiles and other goods, while changing regulations have added uncertainty.Although the U.S. has extended the deadline for a broader trade agreement with Mexico by 90 days, analysts say businesses remain concerned about future trade policies and continued pressure on Mexico to tighten restrictions on imports. CGTN’s Alasdair Baverstock reports from Mexico City. For more, check out our exclusive content onCGTN Nowand subscribe to our weekly newsletter,The China Report.","Fri, 31 Jul 2026 22:46:33 GMT",https://newsus.cgtn.com/news/2026-08-01/Mexico-businesses-squeezed-by-tariff-uncertainty-1PfajVSEqti/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-04 01:20:53
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,Japan's intelligence bureau: Security reform or remilitarization?,Japan's intelligence bureau: Security reform or remilitarization?,"Japan's intelligence bureau: Security reform or remilitarization? Japan's intelligence bureau: Security reform or remilitarization? Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. Copied Japan has launched its National Intelligence Bureau, creating the country's first centralized intelligence command since WWII. The government says it is essential to address today's increasingly complex security challenges. Critics see a different story. They warn the bureau could centralize intelligence power under the prime minister, weaken democratic oversight, and revive concerns rooted in Japan's wartime past. CGTN reporter Cao Bing examines the history, the controversy, and the implications behind Japan's biggest intelligence reform since World War II.","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 07:04:08 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-08-02/Japan-s-intelligence-bureau-Security-reform-or-remilitarization--1Ph6JwUd5wk/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-04 01:20:53
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,Poll: 76% in Japan support upholding non-nuclear principles,Poll: 76% in Japan support upholding non-nuclear principles,"Poll: 76% in Japan support upholding non-nuclear principles A total of 76% of people in Japan support upholding the country's Three Non-Nuclear Principles of not possessing, not producing and not permitting the introduction of nuclear weapons into its territory, Kyodo News reported on Sunday, citing a nationwide opinion poll. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied People offer flowers and prayers for atomic bomb victims at Bakushinchi-koen, Atomic Bomb Hypocenter Park, in Nagasaki, Japan, August 9, 2023. /VCG A total of 76% of people in Japan support upholding the country's Three Non-Nuclear Principles of not possessing, not producing and not permitting the introduction of nuclear weapons into its territory, Kyodo News reported on Sunday, citing a nationwide opinion poll. The survey also found that 77% believe Japan should not pursue nuclear sharing, an arrangement under which the US would station nuclear weapons in Japan for joint operation. As the only country to have suffered atomic bombings in war, Japan continues to show strong anti-nuclear sentiment, with the survey results highlighting opposition to nuclear weapons as debate grows over revising the principles. Asked about the government's April decision to lift its decades-old ban on exporting lethal weapons, 36% said exports should be limited to nonlethal equipment, even to allies, while 53% said the ban should be maintained or the policy reconsidered, according to the survey conducted by the Japan Association for Public Opinion Research. The survey, which targeted 3,000 people aged 18 and over, was conducted in June and July by the nationwide polling organization fo","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 06:38:10 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-08-02/Poll-76-in-Japan-support-upholding-non-nuclear-principles-1PhlMTmwoaQ/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-04 01:20:53
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,Israel yet to make official response to Hamas disarmament proposal,Israel yet to make official response to Hamas disarmament proposal,"Israel yet to make official response to Hamas disarmament proposal No official response from Israel has been released about the complete disarmament deal announced by the US on Thursday. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied Palestinians inspect the debris following an Israeli airstrike the day before in Gaza City, July 30, 2026. /VCG No official response from Israel has been released about the complete disarmament deal announced by the US on Thursday. Earlier in the day, US President Donald Trump announced on his Truth Social account that an agreement was reached on the complete disarmament of Hamas and other armed groups in Gaza. According to Trump, Hamas has agreed to disarm in Gaza, while Israel remains silent. Despite the lack of official response, reports byThe Times of Israel, a prominent Israeli media, said that an Israeli official has expressed reservations about the agreement, saying that the 15-point proposal ""does not adequately address"" Israel's demands for the ""complete demilitarization, [which is] a precondition for any process."" ""There will be no IDF withdrawal from the Yellow Line in the Gaza Strip before Hamas is disarmed and the Strip is fully demilitarized,"" the Israeli official added. A US official told the BBC that Trump would be ""very disappointed"" if Israel decides not to withdraw from Gaza.","Fri, 31 Jul 2026 08:33:07 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-07-31/Israel-yet-to-make-official-response-to-Hamas-disarmament-proposal-1Pe74SJIxzi/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-04 01:20:54
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,China rejects Reuters report on alleged arms sales to Iran,China rejects Reuters report on alleged arms sales to Iran,"China rejects Reuters report on alleged arms sales to Iran The Chinese Foreign Ministry on Thursday denied a Reuters report alleging that Beijing sold weapons to Iran. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied The Chinese Foreign Ministry on Thursday denied a Reuters report alleging that China sold weapons to Iran. ""China has made its position clear on relevant issues on multiple occasions. The report is not true and has no factual ground at all,"" a spokesperson for the ministry said. ""China always works for peace and the end of the conflict."" CGTN's Fact Hunter, a global verification platform, searched online mentions of the story, discovering thousands of reposts on social media platforms, including X, YouTube and Bluesky. However, retracing the relevant posts in reverse chronological order shows that the entire narrative online was based on a Reuters report, which was the only source of this information. All the later reports of the story cited Reuters directly and provided no further evidence to corroborate the claim. No further verification on the claim was made by the subsequent reposts either. The original Reuters report itself, which was published on Wednesday as an ""exclusive"" story, relied entirely on unnamed sources and provided no details about their identity, background or credibility. No other news agency has independently obtained similar information. Reuters has not yet responded to CGTN's request for comment, and no further updates have been published by","Fri, 31 Jul 2026 14:58:30 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-07-31/China-rejects-Reuters-report-on-alleged-arms-sales-to-Iran-1PenT6X1Q08/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-04 01:20:54
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,"Hungary to develop 4 GW of wind power capacity by 2030, PM Magyar says","Hungary to develop 4 GW of wind power capacity by 2030, PM Magyar says","Hungary to develop 4 GW of wind power capacity by 2030, PM Magyar says Hungary to develop 4 GW of wind power capacity by 2030, PM Magyar says Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied Hungary will develop 4 gigawatts (GW) of wind energy capacity by 2030 as part of efforts to diversify the country's energy sources, Prime Minister Peter Magyar said on Friday.","Fri, 31 Jul 2026 14:47:54 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-07-31/news-1PeCkm2yX8k/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-04 01:20:54
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,"Trump threatens to hit Iran 'very hard,' Israel expected to join","Trump threatens to hit Iran 'very hard,' Israel expected to join","Trump threatens to hit Iran 'very hard,' Israel expected to join Trump threatens to hit Iran 'very hard,' Israel expected to join Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied President Donald Trump departs following a cabinet meeting at Camp David, near Thurmont, Maryland, US, July 31, 2026. /VCG US President Donald Trump threatened on Friday to hit Iran ""very hard,"" as US media reported he was considering renewed heavy attacks as soon as this weekend, including against energy infrastructure targets, with Israel expected to join the campaign. After more than five months of war, which began on February 28 when the United States and Israel launched strikes on Iran, there appears to be no end to the conflict, with tit-for-tat attacks resuming. ""We'll be hitting him very hard and, you know, at some point they're going to say, 'We just can't take it anymore,'"" Trump said on Friday as he hosted a cabinet meeting at the Camp David presidential retreat in Maryland. The Wall Street Journal later reported that Trump had ordered a fresh attack aimed at convincing Tehran to surrender, which could begin as soon as this weekend, citing unnamed US officials. CBS News, meanwhile, reported that the United States and Israel were planning joint strikes on energy-related targets, possibly throughout the weekend. Such targets would likely include oil refineries and power plants. Trump has repeatedly threatened to strike Iran's vital infrastructure throughou","Sat, 01 Aug 2026 01:01:53 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-08-01/Trump-threatens-to-hit-Iran-very-hard-Israel-expected-to-join-1PfgUWRcQ6c/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-04 01:20:54
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,China rejects Philippines' delimitation of Huangyan Dao 'baselines',China rejects Philippines' delimitation of Huangyan Dao 'baselines',"China rejects Philippines' delimitation of Huangyan Dao 'baselines' The Chinese Foreign Ministry on Friday issued a statement on the Philippines' delimitation of the ""baselines of the territorial sea"" of China's territory of Huangyan Dao. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied A view of the territorial waters off China's Huangyan Dao and surrounding areas, Sansha, south China's Hainan Province, June 30, 2025. /VCG The Chinese Foreign Ministry on Friday issued a statement on the Philippines' delimitation of the so-called ""baselines of the territorial sea"" of China's territory of Huangyan Dao. The move ""is a grave infringement upon China's territorial sovereignty and a serious violation of international law, including the United Nations Charter and the United Nations Convention on the Law of the Sea (UNCLOS),"" said the statement. ""It is illegal, null and void. China firmly rejects and will never accept it."" ""Huangyan Dao is China's inherent territory. China has indisputable sovereignty over it and its adjacent waters and has sovereign rights and jurisdiction over the relevant waters. China has continuously, peacefully and effectively exercised sovereignty and jurisdiction over Huangyan Dao,"" said the statement. The statement pointed out that the territory of the Philippines has been defined by a series of international treaties, and Huangyan Dao has never been a part of it. ""The Philippines' illegal territorial claim over China's Huangyan Dao is completely baseless under international law."" According to the statement, the Philippines' unil","Fri, 31 Jul 2026 12:35:09 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-07-31/China-rejects-Philippines-delimitation-of-Huangyan-Dao-baselines--1PeoMp03kZy/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-04 01:20:55
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,"Severe heat grips western US, raising health and wildfire risks","Severe heat grips western US, raising health and wildfire risks","Severe heat grips western US, raising health and wildfire risks Severe heat grips western US, raising health and wildfire risks Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied Guests cool off in a wave pool to escape a heat dome affecting much of the western United States, Las Vegas, Nevada, US, July 31, 2026. /VCG Blistering heat blanketed the western United States on Saturday, with temperatures hovering near record highs, increasing the risks of heat-related illness and wildfire. The US National Weather Service (NWS) has issued extreme heat warnings for parts of California, Arizona, Nevada and Utah, with temperatures in some southwestern deserts forecast to reach 49 degrees Celsius. According to weekend forecasts, temperatures in Sacramento, California's capital, could exceed 39.4 degrees Celsius. Palm Springs in inland California is expected to reach 47.2 degrees Celsius, while Death Valley, a desert valley in eastern California known for its extreme heat, could soar to 50.6 degrees Celsius. Salt Lake City, Utah, is forecast to reach 40.6 degrees Celsius, while Las Vegas, Nevada, could hit 46.1 degrees Celsius. In Arizona, the capital Phoenix is expected to reach 43 to 47 degrees Celsius through Monday, with highs of 44 to 49 degrees Celsius forecast for Yuma, a city near the Mexican border. The NWS warned that the dangerous heat is expected to persist across much of the West over the coming days. Daniel Swain, a climate scientist at ","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 10:26:42 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-08-02/Severe-heat-grips-western-US-raising-health-and-wildfire-risks-1Pht5hKZRAs/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-04 01:20:55
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,The Road to Victory: Into the deep blue,The Road to Victory: Into the deep blue,"The Road to Victory: Into the deep blue When they venture into the ocean, they leave behind their roles as fathers, husbands and sons. They are united by a single identity: soldiers. From the skies above to the depths below, officers and soldiers of the Chinese People's Liberation Army (PLA) Navy stand together to safeguard the country's territory. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied When they venture into the ocean, they leave behind their roles as fathers, husbands and sons. They are united by a single identity: soldiers. From the skies above to the depths below, officers and soldiers of the Chinese People's Liberation Army (PLA) Navy stand together to safeguard the country's territory. In the latest episode of CMG's special production The Road to Victory, marking the 99th anniversary of the PLA's founding, we follow the PLA Navy's journey into the deepest blue. We explore the mission, sense of duty and traditions shared by service members as they carry forward the aspirations of those who came before them.","Sat, 01 Aug 2026 01:41:06 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-08-01/The-Road-to-Victory-Into-the-deep-blue-1OX9xmW62Ag/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-04 01:20:55
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,"Record-breaking El Nino may be forming, strongest in 150 years","Record-breaking El Nino may be forming, strongest in 150 years","Record-breaking El Nino may be forming, strongest in 150 years The ongoing El Nino event in the Pacific Ocean is continuing to strengthen and could become the most powerful in the past 150 years, according to the China Meteorological Administration (CMA). Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied Drought-damaged corn plants on a farm in Tacuba, El Salvador, on Friday, July 24, 2026. /VCG The ongoing El Nino event in the Pacific Ocean is continuing to strengthen and could become the most powerful in the past 150 years, according to the China Meteorological Administration (CMA). Observations from the CMA's national climate center show that the central and eastern equatorial Pacific reached the threshold for El Nino conditions in May, and sea surface temperatures in the region continued to rise in June. Since July, it has been under monitoring as a potential strong El Nino event, and the probability of it developing into a super El Nino is increasing. Forecasts indicate that the event is likely to persist until at least next spring, with the overall duration close to the historical average for El Nino events – around 10 to 11 months. A global climate amplifier A firefighter moves beehives away from flames while battling a wildfire in San Martin de Valdeiglesias, west of Madrid, Spain, July 26, 2026. /VCG El Nino is regarded as a global climate ""amplifier"" that changes the probability of extreme weather events, including heatwaves, droughts and heavy rainfall. Through interactions between the ocean and atmosphere, a strong El Nino can alter global atmospheric c","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 03:14:56 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-08-02/Record-breaking-El-Nino-may-be-forming-strongest-in-150-years-1Ph4DMWhV6g/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-04 01:20:55
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,How the Flying Tigers represents a lasting China-US bond,How the Flying Tigers represents a lasting China-US bond,"How the Flying Tigers represents a lasting China-US bond They flew one of the world's most dangerous air routes to keep China's wartime lifeline alive, forging a friendship that lasts to this day. Eighty-five years later, the Flying Tigers' legacy continues to inspire new generations in China and the US. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. Yang Yiran Copied Over 2,900 Japanese aircraft destroyed. Forty-four naval vessels sunk. More than 66,000 enemy troops neutralized. These figures capture the toll of a wartime partnership when the American Volunteer Group fought alongside the Chinese during the toughest time of World War II. The first American Volunteer Group, nicknamed ""the Flying Tigers,"" was made up of a group of military pilots and ground crew recruited from the US, who joined the Chinese in the defense against the Japanese fascist aggressors from August 1941 to July 1942. This year marks the 85th anniversary of their arrival in China. A World War II leather flight jacket sits on display next to a photograph of airmen beside a B-17 bomber at an exhibition at the Kunming Museum in Kunming, Yunnan Province, China, August 3, 2025. /VCG Their mission at the time was dangerous but vital: to protect China's last lifeline after Japan cut the country off from ocean shipping and sealed off port access. The fragile back-door route over the eastern Himalayan mountains from India to China, known as ""the Hump,"" became the last passage through which China received supplies of arms, food and medication, and delivered strategic materials to sustain the wartime economy in the southwest. ""The Hump"" was hazardous at best and","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 04:41:53 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-08-02/How-the-Flying-Tigers-represents-a-lasting-China-US-bond-1Ph2L9rrNIs/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-04 01:20:55
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,"Iran says all threats 'noteworthy,' denies deal on reopening Hormuz","Iran says all threats 'noteworthy,' denies deal on reopening Hormuz","Iran says all threats 'noteworthy,' denies deal on reopening Hormuz Iran's Acting Defense Minister Seyed Majid Ebn Al-Reza said Sunday that Tehran perceives every ""enemy"" threat as ""real and noteworthy,"" rejecting any characterization of them as mere psychological warfare. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied Children wade in the water with cargo ships at anchor in the background and a fisherman nearby, in the Strait of Hormuz off Bandar Abbas, Iran, June 30, 2026. /VCG Iran's Acting Defense Minister Seyed Majid Ebn Al-Reza said Sunday that Tehran perceives every ""enemy"" threat as ""real and noteworthy,"" rejecting any characterization of them as mere psychological warfare. ""We will neither be surprised nor remain passive. We use threats as a basis to increase our preparedness, strengthen our deterrence, and develop our power,"" Al-Reza wrote on social media platform X after US President Donald Trump said earlier that he had agreed to hold off fresh attacks against Iran. In his post on Truth Social, Trump said the United States was ""locked and loaded and ready to go against the Islamic Republic of Iran, at levels of Military Terror, Strength, and Power not seen since World War II,"" but held off after being ""asked by Iran, and other Middle Eastern Countries,"" citing a forthcoming deal that would include the ""Immediate, Complete, and Total OPENING OF THE HORMUZ STRAIT, and an end to Iran's nuclear threat."" Earlier US media reports had suggested US and Israeli strikes on Iranian energy infrastructure could begin over the weekend. Israel's Channel 12 news reported Sunday that ","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 09:18:24 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-08-02/news-1PhyAAaXoqc/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-04 01:20:56
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,2 killed after firefighting helicopters collide over Greek wildfire,2 killed after firefighting helicopters collide over Greek wildfire,"2 killed after firefighting helicopters collide over Greek wildfire 2 killed after firefighting helicopters collide over Greek wildfire Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied Two crew members were killed and two others survived after two firefighting helicopters collided mid-air while battling a major wildfire in western Attica on Sunday, Greek authorities said. Fire Service spokesperson Vassilis Vathrakogiannis confirmed the deaths of a Danish pilot and a Greek firefighting coordinator at a press briefing. The survivors were identified as a British pilot and a Greek firefighting coordinator, one of whom was injured.","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 14:37:04 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-08-02/news-1PhVmsR7ViE/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-04 01:20:56
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,FIFA scraps World Cup stake sale plans after backlash,FIFA scraps World Cup stake sale plans after backlash,"FIFA scraps World Cup stake sale plans after backlash FIFA scraps World Cup stake sale plans after backlash Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied The world football governing body, FIFA, on Friday said it had scrapped plans to sell a stake in the World Cup to private investors after widespread backlash. ""Having listened carefully to all the views, it has become clear that the project has created divisions of a nature that, regardless of the level of support, are no longer in the interest of the objective set out in the first place,"" FIFA President Gianni Infantino said on Friday in a statement. The proposal, referred to as the FIFA Forward Enterprise project, will not proceed, Infantino said.","Fri, 31 Jul 2026 23:33:09 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-08-01/news-1PfdRB38Wt2/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-04 01:20:56
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,"China urges US to revoke FCC curbs on power inverters, advanced robots","China urges US to revoke FCC curbs on power inverters, advanced robots","China urges US to revoke FCC curbs on power inverters, advanced robots China firmly opposes the US decision to place foreign-made power inverters and advanced robotic devices on the Federal Communications Commission's (FCC) ""Covered List,"" the Ministry of Commerce said on Thursday. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied China firmly opposes the US decision to place foreign-made power inverters and advanced robotic devices on the Federal Communications Commission's (FCC) ""Covered List,"" the Ministry of Commerce said on Thursday. The FCC announced on Tuesday that new models of foreign-made power inverters and advanced robotic devices included on the ""Covered List"" will no longer be eligible for FCC authorization, effectively barring them from entering the US market. A spokesperson from the Commerce Ministry said the measures are discriminatory toward Chinese companies and products despite being presented as ""non-discriminatory."" China urged the US to immediately revoke the measures and stop its erroneous actions. If the US proceeds with the measures, China will take firm countermeasures to safeguard its interests, the spokesperson said. The FCC has ignored China's repeated representations and continued to intensify its restrictive measures, which seriously harms China's legitimate trade interests, undermines the stability of China-US economic and trade ties, and disrupts global industrial and supply chains, the spokesperson added. By generalizing the concept of national security, the US has interfered with normal commercial transactions and trade, continued to pursue ""decoupling and","Thu, 30 Jul 2026 04:03:42 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-07-30/China-urges-US-to-revoke-FCC-curbs-on-advanced-robots-power-inverters-1Pc8ntRKy76/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-04 01:20:56
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,"France's devastating fires now 'under control,' says PM","France's devastating fires now 'under control,' says PM","France's devastating fires now 'under control,' says PM The fires that have ravaged France are ""today under control,"" Prime Minister Sebastien Lecornu said on Saturday, more than a week after the country's largest wildfire since 1949. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied A partially burnt forest following a wildfire in Montfort-sur-Argens, southeastern France, August 1, 2026. /VCG The fires that have ravaged France are ""today under control,"" Prime Minister Sebastien Lecornu said Saturday, more than a week after the country's largest wildfire since 1949 flared up. ""Overall, the fires are now under control in our country,"" he said in an interview with the La Tribune Dimanche weekly. The largest wildfire erupted more than a week ago in a pine forest near the southwestern city of Bordeaux. ""We have returned to a more stable situation,"" Lecornu said, confirming earlier comments by Interior Minister Laurent Nunez. France has for weeks been battling wildfires after a series of deadly heatwaves that have dried up riverbeds and vegetation, extreme weather events scientists have linked to human-made climate change. In the Gironde region near the winemaking capital of Bordeaux, an inferno ripped through 42,000 hectares of pine forest along the Atlantic coastline – an area larger than the US city of Detroit. It also destroyed around 240 homes. Some local people think a brushwood-clearing machine accidentally started the blaze with a spark on July 29. Sophie Brocas, the prefect of the southwestern Gironde region, remained cautious on Saturday. ","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 04:54:16 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-08-02/France-s-devastating-fires-now-under-control-says-PM-1Ph8QARmRhK/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-04 01:20:57
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,"China's He Lifeng holds video call with Scott Bessent, Jamieson Greer","China's He Lifeng holds video call with Scott Bessent, Jamieson Greer","China's He Lifeng holds video call with Scott Bessent, Jamieson Greer Chinese Vice Premier He Lifeng, also China's lead person for China-US economic and trade affairs, held a video call on Thursday with US Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent and US Trade Representative Jamieson Greer. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied Chinese Vice Premier He Lifeng, also China's lead person for China-US economic and trade affairs, held a video call on Thursday with US Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent and US Trade Representative Jamieson Greer. The two sides held candid, in-depth and constructive exchanges on implementing the important consensus reached between the two heads of state at their meeting in Beijing, and on maintaining stable economic and trade relations, expanding practical cooperation, and properly addressing each other's concerns in the next stage. The Chinese side expressed serious concern over the recent economic and trade restrictions imposed by the United States on China. Both sides agreed that under the strategic guidance of the two heads of state, they would further leverage the role of the China-US economic and trade consultation mechanism to enhance communication, build mutual trust and dispel doubts, expand cooperation, promote the stable and positive development of China-US economic and trade relations, and contribute to building a constructive China-US relationship of strategic stability.","Thu, 30 Jul 2026 15:01:06 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-07-30/Chinese-vice-premier-holds-video-call-with-US-treasury-secretary-trade-representative-1PcYmN9CDVm/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-04 01:20:57
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,Events of APEC 'China Year' achieve early results: spokesperson,Events of APEC 'China Year' achieve early results: spokesperson,"Events of APEC 'China Year' achieve early results: spokesperson Since the launch of the APEC ""China Year,"" China has held three senior officials' meetings, five ministerial meetings and over 180 meetings and activities under various mechanisms and in various fields, achieving a number of early harvests, Chinese Foreign Ministry spokesperson Mao Ning said on Friday. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied Promotional slogans for the APEC ""China Year"" are seen in Shenzhen, south China's Guangdong Province, April 13, 2026. /VCG Since the launch of the APEC ""China Year,"" China has held three senior officials' meetings, five ministerial meetings and over 180 meetings and activities under various mechanisms and in various fields, achieving a number of early results, Chinese Foreign Ministry spokesperson Mao Ning said on Friday. Mao made the remarks during a news briefing in response to a related query. Mao said events of the 2026 APEC Digital Week were held in Chengdu, southwest China's Sichuan Province, from July 16 to 29. ""Participating parties reached a number of important common understandings on empowering growth through digital technology and AI development and application. They had discussions for the first time on boosting growth through digital technology, which enriched APEC digital cooperation."" Participating representatives also had field tours to experience the unique charm of Chengdu as a city of innovation and creation in Western China, said Mao. Participating parties reached broad-based consensus on advancing the global goals related to forestry and issued a joint statement at the APEC Ministerial Meeting on Forestry held in Shenzhen, Mao noted. ""Going fo","Fri, 31 Jul 2026 12:58:05 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-07-31/Events-of-APEC-China-Year-achieve-early-results-spokesperson-1PeqgUOb7uo/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-04 01:20:57
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,"EU aims for 7 AI gigafactories worth 10bn euros racing US, China","EU aims for 7 AI gigafactories worth 10bn euros racing US, China","EU aims for 7 AI gigafactories worth 10bn euros racing US, China EU aims for 7 AI gigafactories worth 10bn euros racing US, China Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied Server cabinets are seen in a data center of the AI factory ""Industrial AI Cloud"" of Deutsche Telekom and NVIDIA during the official opening, Munich, Germany, February 4, 2026. /VCG The European Union (EU) will fund seven artificial intelligence gigafactories across the bloc ​with 10 billion euros ($11.5 billion), the European Commission said ‌on Thursday, as the EU steps up efforts to close the technology gap with the US and China. The Commission said ​it aims to attract at least €20 billion in ​private investments for the projects. The total ⁠was increased from five planned gigafactories to seven following ​strong interest from EU countries. The facilities will combine advanced ​AI processors, software, cloud technology, high-speed connectivity and data centers. They will come on top of the existing 19 AI ​factories in various EU countries. ""Access to the raw ​scale of computing power within AI Gigafactories is a strategic necessity ‌for ⁠Europe as AI development accelerates,"" EU tech chief Henna Virkkunen said in a statement. Consortia or special purpose vehicles made up of technology providers, cloud service providers, ​public entities and ​investors can ⁠apply to take part in the gigafactories. The tender process will close on November ​12. The Commission expe","Fri, 31 Jul 2026 08:26:24 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-07-31/EU-aims-for-7-AI-gigafactories-worth-10bn-euros-racing-US-China-1Pe9ueWy5uo/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-04 01:20:57
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,UNAIDS report warns HIV infections could rise as global aid declines,UNAIDS report warns HIV infections could rise as global aid declines,"UNAIDS report warns HIV infections could rise as global aid declines UNAIDS has warned that cuts to international HIV prevention funding could trigger a resurgence of the epidemic, putting decades of progress at risk. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied A red ribbon is the international symbol of the fight against HIV/AIDS and solidarity with people living with HIV. /CFP UNAIDS has warned that cuts to international HIV prevention funding could trigger a resurgence of the epidemic, putting decades of progress at risk. In its report released during the 26th International AIDS Conference, taking place in Rio de Janeiro, Brazil, from July 26–31, 2026, the agency said global development assistance for HIV programs fell by 23% in 2025, the sharpest decline on record. The funding shortfall contributed to an estimated 1.2 million new HIV infections and 570,000 AIDS-related deaths, as the world fell short of key global targets. Although new HIV infections and AIDS-related deaths are at their lowest levels in more than three decades, UNAIDS noted that these gains remain fragile and could easily be reversed without sustained investment and commitment. The report also highlighted significant progress in the global fight against HIV. Kenya, Lesotho, Benin, Eswatini, Rwanda, and Zimbabwe have recorded an almost 80% reduction in new infections since 2010, demonstrating that sustained efforts can deliver meaningful results. The report shows that further progress is still possible, with new prevention tools offering renewed hope i","Fri, 31 Jul 2026 18:11:38 GMT",https://newsaf.cgtn.com/news/2026-08-01/UNAIDS-report-warns-HIV-infections-could-rise-as-global-aid-declines-1PeK5jo7m48/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-04 01:20:57
The Hindu,South Asia,en,"New talks 'last chance' for Iran to forge deal, avoid escalation of U.S. strikes: Trump","New talks 'last chance' for Iran to forge deal, avoid escalation of U.S. strikes: Trump","New talks 'last chance' for Iran to forge deal, avoid escalation of U.S. strikes: Trump Mr. Trump, speaking at the Oval Office, said he expects negotiations that will reopen the Strait of Hormuz and create a pathway for Iran to address the United States' concerns about its nuclear programme will begin in the next day or two You are logged in Loading... You don’t have any Active Subscription. Subscribed with another email? Logout and Login with that one. Your active subscription(s) Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription Products you've access to Additional Subscription Benefits Account Settings Need help with your subscription? Published- August 04, 2026 02:03 am IST - Washington U.S. President Donald Trump. | Photo Credit: Reuters Newly planned talks with Tehran are the “last chance” for Iran to forge a deal and avoid an escalation of US strikes on the country, President Donald Trump said on Monday (August 3, 2026). Mr. Trump, speaking at the Oval Office, said he expects negotiations that will reopen the Strait of Hormuz and create a pathway for Iran to address the United States' concerns about its nuclear programme will begin in the next day or two. “The first phase is the opening of the straits. The second phase will be the denuclearisation,"" the Republican President said. “And that will take a little while.” While Trump has revelled in the US military decimating layers of Tehran's leadership and devastating its air force and navy, Iran is betting it can outlast Trump as he faces diminished stockpiles of munitions and the difficulty of executing a war that is unpopular with the American electorate ahead of November's midterm election. Mr. Trump said he decided to hold off on ordering American forces to carry out ne","Tue, 04 Aug 2026 02:03:35 +0530",https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/new-talks-last-chance-for-iran-to-forge-deal-avoid-escalation-of-us-strikes-trump/article71302832.ece,2026-08-04 01:20:58
