The Hindu,South Asia,en,2 firefighting helicopters collide midair near Athens as Europe's wildfire emergency rages,2 firefighting helicopters collide midair near Athens as Europe's wildfire emergency rages,"2 firefighting helicopters collide midair near Athens as Europe's wildfire emergency rages The collision underscored the continuing danger at the most volatile front of Europe's wildfire emergency. You are logged in Loading... You don’t have any Active Subscription. Subscribed with another email? Logout and Login with that one. Your active subscription(s) Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription Products you've access to Additional Subscription Benefits Account Settings Need help with your subscription? Published- August 02, 2026 10:42 pm IST - Megara (Greece) Firefighters operate during a wildfire near Porto Germeno, northwest of Athens, Greece, Sunday, Aug. 2, 2026. | Photo Credit: AP Two firefighting helicopters collided on Sunday (August 2, 2026) while battling a wind-driven wildfire in the Porto Germeno area, west of Athens. Footage showed one of the aircraft crashing to the ground. Each helicopter was carrying a two-person crew, the Greek fire department said. A search-and-rescue operation was underway. Authorities did not immediately provide information on the crews' condition. The collision underscored the continuing danger at the most volatile front of Europe's wildfire emergency. The continent's crisis split into three stark fronts: strong winds drove flames deeper into the Athens region and forced fresh evacuations, France guarded a still-burning scar four times the size of Paris, and Spain's major fires stopped advancing. The most immediate danger was in Greece. Flames spread through western Attica, the region around Athens, threatening communities and an industrial district outsid","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 22:42:02 +0530",https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/2-firefighting-helicopters-collide-midair-near-athens-as-europes-wildfire-emergency-rages/article71298781.ece,2026-08-04 01:21:06
The Hindu,South Asia,en,"Sheikh Hasina to hold presser on August 5, a month before Tarique Rahman’s expected visit","Sheikh Hasina to hold presser on August 5, a month before Tarique Rahman’s expected visit","Sheikh Hasina to hold presser on August 5, a month before Tarique Rahman’s expected visit Bangladesh’s deposed leader will address the media virtually on the second anniversary of her arrival in India post-2024 uprising You are logged in Loading... You don’t have any Active Subscription. Subscribed with another email? Logout and Login with that one. Your active subscription(s) Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription Products you've access to Additional Subscription Benefits Account Settings Need help with your subscription? Updated- August 02, 2026 10:36 pm IST - New Delhi Bangladesh’s deposed Prime Minister Sheikh Hasina will address the international media virtually to announce her homecoming and outline her vision for Bangladesh. File. | Photo Credit: AFP A month before theexpected visit of Bangladesh Prime Minister Tarique Rahmanfor the India-chaired BRICS summit, the country’s deposed Prime MinisterSheikh Hasinawill address a press conference at the Foreign Correspondents Club in New Delhi on Wednesday (August 5, 2026), the second anniversary of her arrival in India following themonsoon uprising of 2024 in Dhaka. The media interaction will be addressed by Ms. Hasina’s son Sajeeb Wazed Joy and the former Education Minister of Bangladesh, Mohibul Hasan Chowdhury Nowfel. “In this exclusive engagement, Sheikh Hasina will address the international media virtually to announce her homecoming and outline her vision for Bangladesh. The session will also feature senior leaders of the Bangladesh Awami League and former Ministers, participating both in person and virtually, followed by an interactive Q&A,” said Waiel Aww","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 22:36:39 +0530",https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/sheikh-hasina-to-hold-presser-on-august-5-a-month-before-tarique-rahmans-expected-visit/article71298490.ece,2026-08-04 01:21:06
The Hindu,South Asia,en,At least 72 died in Spain’s Ceuta migrant rush,At least 72 died in Spain’s Ceuta migrant rush,"At least 72 died in Spain’s Ceuta migrant rush The largest migrant rush into the enclave has caused an international crisis for Spain, with European partners criticising Madrid for its immigration policies. You are logged in Loading... You don’t have any Active Subscription. Subscribed with another email? Logout and Login with that one. Your active subscription(s) Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription Products you've access to Additional Subscription Benefits Account Settings Need help with your subscription? Published- August 02, 2026 10:17 pm IST - Ceuta, Spain Santiago Abascal, leader of the far-right Vox party, second left, visits the Spanish-Moroccan border in the Spanish enclave of Ceuta, Sunday, August 2, 2026. | Photo Credit: AP At least 72 people died during the mass influx in recent days of migrants into Spain’s Ceuta enclave, when tens of thousands of people mostly swam around the border post from Morocco, local officials said on Sunday (August 2, 2026). Most of the estimated 60,000 people who rushed into Spain’s north African territory have returned to Morocco since the territory’s largest mass migrant crossing. “The latest figure that we have is 72,” the government’s delegate to Ceuta, Miguel Angel Perez Triano, told reporters when asked about the number of fatalities. The previous toll was 67 deaths. Spanish police and troops patrolled the streets of Ceuta on Sunday (August 2, 2026) as the enclave largely returned to normal after the sudden mass influx of migrants from Morocco that had occurred between Wednesday and Friday. Only small groups of migrants were still walking around after ","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 22:17:58 +0530",https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/at-least-72-died-in-spains-ceuta-migrant-rush/article71298103.ece,2026-08-04 01:21:07
The Hindu,South Asia,en,Ruling BNP authorises PM Rahman to finalise nominee for Bangladesh's presidential elections,Ruling BNP authorises PM Rahman to finalise nominee for Bangladesh's presidential elections,"Ruling BNP authorises PM Rahman to finalise nominee for Bangladesh's presidential elections According to Article 123(2) of the Constitution, an election to fill the vacant office of the President must be held within 90 days of the post becoming vacant You are logged in Loading... You don’t have any Active Subscription. Subscribed with another email? Logout and Login with that one. Your active subscription(s) Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription Products you've access to Additional Subscription Benefits Account Settings Need help with your subscription? Published- August 02, 2026 10:07 pm IST - Dhaka Prime Minister Tarique Rahman. File | Photo Credit: Reuters The ruling Bangladesh Nationalist Party (BNP) has authorised Prime Minister Tarique Rahman to select the party's candidate for the country's presidential elections, local media reported. The decision was taken on Saturday (August 1, 2026) at BNP's National Standing Committee's meeting, the Dhaka Tribune newspaper reported. The meeting was headed by PM Rahman, who is also the BNP chairman. ""The Standing Committee has entrusted the Prime Minister and BNP Chairman to take the necessary decisions regarding the presidential election and select the party's nominee,"" state-ownedBangladesh Sangbad Sangstha (BSS)quoted BNP Secretary General Mirza Fakhrul Islam Alamgir as saying. Speaker Hafiz Uddin Ahmad took charge as the acting President after Mohammed Shahabuddin resigned on July 24. According to Article 123(2) of the Constitution, an election to fill the vacant office of the President must be held within 90 days of the post becoming vacant,Dhaka Tribunereported. ""The Election Commission had al","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 22:07:25 +0530",