The Hindu,South Asia,en,Suicide attack kills 13 during protest in northern Pakistan: Police,Suicide attack kills 13 during protest in northern Pakistan: Police,"Suicide attack kills 13 during protest in northern Pakistan: Police The attack took place in Pakistan's northern border province of Khyber Pakhtunkhwa, where authorities are fighting a growing insurgency by the Tehreek-i-Taliban Pakistan (TTP). You are logged in Loading... You don’t have any Active Subscription. Subscribed with another email? Logout and Login with that one. Your active subscription(s) Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription Products you've access to Additional Subscription Benefits Account Settings Need help with your subscription? Updated- August 02, 2026 09:56 pm IST - Peshawar, Pakistan Police officers examine the site following a suicide bombing, in Kabal, a town in the Swat Valley in Pakistan's Khyber Pakhtunkhwa province, Sunday, Aug. 2, 2026. | Photo Credit: AP A suicide bomber attacked a busy area near a police station during a protest in northern Pakistan’s Swat district, killing 13 people and wounding 22, police said on Sunday (August 2, 2026). The blast took place at a crowded intersection near a police station in Swat during a civil society protest, police said. “Thirteen people, including eight police officers, were killed in the suicide bombing,” Swat Deputy Inspector General of Police Fida Hussain toldAFP. He added that 22 people had been wounded and another body, suspected to be that of the bomber, had been brought to hospital. “A suicide bomber attempted to enter the police station located at the chowk (intersection), but was stopped by police at the main gate,” he said. The attack took place in Pakistan’s northern border province of Khyber Pakhtunkhwa, where authorities are fighting a growing insurgency ","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 21:56:39 +0530",https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/suicide-attack-during-protest-in-northern-pakistan-police/article71298666.ece,2026-08-04 01:21:07
The Hindu,South Asia,en,"Ukraine hits multiple Russian regions, killing 8: Officials","Ukraine hits multiple Russian regions, killing 8: Officials","Ukraine hits multiple Russian regions, killing 8: Officials Both Moscow and Kyiv have upped attacks on each other in recent months, as U.S.-led talks aimed at ending the conflict remain largely frozen You are logged in Loading... You don’t have any Active Subscription. Subscribed with another email? Logout and Login with that one. Your active subscription(s) Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription Products you've access to Additional Subscription Benefits Account Settings Need help with your subscription? Updated- August 02, 2026 09:56 pm IST - Moscow A Nova Poshta postal warehouse is destroyed following Russian air attack on the outskirts of Kharkiv, Ukraine, Sunday, Aug. 2, 2026. | Photo Credit: AP Ukraine attacked multiple regions of Russia on Sunday (August 2, 2026), killing at least eight people, Russian officials said. Some of the strikes hit hundreds of kilometres from the front line, according to authorities. Both Moscow and Kyiv have upped attacks on each other in recent months, as U.S.-led talks aimed at ending the conflict remain largely frozen. Kyiv, which denies targeting civilians, says the strikes are fair retaliation for deadly Russian bombardment of its own territory and are aimed at pressuring Moscow into negotiations. Ukrainian shelling of Russia's Belgorod region bordering Ukraine left three dead, while a separate drone attack on the Saratov region bordering Kazakhstan killed two others, regional authorities said. Three were killed in a drone strike on a car in Russia's Udmurtia region, more than 1,000 kilometres (600 miles) from the front line, the region's acting governor O","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 21:56:24 +0530",https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/ukraine-hits-multiple-russian-regions-say-officials/article71298652.ece,2026-08-04 01:21:08
The Hindu,South Asia,en,U.K. PM Burnham signals support for written constitution,U.K. PM Burnham signals support for written constitution,"U.K. PM Burnham signals support for written constitution Unlike most countries around the world, Britain does not have a written Constitution, and is instead governed by a patchwork of statutes, common law judgments, and treaties. You are logged in Loading... You don’t have any Active Subscription. Subscribed with another email? Logout and Login with that one. Your active subscription(s) Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription Products you've access to Additional Subscription Benefits Account Settings Need help with your subscription? Updated- August 02, 2026 09:25 pm IST - London Britain's Prime Minister Andy Burnham looks on, as he meets with members of the Home Office and of the Coastguard, during a visit to HM Coastguard Maritime Rescue Coordination Centre, in Dover, Britain, August 2, 2026. | Photo Credit: Reuters Britain's new Prime Minister Andy Burnham has signalled his support for a written constitution for the U.K., which unlike most countries, does not have one authoritative document. Since entering office just two weeks ago, the former Mayor of Greater Manchester has made devolution of power to regional authorities a focus of his administration. ""In the end, I think it does start to point towards a new constitutional settlement,"" Mr. Burnham said of his devolution plans on the weekend. Calling for a ""new clear set of principles about how this country should be run"", Mr. Burnham said there was a need for a written Constitution — something he has called for before he was Prime Minister. ""It's wrong that people are left arguing for things that are just fundamental... and the lack of a constitution disempowers places","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 21:25:45 +0530",https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/uk-pm-burnham-signals-support-for-written-constitution/article71298588.ece,2026-08-04 01:21:08
The Hindu,South Asia,en,"Four killed, two injured in central China apartment building fire","Four killed, two injured in central China apartment building fire","Four killed, two injured in central China apartment building fire Firefighters rescued the six people from the high-rise residential building and sent them to the hospital for treatment. Four of them later died despite medical efforts, while the remaining two are still receiving medical treatment, says sources You are logged in Loading... You don’t have any Active Subscription. Subscribed with another email? Logout and Login with that one. Your active subscription(s) Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription Products you've access to Additional Subscription Benefits Account Settings Need help with your subscription? Published- August 02, 2026 06:55 pm IST - Beijing Four people were killed, and two others injured after a fire broke out at an apartment building in Changsha, capital of central China's Hunan Province, local firefighting authorities said on Sunday (August 2, 2026). The blaze erupted at 3:54 a.m. Saturday (August 1). Firefighters rescued the six people from the high-rise residential building and sent them to the hospital for treatment. Four of them later died despite medical efforts, while the remaining two are still receiving medical treatment, the state-runXinhuanews agencyreported. An investigation into the cause of the fire is currently underway, the news agency said. Published- August 02, 2026 06:55 pm IST fire/China/accident (general)/disaster (general) Terms & conditions|Institutional Subscriber Comments have to be in English, and in full sentences. They cannot be abusive or personal. Please abide by ourcommunity guidelinesfor posting your comments. We have migrated to a new commenting platform. If you are already a registered user of The Hindu and logged in, you may continue to engage wi","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 18:55:36 +0530",https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/fire-in-central-chinas-changsha-apartment-building-kills-few/article71297937.ece,2026-08-04 01:21:08
