Times of India,India (Mainstream),en,Quote by Ludwig Wittgenstein: 'The real question of life after death isn't whether or not it exists...',Quote by Ludwig Wittgenstein: 'The real question of life after death isn't whether or not it exists...',"Quote by Ludwig Wittgenstein: 'The real question of life after death isn't whether or not it exists...' <img align=""left"" border=""0"" hspace=""10"" src=""https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132840908.cms"" style=""margin-top: 3px; margin-right: 5px;"" />Philosopher Ludwig Wittgenstein challenged the preoccupation with life after death, suggesting that eternal existence does not address the fundamental questions of life’s meaning. His reflections emerged amidst the chaos of World War One. In contemporary discussions on digital immortality, this crucial insight often gets overshadowed; authentic meaning resides in fully embracing the present and living with intention. At TOI World Desk, our dedicated team of seasoned journalists and passionate writers tirelessly sifts through the vast tapestry of global events to bring you the latest news and diverse perspectives round the clock. With an unwavering commitment to accuracy, depth, and timeliness, we strive to keep you informed about the ever-evolving world, delivering a nuanced understanding of international affairs to our readers. Join us on a journey across continents as we unravel the stories that shape our interconnected world.Read More",2026-08-04T01:18:07+05:30,https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/quote-of-the-day-by-ludwig-wittgenstein-the-real-question-of-life-after-death-isnt-whether-or-not-it-exists-but-and-why-forever-wont-fix-us/articleshow/132840908.cms,2026-08-04 01:21:50
Times of India,India (Mainstream),en,Quote of the day by JS Mill: 'I have learned to seek my happiness by limiting my desires...',Quote of the day by JS Mill: 'I have learned to seek my happiness by limiting my desires...',"Quote of the day by JS Mill: 'I have learned to seek my happiness by limiting my desires...' <img align=""left"" border=""0"" hspace=""10"" src=""https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132840677.cms"" style=""margin-top: 3px; margin-right: 5px;"" />Victorian philosopher John Stuart Mill believed that true happiness lies in limiting our desires rather than endlessly pursuing them. After facing a mental crisis due to his upbringing, Mill shifted his philosophy, warning that unending desire leads to a hedonic treadmill. Today, our consumer-driven culture reflects this endless chase; by curbing material wishes, we can unlock a wealth of inner fulfillment and deeper contentment. At TOI World Desk, our dedicated team of seasoned journalists and passionate writers tirelessly sifts through the vast tapestry of global events to bring you the latest news and diverse perspectives round the clock. With an unwavering commitment to accuracy, depth, and timeliness, we strive to keep you informed about the ever-evolving world, delivering a nuanced understanding of international affairs to our readers. Join us on a journey across continents as we unravel the stories that shape our interconnected world.Read More",2026-08-04T01:03:45+05:30,https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/quote-of-the-day-by-js-mill-i-have-learned-to-seek-my-happiness-by-limiting-my-desires-rather-than-and-the-19th-century-cure-for-modern-burnout/articleshow/132840677.cms,2026-08-04 01:21:50
